{"symbols":[{"name":"DataContainer","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class DataContainer"],"doc":"<p>Holds the rows and tracks their edits (<code>getChanges()</code>). Every datasource has one: a new one by\ndefault, or the one given as <code>DatasourceOptions.container</code> - several datasources can share it and\nso show the same rows, each with its own filter, sort, grouping and selection. The field types for\nthe edit tracking come from the <code>fields</code> of the datasources made on it.</p>\n<p>Most of the time you do not use it directly: the datasource&#39;s methods call it and also rebuild the\ndisplayed rows and send the events. The container&#39;s own methods do neither - after changing the rows\nhere, call <code>datasource.reloadDatasource()</code> to show them.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer, Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// two datasources, e.g. two grids, on the same rows\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\nconst left = new Datasource({ container, fields: { born: 'date' } });\nconst right = new Datasource({ container, fields: { born: 'date' } });\n\nleft.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann', born: new Date(1990, 4, 17) }]);\nright.getAllData(); // the same row</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new DataContainer(UniqueKeyAttribute?: string): DataContainer"],"doc":"<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>UniqueKeyAttribute</code> the field that identifies a row, e.g. <code>&#39;id&#39;</code>. The selection follows it,\nso it survives replacing the rows with fresh ones from a server. Left out, every row gets a\ngenerated key (a negative number)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer, Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ container });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"acceptChanges","signatures":["acceptChanges(options?: { newKeys?: ReadonlyMap<string | number, string | number>; rows?: Entity | Entity[] }): void"],"doc":"<p>Call it after a successful save: the changes are now on the server, so they are no changes any\nmore. For every row (or the <code>rows</code> given):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a row marked for deletion is removed from the container, a new one too</li>\n<li>a new row becomes an ordinary row (<code>__rowState</code> <code>undefined</code>)</li>\n<li>the values a row has now become its original values: nothing counts as edited</li>\n<li>the row&#39;s error (<code>setErrors()</code>) and its validation errors are cleared</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then <code>getChanges()</code> lists none of them, <code>hasChanges()</code> is <code>false</code> when every row was accepted,\nand <code>resetData()</code> goes back to these values. The undo history is cleared, also when only some\nrows were accepted. <code>datasource.acceptChanges()</code> calls it and also rebuilds the displayed rows -\nuse that one.</p>\n<p><strong>The keys of new rows.</strong> A new row has a temporary key, a generated negative number: in its key\nfield (<code>id: -1</code> with <code>new DataContainer(&#39;id&#39;)</code>), or without a key field as <code>__KEY</code> in\n<code>getChanges().newEntities</code>. <code>newKeys</code> maps each temporary key to the key the server gave the row.\nThe row gets it in its key field, or as its <code>__KEY</code> without a key field - setting it is no edit.</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> when a key in <code>newKeys</code> is not the key of a new row that is accepted (and not marked\nfor deletion), or the server&#39;s key is blank (<code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) - a map the wrong way\nround, say. Checked first: nothing is accepted then</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// saves the changes in one transaction, and answers with the id it gave each new row\ndeclare function save(changes: object): Promise&lt;{ temporaryId: number; id: number }[]&gt;;\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\ncontainer.setData([{ name: 'Cid' }], { add: true, isNew: true }); // a temporary id: -1, say\ncontainer.getDataSet()[0].name = 'Anna';\n\nconst saved = await save(container.getChanges()); // newEntities: [{ name: 'Cid', id: -1 }]\ncontainer.acceptChanges({ newKeys: new Map(saved.map((row) =&gt; [row.temporaryId, row.id])) });\n\ncontainer.getDataSet().map((row) =&gt; [row.id, row.name, row.__rowState]);\n// [[1, 'Anna', undefined], [7, 'Cid', undefined]] - if the server gave Cid the id 7\ncontainer.hasChanges(); // false</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clearMarkedForDeletion","signatures":["clearMarkedForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Removes the rows marked for deletion from the container, for good: <code>getChanges()</code> no longer lists\nthem in <code>deletedEntities</code> and <code>resetData()</code> does not bring them back, and their changes leave the\nundo history. Call it once the deletes are saved - or call <a href=\"#api/DataContainer.acceptChanges\">acceptChanges</a>, which also\naccepts the new and edited rows. <code>datasource.clearMarkedForDeletion()</code> calls it and rebuilds the\ndisplayed rows.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\nconst { deletedEntities } = container.getChanges(); // send these first\ncontainer.clearMarkedForDeletion();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getChanges","signatures":["getChanges(): Changes"],"doc":"<p>The rows added, edited and marked for deletion, as copies - see <a href=\"#api/Changes\">Changes</a> for what is\nin it and when an edit counts. <code>datasource.getChanges()</code> is the same, typed with the\ndatasource&#39;s row type.</p>\n<p>A <code>Date</code> is compared by its field&#39;s type from the <code>fields</code> of the datasources on this\ncontainer. Used without a datasource every field compares a <code>Date</code> to the second.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }, { id: 2, name: 'Bob' }]);\nconst [ann, bob] = container.getDataSet();\nann.name = 'Anna';\nbob.name = 'Robert';\nbob.name = 'Bob'; // back to the original, no edit\n\ncontainer.getChanges();\n// { newEntities: [], modifiedEntities: [{ id: 1, name: 'Anna' }], deletedEntities: [] }</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getDataSet","signatures":["getDataSet(): DataEntity[]"],"doc":"<p>Every row in the container, in the order they were set: the rows marked for deletion included,\nno filter, sort or grouping. A new array, the rows in it are the container&#39;s own (not copies).\n<code>datasource.getAllData()</code> is the same.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }, { id: 2, name: 'Bob' }]);\ncontainer.getDataSet().map((row) =&gt; row.name); // ['Ann', 'Bob']</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getKeyAttribute","signatures":["getKeyAttribute(): string | undefined"],"doc":"<p>The field that identifies a row, as given to the constructor. <code>undefined</code> when there is none,\nthen every row gets a generated key.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.getKeyAttribute(); // 'id'</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getMarkedForDeletion","signatures":["getMarkedForDeletion(): DataEntity[]"],"doc":"<p>The rows marked for deletion (<code>markForDeletion()</code> / <code>markAllForDeletion()</code>), still in the\ncontainer until <code>acceptChanges()</code> or <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code> removes them. New rows that are\nmarked are in it too, they are not in <code>getChanges().deletedEntities</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.markForDeletion(datasource.getSelectedRows());\ncontainer.getMarkedForDeletion().length; // the rows just marked</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hasChanges","signatures":["hasChanges(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when there is something to save: <code>getChanges()</code> would list a row. For an &quot;unsaved\nchanges&quot; indicator. A new row marked for deletion is no change, and neither is a field edited\nback to its original value.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\ncontainer.hasChanges(); // false\n\ncontainer.getDataSet()[0].name = 'Anna';\ncontainer.hasChanges(); // true</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"length","signatures":["length(): number"],"doc":"<p>The number of rows in the container, the rows marked for deletion included. Was <code>lenght()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const count = datasource.getDataContainer().length(); // every row, no filter</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"markAllForDeletion","signatures":["markAllForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Marks every row for deletion, like <a href=\"#api/DataContainer.markForDeletion\">markForDeletion</a> with all of them: the new rows are\nmarked too, and left out of <code>getChanges()</code>. Was <code>markForDeletion(null, true)</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.markAllForDeletion();\ncontainer.getChanges().deletedEntities; // every row that is not new</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"markForDeletion","signatures":["markForDeletion(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Marks rows for deletion: <code>getChanges()</code> lists them in <code>deletedEntities</code>, <code>__rowState</code> is\n<code>&#39;D&#39;</code>. They stay in the container: <a href=\"#api/DataContainer.unmarkForDeletion\">unmarkForDeletion</a> (or <code>resetData()</code>) takes the mark\noff again, and <a href=\"#api/DataContainer.acceptChanges\">acceptChanges</a> (or <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>) removes them once the\ndeletes are saved.</p>\n<p>A new row (from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>) is marked too, so it can be brought back. While it is marked it\nis in none of the lists of <code>getChanges()</code>: it was never saved, there is nothing to send for it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows. Rows that are not in the container are skipped.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\nconst [first, second] = container.getDataSet();\ncontainer.markForDeletion(first);\ncontainer.markForDeletion([first, second]);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"overrideEntityHandler","signatures":["overrideEntityHandler(entityHandler: any): void"],"doc":"<p>Replaces the class that wraps every row in a <code>Proxy</code> and tracks its edits, for the rows set from\nnow on. An advanced hook: the class gets the <a href=\"#api/EntityHandler\">EntityHandler</a> constructor options\n(<code>{ key, isNew, fieldType, onEdit }</code>) and must implement the proxy traps and the fields the grid\nreads (<code>__isNew</code>, <code>__isDeleted</code>, <code>__edited</code> ...). Its set trap calls <code>onEdit(row, field, oldValue)</code>\nafter a field is set, with the value the field had before: without the call the fields are not\nvalidated on edit and the edits are not in the undo history (<code>datasource.undo()</code>), and without\nthe old value undo can not put it back. <code>EntityHandler</code> is exported as a type only, so it can\nnot be extended - you write the whole handler.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>entityHandler</code> the class to use instead of <code>EntityHandler</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer, type FieldType } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// a handler class of your own, with the same constructor as EntityHandler\ndeclare const MyEntityHandler: new (options: {\n    key?: string;\n    isNew?: boolean;\n    fieldType?: (field: string) =&gt; FieldType | undefined;\n    onEdit?: (row: object, field: string, oldValue: unknown) =&gt; void;\n}) =&gt; ProxyHandler&lt;object&gt;;\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.overrideEntityHandler(MyEntityHandler);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removeAllData","signatures":["removeAllData(): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Removes every row from the container, like <a href=\"#api/DataContainer.removeData\">removeData</a> with all of them, and clears the\nundo history. Was <code>removeData(null, true)</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows removed</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.removeAllData();\ncontainer.getDataSet(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removeData","signatures":["removeData(rows: Entity | Entity[]): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Removes rows from the container, for good: they are not marked for deletion, <code>getChanges()</code>\ndoes not list them and <code>resetData()</code> does not bring them back. Their changes leave the undo\nhistory: undo never writes into a row that is not there.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows. Rows that are not in the container are skipped.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows removed</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\nconst [first] = container.getDataSet();\ncontainer.removeData(first); // [first]</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"replace","signatures":["replace(data: any[], index: number, remove: number): void"],"doc":"<p>Puts rows in at a position in the container, replacing <code>remove</code> rows there - <code>Array.splice</code> for\nthe container&#39;s rows. The new rows are wrapped and get a key like <code>setData()</code> gives them, they are\nnot new rows. The changes of the rows removed leave the undo history. Call\n<code>datasource.reloadDatasource()</code> after to show them.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>data</code> your objects</li>\n<li><code>index</code> where they go, 0 based</li>\n<li><code>remove</code> how many rows from <code>index</code> on are removed for good</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.replace([{ id: 9, name: 'Zed' }], 1, 1); // the second row is replaced\ndatasource.reloadDatasource();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resetData","signatures":["resetData(): void"],"doc":"<p>Throws away every change since the data was set: edited rows get their original values back,\nrows marked for deletion are unmarked, new rows (from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>) are removed, and the\nvalidation errors are cleared - the original values are not validated. Rows removed for good\n(<code>removeData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>) do not come back. The undo history is cleared.\n<code>datasource.resetData()</code> calls it and also rebuilds the displayed rows - use that one.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataContainer().resetData();\ndatasource.getChanges(); // { newEntities: [], modifiedEntities: [], deletedEntities: [] }</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resetDataSelection","signatures":["resetDataSelection(data: Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p><a href=\"#api/DataContainer.resetData\">resetData</a> for the given rows only: their edits are undone, a row marked for deletion is\nunmarked, a new row is removed, and their validation errors are cleared.\n<code>datasource.resetDataSelectionOnly()</code> calls it with the selected rows. Does not rebuild a\ndatasource&#39;s displayed rows.</p>\n<p>It is one step of the undo history (<code>datasource.undo()</code> brings the edits and the marks back),\nbut a new row it removed does not come back: undo never adds a row.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>data</code> the rows to reset. Rows that are not in the container are skipped</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.resetDataSelection(datasource.getSelectedRows());\ndatasource.reloadDatasource(); // show it</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setData","signatures":["setData(rows: any[], options?: { add?: boolean; isNew?: boolean }): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Sets the rows. Every row is wrapped in the proxy that tracks its edits, and gets a key. Without\n<code>add</code> the undo history is cleared, the rows start over; added rows are not in the history (undo\nnever removes a row).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> your objects</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows as the container keeps them</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 2, name: 'Bob' }], { add: true });\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 3, name: 'New' }], { add: true, isNew: true });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setErrors","signatures":["setErrors(errors: Map<string, string>): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets <code>__rowError</code> on the rows: the message for the rows whose key is in the map, <code>null</code> for every\nother row - so each call replaces the errors of the call before. For errors a server sent back\nafter saving.</p>\n<p>It is apart from the validation errors (<code>datasource.validate()</code>, <code>getErrors()</code>): this does not\nchange them, and <code>validate()</code> / <code>hasErrors()</code> do not read <code>__rowError</code>. The grid shows both on\nthe row selector - the error class, and the message as its tooltip. The rows whose error changed\nare in the <code>rows-changed</code> event, so the grid shows it without <code>gridInterface.refresh()</code>.\n<code>acceptChanges()</code> clears it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>errors</code> the error message per row, keyed by the row&#39;s key as text (<code>&#39;7&#39;</code> for <code>id: 7</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataContainer().setErrors(new Map([['7', 'Name is already taken']]));\n\ndatasource.getAllData().filter((row) =&gt; row.__rowError); // the rows with an error</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"unmarkAllForDeletion","signatures":["unmarkAllForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Takes the mark off every row marked for deletion, like <a href=\"#api/DataContainer.unmarkForDeletion\">unmarkForDeletion</a> with all of them.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.markAllForDeletion();\ncontainer.unmarkAllForDeletion();\ncontainer.getMarkedForDeletion(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"unmarkForDeletion","signatures":["unmarkForDeletion(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Takes the mark of <a href=\"#api/DataContainer.markForDeletion\">markForDeletion</a> off rows again: undo a delete. A row is shown and\nlisted in <code>getChanges()</code> as before it was marked - a new row as a new row, an edited row with its\nedits. Unlike <code>resetData()</code>, no edit is undone.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows. Rows that are not in the container, or not marked, are skipped.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\ncontainer.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\nconst [ann] = container.getDataSet();\n\ncontainer.markForDeletion(ann);\nann.__rowState; // 'D'\ncontainer.unmarkForDeletion(ann);\nann.__rowState; // undefined, as it was</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Datasource","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class Datasource<T = any>"],"doc":"<p>The rows of a grid, and what is done with them: the data, the fields (type, label and formatter of\neach), the filter, sorting, grouping, selection, the current row and the edits (<code>getChanges()</code>).\nIt works without a grid too.</p>\n<p>A grid shows one datasource: give it to <code>createGrid()</code>. What you do here - <code>filter()</code>, <code>sort()</code>,\n<code>setData()</code> ... - sends an event (see <a href=\"#api/DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a>), and the grid shows the result.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of your rows. The rows the datasource hands out are <a href=\"#api/EntityUnion\">EntityUnion</a><code>&lt;T&gt;</code>:\nyour object with the key and the edit tracking fields</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    born: Date;\n}\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id', fields: { born: 'date' } });\ndatasource.setData([\n    { id: 1, name: 'Ann', born: new Date(1990, 4, 17) },\n    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', born: new Date(1985, 0, 2) }\n]);\n\ndatasource.filter(where('name', 'BEGIN_WITH', 'a'));\ndatasource.sort({ attribute: 'born', ascending: false });\ndatasource.getDataRows().map((row) =&gt; row.name); // ['Ann']</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new Datasource<T = any>(options?: DatasourceOptions): Datasource<T>"],"doc":"<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of your rows. The rows the datasource hands out are <a href=\"#api/EntityUnion\">EntityUnion</a><code>&lt;T&gt;</code>:\nyour object with the key and the edit tracking fields</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>options</code> the key, the fields and their formatters, the selection mode, or a data\ncontainer shared with another datasource - all optional, see <a href=\"#api/DatasourceOptions\">DatasourceOptions</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> when <code>key</code> and <code>container</code> are both given and <code>key</code> is not the container&#39;s key, a\nfield has a type that does not exist, a formatter id or a validator id is not registered (see\n<a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a> and <a href=\"#api/registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>), a rule&#39;s options are wrong, or a field\nhas another type or other rules than in a datasource made earlier on the same <code>container</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    key: 'id',\n    fields: { born: 'date', age: { type: 'number', label: 'Age' } }\n});\ndatasource.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann', born: new Date(1990, 4, 17), age: 36 }]);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"currentEntity","signatures":["currentEntity: GroupRow | EntityUnion<T> | null"],"doc":"<p>The current row: the one last clicked, selected or set with <code>setRowAsCurrentEntity()</code>. Use it\nfor a detail form next to the grid. <code>null</code> until a row is made current.</p>\n<p>When grouped it can be a <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>: moving the focus up from the first data row into\nthe header filter row makes row 0 current, and that is a group row when grouped.\n<code>setRowAsCurrentEntity(row)</code> does the same for a group row&#39;s index. Clicking a group row,\n<code>select()</code> and <code>selectNext()</code> ... never make one current. Check with <a href=\"#api/isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a>.</p>\n<p><code>setData()</code> sets it to <code>null</code> when the current row is no longer in the data - the rows were\nreplaced by new objects, also ones with the same key - and keeps it when it still is (rows added,\nor the same row objects set again). The methods that remove rows set it to <code>null</code> when they\nremove it: <code>removeData()</code>, <code>removeAllData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>, <code>acceptChanges()</code> (a\nrow marked for deletion), <code>resetData()</code> and <code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code> (a new row). The\n<code>current-entity</code> event is sent when it changes.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const detailForm: { show(row: object): void; clear(): void };\n\ndatasource.on('current-entity', () =&gt; {\n    const row = datasource.currentEntity;\n    if (row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(row)) {\n        detailForm.show(row);\n    } else {\n        detailForm.clear();\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Accessors","members":[{"name":"type","signatures":["get type(): string"],"doc":"<p>Always <code>&#39;Datasource&#39;</code>. Tells a datasource from other objects without <code>instanceof</code>, which fails when\ntwo copies of the package are loaded.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const isDatasource = (value: any) =&gt; value?.type === 'Datasource';\nisDatasource(datasource); // true</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"acceptChanges","signatures":["acceptChanges(options?: { newKeys?: ReadonlyMap<string | number, string | number>; rows?: Entity | Entity[] }): void"],"doc":"<p>Call it after a successful save, to show what was saved: the changes are on the server now, so\nthey are no changes any more. For every row (or the <code>rows</code> given):</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a row marked for deletion is removed, a new one too</li>\n<li>a new row becomes an ordinary row (<code>__rowState</code> <code>undefined</code>)</li>\n<li>the values a row has now become its original values: nothing counts as edited</li>\n<li>the row&#39;s error (<code>setErrors()</code>) and its validation errors are cleared</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Then <code>getChanges()</code> lists none of them, <code>hasChanges()</code> is <code>false</code> when every row was accepted,\nand <code>resetData()</code> goes back to these values. The undo history is cleared - also when only some\nrows were accepted: the saved values are the originals now, undoing past them would make edits\nof them. The displayed rows are rebuilt and <code>collection-filtered</code> is sent once, with\n<code>info: &#39;acceptChanges&#39;</code>. When the current row was\nremoved, <a href=\"#api/Datasource.currentEntity\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code> and <code>current-entity</code> is sent after; a removed\nrow leaves the selection (<code>selection-change</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>The keys of new rows.</strong> A new row has a temporary key, a generated negative number: in its key\nfield (<code>id: -1</code> with <code>key: &#39;id&#39;</code>), or without a key field as <code>__KEY</code> in\n<code>getChanges().newEntities</code>. <code>newKeys</code> maps each temporary key to the key the server gave the row.\nThe row gets it in its key field, or as its <code>__KEY</code> without a key field - setting it is no edit,\nand a selected row stays selected.</p>\n<p>Keep the grid readonly while the save runs (<code>gridInterface.updateConfig({ readonly: true })</code>):\nan edit made in between is accepted too, without being saved.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it. Call\n<code>reloadDatasource()</code> on the others.</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> when a key in <code>newKeys</code> is not the key of a new row that is accepted (and not marked\nfor deletion), or the server&#39;s key is blank (<code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) - a map the wrong way\nround, say. Checked first: nothing is accepted then</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n}\n// saves the changes in one transaction, and answers with the id it gave each new row\ndeclare function save(changes: object): Promise&lt;{ temporaryId: number; id: number }[]&gt;;\n\nconst people = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id' });\npeople.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }, { id: 2, name: 'Bob' }]);\nconst [ann, bob] = people.getDataRows();\nann.name = 'Anna';\npeople.markForDeletion(bob);\npeople.addNewEmpty({ name: 'Cid' }); // a temporary id: -1, say\n\nconst saved = await save(people.getChanges());\npeople.acceptChanges({ newKeys: new Map(saved.map((row) =&gt; [row.temporaryId, row.id])) });\n\npeople.getDataRows().map((row) =&gt; [row.id, row.name, row.__rowState]);\n// [[1, 'Anna', undefined], [7, 'Cid', undefined]] - Bob is gone, Cid has the server's id\npeople.hasChanges(); // false\n\n// only some rows were saved\npeople.acceptChanges({ rows: people.getSelectedRows() });</code></pre>\n","samples":["saving"]},{"name":"addNewEmpty","signatures":["addNewEmpty(row?: Partial<T>, options?: { scrollTo?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Adds a new row at the end: <code>getChanges()</code> lists it in <code>newEntities</code>, its <code>__rowState</code> is <code>&#39;N&#39;</code>.\nWhen grouped it is put in its group, and the group is expanded.</p>\n<p>The row gets a generated key, a negative number: with a key field it is written there\n(<code>{ company: &#39;NEW COMPANY&#39;, id: -1 }</code>), else it is the row&#39;s <code>__KEY</code>. After the save,\n<code>acceptChanges({ newKeys })</code> gives it the key from the server, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.acceptChanges\">acceptChanges</a>.</p>\n<p>Adding the row is not a step of the undo history: <a href=\"#api/Datasource.undo\">undo</a> never removes it. Its edits after\nare steps, like any edit.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the values of the new row, default none. The object itself becomes the row.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.addNewEmpty();\ndatasource.addNewEmpty({ company: 'NEW COMPANY' });\ndatasource.addNewEmpty({ company: 'NEW COMPANY' }, { scrollTo: false });</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"aggregate","signatures":["aggregate(field: string, fn: AggregateFunction, rows?: Entity[] | GroupRow): number | null"],"doc":"<p>Sums up a field over rows: its sum, average, smallest or largest number, or how many values it\nhas - see <a href=\"#api/AggregateFunction\">AggregateFunction</a>. Blank values are left out, <code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>min</code> and <code>max</code>\ntake numbers only. Nothing is rounded, format the result with the field&#39;s formatter\n(<code>getFormatter(field).format(value)</code>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>No rows given</strong>: the rows the filter lets through, <code>getDataRows()</code> - when grouped, the rows of\ncollapsed groups too. Rows marked for deletion count until they are saved, as they are rows\nof the grid until then.</li>\n<li><strong>A group row</strong>: the data rows of the group, of its sub groups - collapsed ones too.</li>\n<li><strong>A list of rows</strong>: those rows, e.g. <code>getSelectedRows()</code>. Computed on each call.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The value of the filtered rows and of a group row is kept until a value of the field changes (set\non a row: an edit, <code>undo()</code>, <code>upsert()</code> ...) or other rows are filtered (<code>filter()</code>, <code>setData()</code>,\nrows added or removed). Asking again is cheap: the grid asks on every rebuild, and for every\ngroup row it renders. A sort changes no value; a filter, sort or <code>group()</code> makes new group rows.</p>\n<p>The grid shows these in its group rows and its totals row: a column&#39;s <code>aggregate</code> in the grid\nconfig, see the aggregates guide.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code> the field, the property on the row</li>\n<li><code>fn</code> <code>&#39;sum&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;avg&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;min&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;max&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;count&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>rows</code> the rows: left out the filtered rows, a group row, or a list of data rows</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the number, <code>null</code> for the average, smallest or largest of no numbers</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>fn</code> is no aggregate function</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.aggregate('balance', 'sum'); // 1234567.89, over the rows the filter lets through\ndatasource.aggregate('age', 'avg'); // 38.5, or null when no row has an age\ndatasource.aggregate('email', 'count'); // the rows with an email\n\n// per group, the rows of collapsed groups included\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\nfor (const row of datasource.getRows()) {\n    if (isGroupRow(row)) {\n        console.log(row.__groupName, datasource.aggregate('balance', 'sum', row));\n    }\n}\n\n// the selected rows, formatted as the field shows its values\nconst sum = datasource.aggregate('balance', 'sum', datasource.getSelectedRows());\ndatasource.getFormatter('balance').format(sum);</code></pre>\n","samples":["aggregates"]},{"name":"canRedo","signatures":["canRedo(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when there is a step to <a href=\"#api/Datasource.redo\">redo</a>: undo took one back, and nothing was recorded since.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const redoButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\nredoButton.disabled = !datasource.canRedo();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"canUndo","signatures":["canUndo(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when there is a step to <a href=\"#api/Datasource.undo\">undo</a>. With the <code>history-changed</code> event, for an Undo button\nof your own.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const undoButton: HTMLButtonElement;\ndeclare const redoButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\ndatasource.on('history-changed', () =&gt; {\n    undoButton.disabled = !datasource.canUndo();\n    redoButton.disabled = !datasource.canRedo();\n});\nundoButton.onclick = () =&gt; datasource.undo();\nredoButton.onclick = () =&gt; datasource.redo();</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"clearHistory","signatures":["clearHistory(): void"],"doc":"<p>Empties the undo history: nothing to undo or redo. The edits stay as they are. Sends\n<code>history-changed</code> with <code>info: &#39;clear&#39;</code> when there was something in it.</p>\n<p>Done by the datasource itself where undoing past would be wrong: <code>setData()</code> without <code>add</code>,\n<code>removeAllData()</code>, <code>resetData()</code> and <code>acceptChanges()</code> - after a save the saved values are the\noriginals.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataRows()[0].name = 'Changed';\ndatasource.clearHistory();\ndatasource.canUndo(); // false, the name stays 'Changed'</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clearMarkedForDeletion","signatures":["clearMarkedForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Removes the rows marked for deletion for good, once the deletes are saved: they leave the rows,\n<code>getChanges()</code> no longer lists them in <code>deletedEntities</code>, and <code>resetData()</code> does not bring them\nback. Sends <code>collection-changed</code> with <code>{ removed: true, info: &#39;clearMarkedForDeletion&#39; }</code>. When\nthe current row is removed, <a href=\"#api/Datasource.currentEntity\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code> and <code>current-entity</code> is sent\nafter; a removed row leaves the selection (<code>selection-change</code>).</p>\n<p>When the new and edited rows were saved in the same go, call <a href=\"#api/Datasource.acceptChanges\">acceptChanges</a> instead: it\nremoves the marked rows and accepts the rest. The changes of the removed rows leave the undo\nhistory.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const { deletedEntities } = datasource.getChanges();\nawait fetch('/api/people/delete', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(deletedEntities) });\ndatasource.clearMarkedForDeletion();</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"collapseGroup","signatures":["collapseGroup(id?: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Collapses a group, so only its group row is displayed, or every group with their sub groups.\nSends <code>collection-collapse</code>. Does nothing while the datasource is not grouped.</p>\n<p>The rows of a collapsed group are not in <code>getRows()</code>, but they are in <code>getDataRows()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the group&#39;s <code>__groupID</code> (see <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>). Left out, every group is collapsed</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.collapseGroup('Norway');\ndatasource.collapseGroup(); // every group: getRows() has the group rows only</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"deselectAll","signatures":["deselectAll(options?: { notify?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Deselects every row.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.deselectAll({ notify: true });</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"expandGroup","signatures":["expandGroup(id?: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Expands a group, so its rows are displayed, or every group with their sub groups. Sends\n<code>collection-expand</code>. Does nothing while the datasource is not grouped.</p>\n<p>A sub group is only shown when the groups above it are expanded: expanding one expands the groups\nabove it too, so it is shown. An id that is no group changes nothing.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the group&#39;s <code>__groupID</code> (see <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>), e.g. <code>&#39;Norway&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;Norway-Apple&#39;</code> for a\nsub group. Left out, every group is expanded</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.expandGroup('Norway'); // the rows of Norway are shown\ndatasource.expandGroup(); // every group</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"filter","signatures":["filter(expression?: FilterExpression | null): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the filter and runs it. The rows it lets through are sorted and grouped the way the\ndatasource is, and are what <code>getRows()</code> returns.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>filter(expression)</code> - filter on this, it replaces the filter there was</li>\n<li><code>filter(null)</code> - no filter, every row is shown</li>\n<li><code>filter()</code> - run the current filter again</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The root can be a group or a single condition. Conditions without a field or operator, date\nconditions without the value they need and empty groups are ignored. The datasource keeps the\nobject it is given, <code>getFilter()</code> returns it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>expression</code> a condition or a group of them, see <a href=\"#api/FilterExpression\">FilterExpression</a>. Build it with\n<a href=\"#api/and\">and</a>, <a href=\"#api/or\">or</a> and <a href=\"#api/where\">where</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('balance', 'GREATER_THAN', 2500));\n\n// country = 'Norway' AND (age &lt; 30 OR age &gt; 60)\ndatasource.filter(\n    and(where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'), or(where('age', 'LESS_THAN', 30), where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 60)))\n);\n\ndatasource.filter(); // run it again\ndatasource.filter(null); // every row</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"filterChangedOnly","signatures":["filterChangedOnly(on: boolean): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows only the changed rows: the new rows, the edited ones and the ones marked for deletion -\nthe rows with a <code>__rowState</code>. On top of the filter there is: a row is shown when the filter lets\nit through AND it is changed. Runs the filter, as <code>filter()</code> does.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>It is not part of the filter</strong>: <code>getFilter()</code>, the header filters, the filter editor,\n<code>getFilterString()</code> and the grid&#39;s state (<code>GridState.filter</code>) do not have it, and setting the\nfilter (<code>filter()</code>, the header filters, the filter editor) leaves it on. It stays on until it\nis turned off: <code>filterChangedOnly(false)</code>, the grid&#39;s row menu (View: Changed rows only) or the\nfooter&#39;s Clear.</li>\n<li><strong>It is applied when the rows are filtered</strong>, as the filter is: <code>filter()</code>, a header filter,\n<code>setData()</code>, <code>reloadDatasource()</code>, marking rows for deletion, <code>acceptChanges()</code> ... An edit does\nnot filter the rows again, so a row edited back to its original values stays shown until the\nrows are filtered next - it does not disappear while the user types in it.</li>\n<li>The grid shows it in the footer, as a chip in front of the filter&#39;s.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>on</code> <code>true</code> for the changed rows only, <code>false</code> for every row the filter lets through</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'));\ndatasource.filterChangedOnly(true); // the changed rows in Norway\ndatasource.isChangedOnly(); // true\ndatasource.getFilter(); // still { field: 'country', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'Norway' }\ndatasource.filterChangedOnly(false); // every row in Norway again</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"getAllData","signatures":["getAllData(): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>Every row in the data: no filter, sort or grouping, the rows marked for deletion included, never a\ngroup row. A new array, the rows in it are the rows themselves (not copies). Shared with every\ndatasource on the same data container.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#api/Datasource.getDataRows\">getDataRows</a> has the rows that pass the filter, sorted; <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getRows\">getRows</a> what the grid shows.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 60));\ndatasource.getDataRows().length; // the rows over 60\ndatasource.getAllData().length; // every row</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"getChanges","signatures":["getChanges(): Changes<T>"],"doc":"<p>The rows added, edited and marked for deletion since the data was set, as copies - what to send\nto a server. See <a href=\"#api/Changes\">Changes</a> for what is in it and when an edit counts: a field edited back\nto its original value is not listed, a <code>date</code> field compares on the day, a <code>datetime</code> field to\nthe second.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    born: Date;\n}\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id', fields: { born: 'date' } });\ndatasource.setData([\n    { id: 1, name: 'Ann', born: new Date(1990, 4, 17) },\n    { id: 2, name: 'Bob', born: new Date(1985, 0, 2) }\n]);\nconst [ann, bob] = datasource.getDataRows();\nann.name = 'Anna';\nbob.born = new Date(1985, 0, 2, 13, 30); // the same day: no edit\ndatasource.addNewEmpty({ name: 'New' });\ndatasource.markForDeletion(bob);\n\nconst { newEntities, modifiedEntities, deletedEntities } = datasource.getChanges();\n// newEntities:      [{ name: 'New', id: -1 }] - a generated key\n// modifiedEntities: [{ id: 1, name: 'Anna' }]\n// deletedEntities:  [{ id: 2, name: 'Bob', born: ... }]</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"getConflicts","signatures":["getConflicts(rows?: Entity | Entity[]): Conflict<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>The conflicts <a href=\"#api/Datasource.upsert\">upsert</a> found: a field the server changed that the user has edited (the\nuser&#39;s value is kept), or a row the server no longer has that has changes here (the row is kept) -\nsee <a href=\"#api/Conflict\">Conflict</a>. Every row&#39;s, or the rows given, in the order of the rows. New objects every\ncall: <code>local</code> is the value the row has now.</p>\n<p>A conflict stays until it is resolved (<a href=\"#api/Datasource.resolveConflict\">resolveConflict</a>) or what it is about is gone: the\nfield is not edited any more (reverted with <code>resetField()</code> or <code>resetRows()</code>, undone, typed back\nto the server&#39;s value, saved with <code>acceptChanges()</code>), the row has no changes any more, or the row\nleaves the data (<code>removeData()</code>, <code>setData()</code> without <code>add</code> ...). <code>resetData()</code> clears every one.\n<code>conflicts-changed</code> is sent when they change.</p>\n<p>The conflicts are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, default every row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const conflictCount: HTMLElement;\n\ndatasource.on('conflicts-changed', () =&gt; {\n    conflictCount.textContent = String(datasource.getConflicts().length);\n});\n\nfor (const conflict of datasource.getConflicts()) {\n    if (conflict.field === null) {\n        console.log(`row ${conflict.row.__KEY} was removed on the server`);\n    } else {\n        console.log(`${conflict.field}: yours ${conflict.local}, the server's ${conflict.remote}`);\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"getDataContainer","signatures":["getDataContainer(): DataContainer"],"doc":"<p>The data container that holds the rows and tracks the edits: the one given as\n<code>DatasourceOptions.container</code>, or the one the datasource made. See <a href=\"#api/DataContainer\">DataContainer</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const container = datasource.getDataContainer();\ncontainer.setErrors(new Map([['7', 'Name is already taken']]));</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getDataRows","signatures":["getDataRows(): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>Returns the data rows: filtered and sorted, never a <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>, and when grouped the rows\nof collapsed groups included. Was <code>getRows(true)</code> in v5.</p>\n<p>It is the datasource&#39;s own list, not a copy - do not change it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.collapseGroup();\n\ndatasource.getRows(); // the group rows only, every group is collapsed\ndatasource.getDataRows().map((row) =&gt; row.name); // every row that passes the filter</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"getErrors","signatures":["getErrors(rows?: Entity | Entity[]): ValidationError<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>The validation errors the rows have now, without validating: from the edits, and the last\n<a href=\"#api/Datasource.validate\">validate</a>. Every row&#39;s, or the rows given. Same entries as <code>validate()</code> returns. A row\nmarked for deletion has none (its errors are back when it is unmarked).</p>\n<p>The server&#39;s error of a row (<code>setErrors()</code>) is not in it, read it as <code>row.__rowError</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, default every row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the errors of the current row, for a form next to the grid\nconst row = datasource.currentEntity;\nif (row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(row)) {\n    for (const { field, messages } of datasource.getErrors(row)) {\n        console.log(datasource.getField(field).label, messages.join(', '));\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"]},{"name":"getExpanded","signatures":["getExpanded(): string[]"],"doc":"<p>The ids (<code>__groupID</code>) of the expanded groups. It is what <code>GridState.expandedGroups</code> holds. A new\narray.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.expandGroup('Norway');\ndatasource.getExpanded(); // ['Norway']</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getField","signatures":["getField(name: string): Field"],"doc":"<p>A field as the datasource sees it: its type, label, formatter, validation rules and whether it\nis multiline, with every default filled in. A field that is not listed in <code>fields</code> is a <code>&#39;text&#39;</code>\nfield labelled with its name, without rules.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>name</code> the field name, the property on the row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { born: { type: 'date', label: 'Born' } } });\n\ndatasource.getField('born'); // { name: 'born', type: 'date', label: 'Born', formatter: DateFormatterYYYYMMDD, validate: [], multiline: false }\ndatasource.getField('name'); // { name: 'name', type: 'text', label: 'name', formatter: TextFormatter, validate: [], multiline: false }\n// formatter: the formatter object, looked up by its id when the datasource was made</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getFilter","signatures":["getFilter(): FilterExpression | null"],"doc":"<p>The filter that is set: the object given to <code>filter()</code> / <code>setFilter()</code>, the header filters and\nthe filter editor&#39;s, or null when there is none. The root is a group or a single condition.</p>\n<p>It is the datasource&#39;s own object, not a copy.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18));\ndatasource.getFilter(); // { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: 18 }\n\n// typing 'x' in the header filter of name adds to it\ndatasource.getFilter();\n// { group: 'AND', children: [\n//     { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: 18 },\n//     { field: 'name', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'x' }\n// ] }\n\ndatasource.filter(null);\ndatasource.getFilter(); // null</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"getFilterFromType","signatures":["getFilterFromType(type: string): FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>The operator a header filter of this type starts with: <code>&#39;GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO&#39;</code> for\n<code>&#39;number&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;date&#39;</code> and <code>&#39;datetime&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;EQUAL&#39;</code> for the rest - for text the whole text, <code>ann</code>\ndoes not find <code>Anna</code>. The grid uses it for a column without an <code>operator</code> in its config\n(<code>columns: { name: { operator: &#39;CONTAINS&#39; } }</code> for a contains search).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type</code> a field type, see <a href=\"#api/FieldType\">FieldType</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getFilterFromType('number'); // 'GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO'\ndatasource.getFilterFromType('text'); // 'EQUAL'</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getFilterString","signatures":["getFilterString(label?: (field: string) => string): string"],"doc":"<p>The filter as text, e.g. <code>([NAME] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; &#39;X&#39;)</code>, upper case. Values are shown with the\nfield&#39;s formatter, a <code>valueField</code> as <code>[LABEL]</code>. What the filter ignores - incomplete conditions,\nempty groups - is left out, and <code>&#39;&#39;</code> is returned when nothing is left (or no filter is set).</p>\n<p>The operators and AND / OR are texts, the ids <code>filterString.*</code> of <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>: change them with\n<a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a> (<code>&#39;filterString.operator.EQUAL&#39;: &#39;equal_to&#39;</code> is shown as <code>&lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt;</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>label</code> the name to show for a field. Default the field&#39;s label (<code>FieldConfig.label</code>, else\nthe field name). The grid passes its column labels.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, Datasource, or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { born: { type: 'date', label: 'Born' } } });\ndatasource.filter(where('born', 'GREATER_THAN', new Date(1990, 0, 1)));\n\ndatasource.getFilterString(); // &quot;([BORN] &lt;&lt;GREATER_THAN&gt;&gt; '1990-01-01')&quot;\ndatasource.getFilterString((field: string) =&gt; `${field}!`); // &quot;([BORN!] &lt;&lt;GREATER_THAN&gt;&gt; '1990-01-01')&quot;\n\ndatasource.filter(and(where('a', 'EQUAL', 'x'), or(where('b', 'EQUAL', 'y'), where('b', 'EQUAL', 'z'))));\ndatasource.getFilterString(); // &quot;([A] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; 'X' AND ([B] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; 'Y' OR [B] &lt;&lt;EQUAL_TO&gt;&gt; 'Z'))&quot;</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"getFilterTree","signatures":["getFilterTree(label?: (field: string) => string): FilterGroupNode | null"],"doc":"<p>Same information as <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getFilterString\">getFilterString</a>, but as a tree of <a href=\"#api/FilterNode\">FilterNode</a>s that\nkeeps the group nesting, so the footer can render grouped conditions as clusters\ninstead of a flat, ambiguous list. The root is always a group, also when the filter is a\nsingle condition. What the filter ignores is left out: incomplete conditions are, an empty\ngroup is a group with no children. Returns <code>null</code> when no filter is set or nothing of it is\nshown - when <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getFilterString\">getFilterString</a> returns <code>&#39;&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>label</code> the name to show for a field. Default the field&#39;s label (<code>FieldConfig.label</code>, else\nthe field name). The grid passes its column labels.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { age: { type: 'number', label: 'Age' } } });\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18));\n\ndatasource.getFilterTree();\n// { kind: 'group', logicalOperator: 'AND', children: [\n//     { kind: 'condition', label: 'Age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: '18', hasValue: true }\n// ] }</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"getFormatter","signatures":["getFormatter(field: string, type?: FieldType): Formatter"],"doc":"<p>The formatter for a field: its own (<code>FieldConfig.formatter</code>), else the datasource&#39;s default for\nits type. The formatter object, as registered under the id the options name (see\n<a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>) when the datasource was made.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code> the field name. A field that is not listed in <code>fields</code> is <code>&#39;text&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>type</code> use this type instead of the field&#39;s. When it is not the field&#39;s type, the default\nformatter for <code>type</code> is returned - the field&#39;s own formatter is written for its own type. The\ngrid uses it for <code>dynamicCellTypeColumn</code>, where another column of the row decides the type.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'numberComma' }, born: 'date' }\n});\n\ndatasource.getFormatter('price').format(12.5); // '12,5'\ndatasource.getFormatter('born').format(new Date(2026, 10, 20)); // '2026-11-20'\ndatasource.getFormatter('value', 'number').parse('12.5'); // 12.5, the default number formatter</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getGrouping","signatures":["getGrouping(): GroupArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>The grouping: the fields grouped on, the outer group first. <code>[]</code> when not grouped. It is what\n<code>GridState.grouping</code> holds. The datasource&#39;s own array, not a copy - change the grouping with\n<a href=\"#api/Datasource.group\">group</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.getGrouping(); // [{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"getLastSorting","signatures":["getLastSorting(): SortArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>The sort that is set: the fields and directions, the first decides. When grouped, the grouped\nfields come first. <code>[]</code> when the rows are not sorted. It is what <code>GridState.sorting</code> holds.</p>\n<p>It is the datasource&#39;s own array, not a copy - do not change it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.sort({ attribute: 'name', ascending: true });\ndatasource.getLastSorting(); // [{ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }]</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getMarkedForDeletion","signatures":["getMarkedForDeletion(): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>The rows marked for deletion with <a href=\"#api/Datasource.markForDeletion\">markForDeletion</a> / <a href=\"#api/Datasource.markAllForDeletion\">markAllForDeletion</a>: still in\nthe data until <a href=\"#api/Datasource.acceptChanges\">acceptChanges</a> or <a href=\"#api/Datasource.clearMarkedForDeletion\">clearMarkedForDeletion</a> removes them. The rows\nthemselves, not copies - the rows of <code>getChanges().deletedEntities</code>, plus the new rows that are\nmarked (they are not sent to a server).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.markForDeletion(datasource.getSelectedRows());\ndatasource.getMarkedForDeletion().length; // the rows just marked</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getMergedAt","signatures":["getMergedAt(row: Entity, field: string): number | undefined"],"doc":"<p>When the last <a href=\"#api/Datasource.upsert\">upsert</a> changed the value of a field of a row: the <code>Date.now()</code> of that upsert.\n<code>undefined</code> when no upsert changed it. A value set by the user or by code does not count, nor\ndoes a conflict (the value stays the user&#39;s). For a short highlight on the cells a merge changed:\nthe grid renders the rows an upsert changed, a <code>cellClass</code> hook can read it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the field</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// the cells an upsert changed in the last second get a class, with a css animation that runs once\ngridInterface.updateHooks({\n    cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; {\n        const at = datasource.getMergedAt(row, field);\n        return at !== undefined &amp;&amp; Date.now() - at &lt; 1000 ? { input: 'just-changed' } : null;\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"getOrderBy","signatures":["getOrderBy(): SortArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>The sort that is set, with <a href=\"#api/Datasource.setOrderBy\">setOrderBy</a> or <a href=\"#api/Datasource.sort\">sort</a>: the same fields and directions as\n<a href=\"#api/Datasource.getLastSorting\">getLastSorting</a>. The datasource&#39;s own array, not a copy.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setOrderBy({ attribute: 'company', ascending: true });\ndatasource.getOrderBy(); // [{ attribute: 'company', ascending: true }]</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getRow","signatures":["getRow(rowNo: number): GroupRow | EntityUnion<T>"],"doc":"<p>One row of the displayed rows, <code>getRows()[rowNo]</code>. When grouped it can be a <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>, check\nwith <a href=\"#api/isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a>. Out of range gives <code>undefined</code>, though the type does not say so.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rowNo</code> the index in the displayed rows, 0 based</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst row = datasource.getRow(0);\nif (row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(row)) {\n    console.log(row.name);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getRows","signatures":["getRows(): (GroupRow | EntityUnion<T>)[]"],"doc":"<p>Returns the rows as they are displayed: filtered, sorted and grouped. When grouped, that\nis your data rows with a <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> in front of each group, and the rows of a\ncollapsed group left out.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#api/Datasource.getDataRows\">getDataRows</a> returns the data rows only - never a group row (was <code>getRows(true)</code> in v5).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\n\n// data rows and group rows, as the grid shows them\ndatasource.getRows().forEach((row) =&gt; {\n    if (isGroupRow(row)) {\n        console.log(row.__groupName);\n    } else {\n        console.log(row.name);\n    }\n});\n\n// data rows only, no check needed\nconst names = datasource.getDataRows().map((row) =&gt; row.name);</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data","sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"getSelectedRows","signatures":["getSelectedRows(): EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>The selected rows, in the order they are displayed. Data rows only, a group row can not be\nselected.</p>\n<p>Only displayed rows are returned: a selected row in a collapsed group, or one the filter leaves\nout, is not in it (it is selected again once it is displayed).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.on('selection-change', () =&gt; {\n    console.log(datasource.getSelectedRows().map((row) =&gt; row.name));\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"getSelectionMode","signatures":["getSelectionMode(): SelectionMode"],"doc":"<p>How rows can be selected: <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;single&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;none&#39;</code>, see <a href=\"#api/SelectionMode\">SelectionMode</a>. Set\nwith <code>DatasourceOptions.selectionMode</code> or <a href=\"#api/Datasource.setSelectionMode\">setSelectionMode</a>; a grid showing the datasource\nuses it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>if (datasource.getSelectionMode() === 'multiple') {\n    datasource.selectAll();\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"group","signatures":["group(groups: GroupArgument[], options?: { add?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Groups the rows: a <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> in front of each group, in <code>getRows()</code>. The rows are sorted\non the grouped fields, ascending. <code>group([])</code> removes the grouping.</p>\n<p>The groups start collapsed, apart from the ones whose id is in <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getExpanded\">getExpanded</a> (set with\n<a href=\"#api/Datasource.setExpanded\">setExpanded</a>, or expanded before): <code>getRows()</code> has only the group rows until a group is\nexpanded. The rows are grouped on their value as the field&#39;s formatter shows it, so a <code>date</code> field\ngroups by day; every blank value (null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) is one group with the id <code>&#39; blank&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>groups</code> the fields to group on, the first is the outer group</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'company', title: 'Company' }], { add: true }); // country, then company\ndatasource.group([]); // no grouping</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"hasChanges","signatures":["hasChanges(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when there is something to save: <code>getChanges()</code> would list a row. For an &quot;unsaved\nchanges&quot; indicator, or to ask before the user leaves the page. A new row marked for deletion is\nno change, and neither is a field edited back to its original value.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const saveButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\n// the grid sends no event for an edit: check when the user is about to leave\nwindow.addEventListener('beforeunload', (event) =&gt; {\n    if (datasource.hasChanges()) {\n        event.preventDefault();\n    }\n});\nsaveButton.disabled = !datasource.hasChanges();</code></pre>\n","samples":["saving"]},{"name":"hasConflicts","signatures":["hasConflicts(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when a row is in conflict, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getConflicts\">getConflicts</a>. Before a save, say: the user&#39;s values\nof a field in conflict overwrite the server&#39;s newer ones.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const saveButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\ndatasource.on('conflicts-changed', () =&gt; {\n    saveButton.title = datasource.hasConflicts() ? 'Some of your changes were also changed on the server' : '';\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"hasErrors","signatures":["hasErrors(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when a row has a validation error now: from an edit, or the last <a href=\"#api/Datasource.validate\">validate</a>. It does\nnot validate - before a save, call <code>validate()</code>, which also checks the fields never edited. The\nrows marked for deletion and the server&#39;s errors (<code>__rowError</code>) do not count.</p>\n<p>The errors are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const saveButton: HTMLButtonElement;\n\n// the grid sends no event for an edit: check when it matters\nsaveButton.disabled = datasource.hasErrors();</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"]},{"name":"isChangedOnly","signatures":["isChangedOnly(): boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> while only the changed rows are shown, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.filterChangedOnly\">filterChangedOnly</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.isChangedOnly(); // false\ndatasource.filterChangedOnly(true);\ndatasource.isChangedOnly(); // true</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"length","signatures":["length(): number"],"doc":"<p>The number of displayed rows, <code>getRows().length</code>: filtered, and when grouped the group rows\nincluded and the rows of collapsed groups left out. The number of data rows is\n<code>getDataRows().length</code> (was <code>length(true)</code> in v5).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.length(); // rows the grid shows\ndatasource.getDataRows().length; // data rows that pass the filter</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"markAllForDeletion","signatures":["markAllForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Marks every row for deletion, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.markForDeletion\">markForDeletion</a>: the new rows too. Was\n<code>markForDeletion(null, true)</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.markAllForDeletion();\ndatasource.getChanges().deletedEntities; // every row that is not new\ndatasource.unmarkAllForDeletion(); // unmarked again</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"markForDeletion","signatures":["markForDeletion(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Marks rows for deletion, so the delete can be undone: <code>getChanges()</code> lists them in\n<code>deletedEntities</code>, and <a href=\"#api/Datasource.unmarkForDeletion\">unmarkForDeletion</a> (or <code>resetData()</code>) takes the mark off again.\nThey stay in the rows, with <code>__rowState</code> <code>&#39;D&#39;</code> - the grid marks them as deleted in the row\nselector. <a href=\"#api/Datasource.acceptChanges\">acceptChanges</a> removes them once the deletes are saved.</p>\n<p>A new row (from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>) is marked too. While it is marked it is in none of the lists of\n<code>getChanges()</code> - it was never saved, there is nothing to send - and unmarked it is a new row again.</p>\n<p>In the grid, the row menu&#39;s &quot;Delete:&quot; entries mark and unmark the selected rows, see <code>MENU_IDS</code>.\nTo remove rows that are not on a server, without tracking, use <a href=\"#api/Datasource.removeData\">removeData</a>.</p>\n<p>A step of the undo history: <a href=\"#api/Datasource.undo\">undo</a> (Ctrl+Z in the grid) takes the marks off again.</p>\n<p>Sends <code>collection-filtered</code> with <code>info: &#39;markForDeletion&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, e.g. <code>getSelectedRows()</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.markForDeletion(datasource.getSelectedRows());</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"on","signatures":["on<Type extends keyof DatasourceEvents>(type: Type, handler: EventHandler<DatasourceEvents[Type]>): () => void"],"doc":"<p>Subscribes to an event. The handler gets the event&#39;s payload, typed from\n<a href=\"#api/DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a> - see there for every event and what it sends.</p>\n<p>The handler stays subscribed until you call the function this returns. What the handler\nreturns is ignored (in v5 it had to return <code>true</code> to stay subscribed).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type</code> the event name</li>\n<li><code>handler</code> called with the payload every time the event is sent</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> a function that unsubscribes the handler</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const off = datasource.on('collection-filtered', (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log('filtered by', data.info, '-', datasource.getDataRows().length, 'rows');\n});\n\ndatasource.on('current-entity', () =&gt; {\n    console.log('current row', datasource.currentEntity);\n});\n\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":["events"]},{"name":"redo","signatures":["redo(): boolean"],"doc":"<p>Does the last step <a href=\"#api/Datasource.undo\">undo</a> took back again. Recording a new step empties what there is to\nredo. The grid does it with Ctrl+Y, Ctrl+Shift+Z (Cmd+Shift+Z), and from its row menu. Sends\n<code>history-changed</code> with <code>info: &#39;redo&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> <code>false</code> when there is nothing to redo</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>if (datasource.canRedo()) {\n    datasource.redo();\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"reloadDatasource","signatures":["reloadDatasource(): void"],"doc":"<p>Builds the displayed rows again from every row in the data container: filtered, sorted and grouped\nthe way the datasource is. Sends <code>collection-filtered</code> (<code>info: &#39;filter&#39;</code>). For rows changed in the\ndata container directly (<code>getDataContainer().setData()</code>, <code>replace()</code> ...), or by another datasource\non the same container.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataContainer().setData([{ id: 3, name: 'Cid' }], { add: true });\ndatasource.reloadDatasource(); // the new row is shown, if the filter lets it through</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removeAllData","signatures":["removeAllData(): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Removes every row for good, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.removeData\">removeData</a>. Was <code>removeData(null, true)</code> in v5. Sends\nthe same <code>collection-changed</code> event, with <code>data: null</code>. The rows leave the selection and\n<a href=\"#api/Datasource.currentEntity\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code>, with their events after it. The undo history is cleared.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows removed</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.removeAllData();\ndatasource.getAllData(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"removeData","signatures":["removeData(rows: Entity | Entity[], options?: { refilter?: boolean }): Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>Removes rows for good: they are not marked for deletion, <code>getChanges()</code> does not list them and\n<code>resetData()</code> does not bring them back. Use <a href=\"#api/Datasource.markForDeletion\">markForDeletion</a> to delete rows on a server.\nTheir changes leave the undo history, and a step left without changes is dropped: undo never\nwrites into a row that is gone.</p>\n<p>Sends <code>collection-changed</code>. A removed row leaves the selection (<code>selection-change</code> is sent\nafter), and when it was the current row <a href=\"#api/Datasource.currentEntity\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code>\n(<code>current-entity</code> is sent after).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows removed</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.removeData(datasource.getSelectedRows());\n\n// many calls: rebuild the displayed rows once, at the end\nconst rows = datasource.getAllData().filter((row) =&gt; row.archived);\nrows.forEach((row, i) =&gt; datasource.removeData(row, { refilter: i === rows.length - 1 }));</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"removeGroup","signatures":["removeGroup(group?: GroupArgument): void"],"doc":"<p>Removes one level of grouping, or all of it. The sort is set to the grouped fields that are left\n(none: the rows keep the order they are in). Sends <code>collection-grouped</code> twice: <code>info: &#39;group&#39;</code> with\nthe grouping left, then <code>info: &#39;removeGroup&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>group</code> the level to remove, found by its field (<code>attribute</code>): the object from\n<a href=\"#api/Datasource.getGrouping\">getGrouping</a> or a copy, the <code>title</code> does not matter. A field that is not grouped on changes\nnothing and sends no event. Left out, all grouping is removed</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.group([\n    { attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' },\n    { attribute: 'company', title: 'Company' }\n]);\ndatasource.removeGroup({ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }); // grouped on company only\ndatasource.removeGroup(); // not grouped</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"resetData","signatures":["resetData(): void"],"doc":"<p>Throws away every change since the data was set: edited rows get their original values back,\nrows marked for deletion are unmarked, new rows (from <code>addNewEmpty()</code>) are removed, and the\nvalidation errors are cleared. Then the displayed rows are rebuilt. Rows removed for good\n(<code>removeData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>) do not come back. A new row that was the current\nrow sets <a href=\"#api/Datasource.currentEntity\">currentEntity</a> to <code>null</code> (<code>current-entity</code> is sent after), and leaves the\nselection (<code>selection-change</code>). The undo history is cleared: there is nothing left to undo.</p>\n<p>The changes are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.getDataRows()[0].name = 'Changed';\ndatasource.addNewEmpty({ name: 'New' });\n\ndatasource.resetData();\ndatasource.getChanges(); // { newEntities: [], modifiedEntities: [], deletedEntities: [] }</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"resetDataSelectionOnly","signatures":["resetDataSelectionOnly(): void"],"doc":"<p><a href=\"#api/Datasource.resetData\">resetData</a> for the selected rows only: their edits are undone, the ones marked for deletion\nare unmarked, the new ones are removed, and their validation errors are cleared. The other rows\nkeep their changes.</p>\n<p>Unlike <code>resetData()</code> it is a step of the undo history: <a href=\"#api/Datasource.undo\">undo</a> brings the edits and the\ndeletion marks back - not a new row it removed, undo never adds a row. <a href=\"#api/Datasource.resetRows\">resetRows</a> keeps\nthe new rows.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.select(1); // the first row\ndatasource.resetDataSelectionOnly(); // only that row gets its original values back</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resetField","signatures":["resetField(row: Entity, field: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Reverts one cell: the field of the row gets its original value back - the value it had when the\ndata was set, or when the changes were last accepted. A field that is not edited (that\n<code>getChanges()</code> would not list) is left as it is.</p>\n<p>It is an edit like any other: validated, and one step of the undo history - <a href=\"#api/Datasource.undo\">undo</a> brings\nthe edited value back. The grid&#39;s row menu has it as &quot;Undo cell edit&quot; (<code>row.edit.revertCell</code>). The\ngrid shows it on its own, as any value set on a row (the <code>rows-changed</code> event). A conflict of the\nfield goes with the edit, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getConflicts\">getConflicts</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row, one the datasource handed out. A row that is not in the data is skipped</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the field</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const row = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nrow.name = 'Changed';\n\ndatasource.resetField(row, 'name'); // the name it had\ndatasource.undo(); // 'Changed' again</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"resetRows","signatures":["resetRows(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Reverts rows: their fields get their original values back and a row marked for deletion is\nunmarked - <a href=\"#api/Datasource.resetDataSelectionOnly\">resetDataSelectionOnly</a>, for the rows given.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A new row stays</strong>, with the values it was added with (<code>addNewEmpty(row)</code>), still new. Unlike\n<code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code>, which removes it: a revert can be undone, and undo never adds a row\nback. To get rid of a new row, mark it for deletion.</li>\n<li>It is one step of the undo history: <a href=\"#api/Datasource.undo\">undo</a> brings the edits and the marks back.</li>\n<li>The fields are validated as for an edit: an error of an edit goes away with it, an original\nvalue that breaks a rule shows its error.</li>\n<li>The displayed rows are not rebuilt, the rows stay where they are. The grid&#39;s row menu has it\nas &quot;Undo row edits&quot; (<code>row.edit.revertRow</code>, the row right clicked, and <code>row.edit.revertRows</code>, the selected rows). The grid shows it on its own, as\nany value set on a row (the <code>rows-changed</code> event).</li>\n<li>The conflicts of the rows go with their changes, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getConflicts\">getConflicts</a>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, e.g. <code>getSelectedRows()</code>. Rows that are not in the data are\nskipped</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.resetRows(datasource.getSelectedRows());</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"resetSort","signatures":["resetSort(defaultSortAttribute?: string): void"],"doc":"<p>Clears the sort, without sorting: the rows keep their order until the displayed rows are built\nagain (<code>filter()</code>, <code>setData()</code> ...), then they are in the order they were set - sorted on the\ngrouped fields when grouped, the groups need that. No event is sent.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>defaultSortAttribute</code> a field to sort on ascending instead, set the same way (not run)</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.resetSort();\ndatasource.getLastSorting(); // []\n\ndatasource.resetSort('name');\ndatasource.sort(); // sorted on name, ascending</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resolveConflict","signatures":["resolveConflict(row: Entity, field: string | null, take: \"local\" | \"remote\"): void"],"doc":"<p>Resolves a conflict, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getConflicts\">getConflicts</a>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;local&#39;</code>: the user&#39;s value stays, still edited - <code>getChanges()</code> sends it, as an edit of the\nserver&#39;s value. For a row the server removed: the row stays with its changes, and a later\n<code>upsert(rows, { removeMissing: true })</code> gives it no conflict again (it removes it once it has no\nchanges)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;remote&#39;</code>: the field gets the server&#39;s value - its original - as <a href=\"#api/Datasource.resetField\">resetField</a> does: an\nedit, validated, a step of the undo history (<a href=\"#api/Datasource.undo\">undo</a> brings the user&#39;s value back). For a\nrow the server removed: the row is removed, as <a href=\"#api/Datasource.removeData\">removeData</a> does, with its events</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The grid shows it on its own (<code>rows-changed</code>). Nothing happens when there is no such conflict.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the field, <code>null</code> for a row the server removed</li>\n<li><code>take</code> <code>&#39;local&#39;</code> for the user&#39;s value, <code>&#39;remote&#39;</code> for the server&#39;s</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>take</code> is neither</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// the server wins every conflict\nfor (const conflict of datasource.getConflicts()) {\n    datasource.resolveConflict(conflict.row, conflict.field, 'remote');\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"select","signatures":["select(row?: number, options?: { notify?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects a row and makes it the current entity. A group row can not be selected, the first\ndata row after it is.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the row number in the displayed rows, starting on 1 (not 0 like <code>getRow()</code>).\nDefault the first row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.select(5); // the fifth displayed row, getRow(4)\ndatasource.select(5, { notify: true }); // and scroll the grid to it</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectAll","signatures":["selectAll(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects every displayed data row - not the rows of collapsed groups or the ones the filter leaves\nout - and sends <code>selection-change</code>. Only in the <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code> selection mode: in <code>&#39;single&#39;</code> and\n<code>&#39;none&#39;</code> it does nothing, it selects nothing and sends no event.\nClicking the grid&#39;s top left corner does the same (ctrl+click there deselects every row).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.selectAll();\ndatasource.getSelectedRows().length; // every displayed data row</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectFirst","signatures":["selectFirst(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects the first displayed data row, makes it current and sends <code>select</code> (<code>info: &#39;select-first&#39;</code>),\nso the grid scrolls to it. Does nothing when no data row is displayed.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.selectFirst();\ndatasource.currentEntity; // the first data row</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectLast","signatures":["selectLast(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects the last displayed data row, makes it current and sends <code>select</code> (<code>info: &#39;select-last&#39;</code>),\nso the grid scrolls to it. Does nothing when no data row is displayed.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.selectLast();</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectNext","signatures":["selectNext(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects the data row below the current one, makes it current and sends <code>select</code>\n(<code>info: &#39;select-next&#39;</code>). From the last row it goes to the first, and without a current row it\nstarts at the first. Group rows are skipped.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('next')!.onclick = () =&gt; datasource.selectNext();</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"selectPrev","signatures":["selectPrev(): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects the data row above the current one, makes it current and sends <code>select</code>\n(<code>info: &#39;select-prev&#39;</code>). From the first row it goes to the last. Group rows are skipped.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('prev')!.onclick = () =&gt; datasource.selectPrev();</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"setData","signatures":["setData(rows: any[], options?: { add?: boolean; refilter?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the rows, in the data container - so every datasource sharing it gets them. The rows are\nfiltered, sorted and grouped the way the datasource is: a filter that is set applies to the new\nrows too.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> your objects</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const rowsFromServer: object[];\ndeclare const moreRows: object[];\n\ndatasource.setData(rowsFromServer); // replaces the rows, the filter applies\ndatasource.setData(moreRows, { add: true });\ndatasource.setData(moreRows, { add: true, refilter: false }); // shown even if the filter leaves them out</code></pre>\n","samples":["rows-data"]},{"name":"setExpanded","signatures":["setExpanded(x: string[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets which groups are expanded, by their <code>__groupID</code>, for the next <a href=\"#api/Datasource.group\">group</a>: those groups start\nexpanded, the rest collapsed. The groups shown now do not change.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>x</code> the group ids, e.g. <code>[&#39;Norway&#39;, &#39;Norway-Apple&#39;]</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setExpanded(['Norway']);\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]); // Norway is expanded</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setFilter","signatures":["setFilter(expression: FilterExpression | null): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the filter without running it - <code>filter()</code> runs it. <code>setFilter(null)</code> removes it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>expression</code> a condition or a group, see <a href=\"#api/FilterExpression\">FilterExpression</a>, or null for no filter</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.setFilter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18));\ndatasource.filter(); // runs it</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"]},{"name":"setGrouping","signatures":["setGrouping(group: GroupArgument[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the grouping without grouping the rows now. The next call that builds the displayed rows\ngroups them - <code>group()</code>, <code>sort()</code>, <code>filter()</code>, <code>setData()</code>, <code>reloadDatasource()</code> ... - with the rows\nsorted on the grouped fields first. Until then <code>getRows()</code> is not grouped and <code>expandGroup()</code> /\n<code>collapseGroup()</code> do nothing.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>group</code> the fields to group on, the outer group first</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setGrouping([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.filter(); // grouped now, the rows sorted on country first</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setLocaleCompare","signatures":["setLocaleCompare(code: string, options?: any): void"],"doc":"<p>Sorts text with an <code>Intl.Collator</code> for a language, from the next sort on. Without it text is\nsorted with <code>localeCompare()</code> of the browser&#39;s language. Filtering is not changed.</p>\n<p>Was <code>setLocalCompare()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>code</code> the language, e.g. <code>&#39;nb&#39;</code> - <code>å</code> sorts after <code>z</code></li>\n<li><code>options</code> the <code>Intl.Collator</code> options, e.g. <code>{ sensitivity: &#39;base&#39; }</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setLocaleCompare('nb');\ndatasource.sort({ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }); // ... 'Zara', 'Øystein', 'Åse'</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setOrderBy","signatures":["setOrderBy(param: SortArgument | SortArgument[], options?: { add?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the sort without sorting, <code>sort()</code> sorts. Takes the same arguments as <a href=\"#api/Datasource.sort\">sort</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>param</code> the field and direction, or a list of them</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setOrderBy({ attribute: 'company', ascending: true });\ndatasource.setOrderBy({ attribute: 'age', ascending: false }, { add: true });\ndatasource.sort(); // sorts on company, then age</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setRowAsCurrentEntity","signatures":["setRowAsCurrentEntity(row: number): void"],"doc":"<p>Makes a displayed row the current entity (<a href=\"#api/Datasource.currentEntity\">currentEntity</a>) and sends <code>current-entity</code>. The\nselection is not changed. A group row&#39;s index makes the group row current, an index out of range\nmakes it <code>null</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the index in the displayed rows (<code>getRows()</code>), 0 based - not 1 based like <a href=\"#api/Datasource.select\">select</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setRowAsCurrentEntity(0); // the first displayed row\ndatasource.currentEntity; // that row</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setSelectionMode","signatures":["setSelectionMode(mode: SelectionMode): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets how rows can be selected: <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;single&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;none&#39;</code>. A blank value is <code>&#39;none&#39;</code>. The\nrows selected before stay selected.</p>\n<p>The datasource owns the selection mode: a grid showing it uses this one from the next click on, it\nhas no option of its own.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>mode</code> the selection mode, see <a href=\"#api/SelectionMode\">SelectionMode</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.setSelectionMode('single'); // a click selects one row, ctrl/shift+click too\ndatasource.setSelectionMode('none'); // a click makes the row current, selects nothing</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"]},{"name":"sort","signatures":["sort(args?: SortArgument | SortArgument[], options?: { add?: boolean }): void"],"doc":"<p>Sorts the rows. When grouped, the grouped fields are sorted first.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>sort(arg)</code> - sort on one field, replacing the sort there was</li>\n<li><code>sort(arg, { add: true })</code> - add the field to the sort there is, after the fields there are.\nA field that is sorted on already gets the new direction. The grid does this on shift+click.</li>\n<li><code>sort([a, b])</code> - sort on these fields, replacing the sort there was (<code>add</code> is ignored)</li>\n<li><code>sort()</code> - sort again with the current sort</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>args</code> the field and direction, or a list of them</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.sort({ attribute: 'company', ascending: true });\ndatasource.sort({ attribute: 'age', ascending: false }, { add: true }); // company, then age\ndatasource.sort([\n    { attribute: 'country', ascending: true },\n    { attribute: 'company', ascending: false }\n]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"]},{"name":"undo","signatures":["undo(): boolean"],"doc":"<p>Takes the last step of the undo history back: the values it changed get the values they had\nbefore, a row it marked for deletion is unmarked (and the other way round). The grid does it\nwith Ctrl+Z (Cmd+Z), and from its row menu.</p>\n<p><strong>What a step is</strong>: the changes made in one go - what the user typed in one cell until the focus\nleft it, a paste or a clear over the selected rows, a <code>markForDeletion()</code> call, a revert, or what\ncode sets on the rows in one synchronous run (no <code>await</code> in between). Edits from code are\nrecorded too, they are edits like the user&#39;s. New rows (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>, <code>setData(rows, { add: true })</code>) are not in the history: undo never removes or adds a row. The last 100 steps are kept.</p>\n<p>The values are set as an edit sets them: the edit tracking follows (a value back at its original\nis no edit any more) and so does the validation. The displayed rows are not rebuilt - no filter,\nsort or grouping runs, the rows stay where they are - and <code>history-changed</code> is sent with\n<code>info: &#39;undo&#39;</code>, on which the grid renders its cells again. The history is the data container&#39;s,\nshared by the datasources on it.</p>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> <code>false</code> when there is nothing to undo</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const row = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nrow.name = 'Changed';\n\ndatasource.undo(); // true: the name it had\ndatasource.redo(); // true: 'Changed' again\ndatasource.undo();\ndatasource.undo(); // false, nothing left to undo</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"unmarkAllForDeletion","signatures":["unmarkAllForDeletion(): void"],"doc":"<p>Takes the mark off every row marked for deletion, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.unmarkForDeletion\">unmarkForDeletion</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>datasource.markAllForDeletion();\ndatasource.unmarkAllForDeletion();\ndatasource.getMarkedForDeletion(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"unmarkForDeletion","signatures":["unmarkForDeletion(rows: Entity | Entity[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Undoes a delete: takes the mark of <a href=\"#api/Datasource.markForDeletion\">markForDeletion</a> off rows again. A row is back as it\nwas before it was marked - with its edits, and a new row as a new row. Unlike <code>resetData()</code>, no\nedit is undone. A step of the undo history, like <a href=\"#api/Datasource.markForDeletion\">markForDeletion</a>.</p>\n<p>Sends <code>collection-filtered</code> with <code>info: &#39;unmarkForDeletion&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, e.g. <code>getSelectedRows()</code>. Rows that are not marked are skipped</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const rows = datasource.getSelectedRows();\ndatasource.markForDeletion(rows);\ndatasource.unmarkForDeletion(rows); // as they were</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"upsert","signatures":["upsert(rows: Partial<T>[], options?: UpsertOptions): UpsertResult<T>"],"doc":"<p>Merges rows from a server into the data by their key: for polling, or for changes a server\npushes. Needs a key (<code>new Datasource({ key: &#39;id&#39; })</code>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A row whose key is in the data</strong> gets the values of the fields the incoming row has, as the\nserver&#39;s values: the value and its original - the row is not edited by them. A field the\nincoming row does not have stays as it is. Not a step of the undo history; the fields are\nvalidated as for an edit.</li>\n<li><strong>A field the user has edited</strong> keeps the user&#39;s value. The server&#39;s value becomes its original,\nso <code>getChanges()</code> sends the user&#39;s value as an edit of what the server has now. When the server\nchanged the field too, it is a conflict (see <a href=\"#api/Datasource.getConflicts\">getConflicts</a>); when the server has the\nuser&#39;s value, the edit is done - not edited any more. A cell the user is typing in counts as\nedited: it is never overwritten.</li>\n<li><strong>A row marked for deletion</strong> gets the values too, and keeps its mark.</li>\n<li><strong>A key that is not in the data</strong>: the row is added, a loaded row (not new, not edited) - the\nobject itself, as <code>setData()</code> adds it.</li>\n<li><strong>A new row</strong> (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>) is not on the server: its key is a generated one, it never matches.</li>\n<li><strong><code>removeMissing</code></strong>: the rows whose key is not among the rows are removed for good (their changes\nleave the undo history) - not a new row, and not a row with changes of the user&#39;s (edits, a\ndeletion mark, a cell being typed in): that one stays, in conflict (<code>field: null</code>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The keys are compared as text: <code>7</code> and <code>&#39;7&#39;</code> are the same key. The key field is never written. A\nkey given twice: the second row updates what the first one added or updated.</p>\n<p>Then the displayed rows are rebuilt once - filtered (see <code>refilter</code>, and <code>filterChangedOnly()</code>),\nsorted, grouped. The selection (it follows the key), the expanded groups and the grid&#39;s scroll\nposition stay; a removed row leaves the selection, and <a href=\"#api/Datasource.currentEntity\">currentEntity</a> is set to <code>null</code>\nwhen it is removed. <code>collection-changed</code> (<code>info: &#39;upsert&#39;</code>) is sent once when rows were added or\nremoved or the displayed rows changed - not when only values changed: the grid renders those\nfrom <code>rows-changed</code>, which follows in a microtask with the rows changed, then <code>conflicts-changed</code>\nwhen the conflicts changed.</p>\n<p>Cheap on many rows: one look up per row, by its key. The rows of the other datasources on the same\ncontainer are merged too, call <code>reloadDatasource()</code> on them to show it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> the server&#39;s rows, plain objects: each with its key, and the fields sent</li>\n<li><code>options</code> <code>removeMissing</code> and <code>refilter</code>, see <a href=\"#api/UpsertOptions\">UpsertOptions</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the rows added, updated and removed, and the conflicts it made, see <a href=\"#api/UpsertResult\">UpsertResult</a></p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when the datasource has no key, <code>rows</code> is no array, or a row has no key\n(blank) - checked first, nothing is merged then</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Stock {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    price: number;\n}\ndeclare function fetchStocks(): Promise&lt;Stock[]&gt;;\n\nconst stocks = new Datasource&lt;Stock&gt;({ key: 'id', fields: { price: 'number' } });\nstocks.setData(await fetchStocks());\n\n// every second the rows the server has: gone there is gone here, unless it has changes here\nsetInterval(async () =&gt; {\n    stocks.upsert(await fetchStocks(), { removeMissing: true });\n}, 1000);\n\n// one value pushed by the server: only the fields sent change\nstocks.upsert([{ id: 7, price: 12.5 }]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate(rows?: Entity | Entity[]): ValidationError<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>Validates the rows: every field that has rules (<code>FieldConfig.validate</code>), of every row or of the\nrows given. Call it before a save - the edits are validated as they are made, but a field that\nwas never edited (an empty field of a new row, say) only here.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The rows marked for deletion are skipped</strong>: they are not saved, they have no errors.</li>\n<li><strong>Every row is checked</strong>, also a row the filter leaves out and a row that was not edited. To\ncheck only what a save sends, pass the new and edited rows (see the example).</li>\n<li><strong>The errors are kept</strong>: <code>getErrors()</code> and <code>hasErrors()</code> read them, and the grid shows them on\nthe cells and the row selectors - this sends <code>validate</code>, the grid renders its rows again. A\nfield that passes loses its error. <code>acceptChanges()</code> and <code>resetData()</code> clear them.</li>\n<li>The server&#39;s errors (<code>setErrors()</code>, <code>__rowError</code>) are apart: not checked, not returned.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The errors are those of the data container, so of every datasource sharing it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>rows</code> a row or a list of rows, default every row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the errors, one entry per field with an error: the rows in the order of the data, the\nfields in the order they are listed in <code>fields</code>. <code>[]</code> when every row is valid</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst people = new Datasource({\n    key: 'id',\n    fields: { name: { validate: ['required'] }, age: { type: 'number', validate: [{ id: 'min', value: 0 }] } }\n});\npeople.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann', age: 36 }]);\npeople.addNewEmpty({ age: -1 }); // not validated yet\n\nconst errors = people.validate();\n// [{ row: &lt;the new row&gt;, field: 'name', messages: ['Required'] },\n//  { row: &lt;the new row&gt;, field: 'age', messages: ['Must be at least 0'] }]\nif (errors.length === 0) {\n    await fetch('/api/people/save', { method: 'POST', body: JSON.stringify(people.getChanges()) });\n}\n\n// only what a save sends: the new and edited rows\npeople.validate(people.getAllData().filter((row) =&gt; row.__rowState === 'N' || row.__rowState === 'M'));</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"]}]}]},{"name":"DateElement","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class DateElement extends HTMLElement"],"doc":"<p>The <code>&lt;simple-html-date&gt;</code> element: shows the date picker or calendar of the <a href=\"#api/DateInterface\">DateInterface</a>\nconnected to it. Create it, connect an interface and put it on the page. Give it the\n<code>simple-html-date</code> class for the styles of <code>@simple-html/grid/date.css</code>.</p>\n<p>Removing it from the page unsubscribes the interface&#39;s <code>on()</code> handlers.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig;\n\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.classList.add('simple-html-date');\nelement.connectInterface(new DateInterface(config));\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"connectedCallback","signatures":["connectedCallback(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by the browser when the element is put on the page: renders the connected interface. Not for\ncalling yourself.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"connectInterface","signatures":["connectInterface(dateInterface: DateInterface): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows a date interface in this element, and renders it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>dateInterface</code> the date picker or calendar to show</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig;\n\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.connectInterface(new DateInterface(config));\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"disconnectedCallback","signatures":["disconnectedCallback(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by the browser when the element is removed from the page: disconnects the interface and\nunsubscribes its <code>on()</code> handlers. Not for calling yourself.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DateInterface","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class DateInterface"],"doc":"<p>A date picker or a calendar: its config, the selected dates and the <code>date-select</code> event. It is shown in\na <code>&lt;simple-html-date&gt;</code> element (<a href=\"#api/DateElement\">DateElement</a>). The grid uses one for its date cells and date\nheader filters; make one yourself for a date picker or calendar outside a grid. See <a href=\"#api/IDateConfig\">IDateConfig</a>\nfor the two modes.</p>\n<p>Import <code>@simple-html/grid/date.css</code> for its styles.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\nimport '@simple-html/grid/date.css';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig; // see IDateConfig, with datepicker: true\n\nconst dateInterface = new DateInterface(config);\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.classList.add('simple-html-date');\nelement.connectInterface(dateInterface);\nhost.appendChild(element);\n\ndateInterface.on('date-select', (date) =&gt; {\n    console.log(date ? date.toISOString() : 'cleared');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new DateInterface(config: IDateConfig): DateInterface"],"doc":"<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>config</code> what to show, see <a href=\"#api/IDateConfig\">IDateConfig</a>. Not copied: a date picker sets the start\nmonth and year, the time and <code>datepickerDate</code> in it</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: IDateConfig;\nconst dateInterface = new DateInterface({ ...config, datepicker: false, monthsToShow: 3, monthColumns: 3 });</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"config","signatures":["config: IDateConfig"],"doc":"<p>The config. The picker replaces it with a changed copy when the month or time changes\n(<code>nextMonth()</code>, <code>gotoNow()</code> ...), so read it here, not from the object you passed in.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"element","signatures":["element?: DateElement | null"],"doc":"<p>The element it is shown in: <code>undefined</code> until connected, <code>null</code> after the element left the page.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"lastSelected","signatures":["lastSelected: Date | null"],"doc":"<p>The day clicked last, the start of a shift+click range. <code>null</code> after a day was clicked off again.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selected","signatures":["selected: Set<number>"],"doc":"<p>The selected dates, as timestamps (<code>date.getTime()</code>: the day at 00:00 for a day clicked in a\ncalendar, the picked time in a date picker). A day is shown selected when a timestamp falls on it,\nwhatever its time. Read it with <a href=\"#api/DateInterface.getSelected\">getSelected</a>, set it with <a href=\"#api/DateInterface.setSelected\">setSelected</a>.</p>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"checkDatePicker","signatures":["checkDatePicker(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called when the element connects: in a date picker it sets the start month and year, the hour and\nthe minutes from <code>datepickerDate</code> (today when it is blank) and selects that date. Does nothing in a\ncalendar. You do not need to call it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clearSelection","signatures":["clearSelection(): void"],"doc":"<p>Unselects every day and renders the picker again.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.clearSelection();\ndateInterface.getSelected(); // []</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"connectElement","signatures":["connectElement(element: DateElement): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by the element when it is put on the page: renders the picker in it. You do not need to call\nit.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>element</code> the <code>&lt;simple-html-date&gt;</code> element</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"connectGridInterface","signatures":["connectGridInterface(element: DateElement): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by <code>element.connectInterface()</code>: shows the picker in the element. You do not need to call it.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>element</code> the <code>&lt;simple-html-date&gt;</code> element</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"disconnectElement","signatures":["disconnectElement(): void"],"doc":"<p>Called by the element when it is removed from the page: forgets the element and unsubscribes every\nhandler subscribed with <a href=\"#api/DateInterface.on\">on</a>. You do not need to call it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getSelected","signatures":["getSelected(): number[]"],"doc":"<p>The selected dates, as timestamps: the days clicked in a calendar (at 00:00), the date picked in a\ndate picker, the dates given to <a href=\"#api/DateInterface.setSelected\">setSelected</a> (with their time). In the order they were\nselected.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\nconst dates = dateInterface.getSelected().map((time) =&gt; new Date(time));</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"gotoNow","signatures":["gotoNow(): void"],"doc":"<p>Goes to the current date and time: picks it, shows its month. What the date picker&#39;s &quot;Now&quot; button\ndoes. Does not send <code>date-select</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.gotoNow();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"nextMonth","signatures":["nextMonth(): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows the next month, what the arrow in the month header does.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.nextMonth();\ndateInterface.config.startMonth; // one later, 0 again after December</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"on","signatures":["on<Type extends \"date-select\">(type: Type, handler: EventHandler<DateEvents[Type]>): () => void"],"doc":"<p>Subscribes to an event of the date picker. The handler gets the event&#39;s payload, typed\nfrom <a href=\"#api/DateEvents\">DateEvents</a> - see there for every event and what it sends.</p>\n<p>The handler stays subscribed until you call the function this returns, or the date element\nis removed from the dom. What the handler returns is ignored (in v5 it had to return <code>true</code>\nto stay subscribed).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type</code> the event name</li>\n<li><code>handler</code> called with the payload every time the event is sent</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> a function that unsubscribes the handler</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\nconst input = document.querySelector('input')!;\nconst off = dateInterface.on('date-select', (date) =&gt; {\n    input.value = date ? date.toLocaleString() : '';\n});\n\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"prevMonth","signatures":["prevMonth(): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows the month before, what the arrow in the month header does.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.prevMonth();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"render","signatures":["render(): void"],"doc":"<p>Renders the picker in its element again. The methods that change what is shown call it; call it\nafter changing <code>config</code> yourself. Does nothing while no element is connected.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.config.hideDimmedDates = true;\ndateInterface.render();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selectRangeWithFromTo","signatures":["selectRangeWithFromTo(fromDate: Date, toDate: Date): void"],"doc":"<p>Not implemented: it only logs a warning.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>fromDate</code> the first date of the range</li>\n<li><code>toDate</code> the last date of the range</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"setSelected","signatures":["setSelected(newSelectedDates: Date[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Replaces the selected days and renders the picker again. A day is shown selected when one of the\ndates falls on it - the time of a date does not matter. They are kept as timestamps, see\n<a href=\"#api/DateInterface.getSelected\">getSelected</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>newSelectedDates</code> the days to select</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\ndateInterface.setSelected([new Date(2026, 10, 20), new Date(2026, 10, 21, 9, 30)]);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"styleRange","signatures":["styleRange(StyleArray: IStyle[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Not implemented: it only logs a warning.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>StyleArray</code> the dates to style, see <a href=\"#api/IStyle\">IStyle</a></li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridElement","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class GridElement extends HTMLElement"],"doc":"<p>The <code>&lt;simple-html-grid&gt;</code> element: shows the grid of the <a href=\"#api/GridInterface\">GridInterface</a> connected to it.</p>\n<p><code>createGrid()</code> makes one for you, sized to fill a container, and is the easy way. Use the element\nyourself when you want to place and size it on your own: create it, connect an interface and add it\nto the page. It adds its <code>simple-html-grid</code> class itself; give it a size, e.g. width and height\n100% of a container with a height.</p>\n<p>Removing the element from the page disconnects the grid from the datasource and the document. Put\nback, it connects again and shows the rows as they are then.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, type GridElement, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-grid') as GridElement;\nelement.style.width = '100%';\nelement.style.height = '100%';\nelement.connectInterface(new GridInterface(config, datasource));\ndocument.getElementById('grid')!.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new GridElement(): GridElement"],"doc":"<p>Made by <code>document.createElement(&#39;simple-html-grid&#39;)</code>, or <code>new GridElement()</code> - <code>createGrid()</code> does\nthat. Connect an interface with <a href=\"#api/GridElement.connectInterface\">connectInterface</a> before or after it is put on the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, GridElement, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst element = new GridElement();\nelement.style.height = '400px';\nelement.connectInterface(new GridInterface(config, datasource));\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"connectInterface","signatures":["connectInterface(value: GridInterface<any>): void"],"doc":"<p>Shows a grid interface in this element: its config, its datasource and its state.</p>\n<p>Connecting another interface later replaces the first one, which is disconnected from its\ndatasource. The dom is kept, the grid is rebuilt for the new interface.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>value</code> the interface to show</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, type GridElement, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-grid') as GridElement;\nelement.connectInterface(new GridInterface(config, datasource));\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridInterface","group":"Classes","kind":"Class","signatures":["class GridInterface<T>"],"doc":"<p>The grid: its config, its datasource and its state. What you call to work with a grid - read and\nset the state, change an option, subscribe to events, re-render.</p>\n<p>Make one with <a href=\"#api/createGrid\">createGrid</a>, which also puts the grid on the page. <code>new GridInterface()</code> is for\na <code>&lt;simple-html-grid&gt;</code> element you place yourself, see <a href=\"#api/GridElement\">GridElement</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, from the datasource: a <code>Datasource&lt;Person&gt;</code> gives a\n<code>GridInterface&lt;Person&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(document.getElementById('grid')!, { config, datasource });\n\ngridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; console.log(data.attribute, data.rowData));\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ readonly: false });\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'age' &amp;&amp; row.age &lt; 18 ? { input: 'minor' } : null) });\nconst state = gridInterface.getState();\n\ngridInterface.destroy(); // done with it</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Constructors","members":[{"name":"constructor","signatures":["new GridInterface<T>(gridConfig: GridConfig, datasource: Datasource<T>, hooks?: GridHooks<T>): GridInterface<T>"],"doc":"<p>Most of the time <a href=\"#api/createGrid\">createGrid</a> makes the interface. Make it yourself for a\n<code>&lt;simple-html-grid&gt;</code> element you place on your own, and connect it with\n<code>element.connectInterface()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, from the datasource: a <code>Datasource&lt;Person&gt;</code> gives a\n<code>GridInterface&lt;Person&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>gridConfig</code> the columns, the layout and the options, see <a href=\"#api/GridConfig\">GridConfig</a>. The object is\nnot changed, the grid copies the parts it changes</li>\n<li><code>datasource</code> the rows. The grid applies <code>gridConfig.initialState</code> to it: its sorting,\ngrouping and filter are replaced (left out, they are cleared)</li>\n<li><code>hooks</code> optional: the functions - <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code>, <code>menus</code>, see <a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>.\nThe grid keeps a copy of the object, change them later with <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.updateHooks\">updateHooks</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>gridConfig</code> has <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> or <code>menus</code> (those are\nhooks), a column has v5&#39;s <code>mandatory</code> (it is the field&#39;s <code>required</code> rule), <code>texts</code> is not an\nobject of strings, or a column&#39;s <code>aggregate</code> is no aggregate function or needs a number field</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, type GridElement, type GridHooks, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\ndeclare const hooks: GridHooks;\n\nconst gridInterface = new GridInterface(config, datasource, hooks);\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-grid') as GridElement;\nelement.connectInterface(gridInterface);\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"autoResizeColumns","signatures":["autoResizeColumns(): void"],"doc":"<p>Sizes the columns to their content: the label, the header filter&#39;s placeholder, and the longest\nvalue of the fields in each column (every row, not only the filtered ones). A column is at most\n750px. Rebuilds the grid.</p>\n<p>Measures the text with the grid&#39;s font, so call it once the grid is on the page: right after\n<a href=\"#api/createGrid\">createGrid</a>, or from a <code>grid-connected</code> handler for an element you connect yourself. It\ndoes nothing before the interface is connected to an element.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, { config, datasource });\ngridInterface.autoResizeColumns();</code></pre>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"clearRanges","signatures":["clearRanges(): void"],"doc":"<p>Clears the ranges of cells: no cell is selected. Sends <code>range-change</code> when there were ranges.\nThe rows selected in the datasource stay selected.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('clear-selection')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.clearRanges();</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"closeMenu","signatures":["closeMenu(): void"],"doc":"<p>Closes the menu that is open: one opened with <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.openMenu\">openMenu</a>, or one of the grid&#39;s own right\nclick menus. Does nothing when no menu is open. The focus goes back as when the user closes it,\nsee <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.openMenu\">openMenu</a>.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>removeContextMenuElement()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// moving to another cell closes a dropdown opened from a cell\ngridInterface.on('cell-row-focus', () =&gt; gridInterface.closeMenu());</code></pre>\n","samples":["dropdown-grid"]},{"name":"destroy","signatures":["destroy(): void"],"doc":"<p>Removes the grid from the page and disconnects it: from the datasource, the document and the\nhandlers subscribed with <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.on\">on</a>. For a grid made with <a href=\"#api/createGrid\">createGrid</a>, when you are done\nwith it. The datasource is not changed, it can be shown again in a new grid.</p>\n<p>The element is removed also when you placed it yourself (<code>element.connectInterface()</code>). Removing\nsuch an element from the page disconnects the grid as well: there <code>destroy()</code> is not needed.</p>\n<p>Do not use the interface after this: make a new one.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, { config, datasource });\n// ...\ngridInterface.destroy(); // host is empty again</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"downloadCsv","signatures":["downloadCsv(filename?: string, options?: CsvOptions): void"],"doc":"<p>Saves the rows as a CSV file: the browser downloads it, as from a link. The text is\n<a href=\"#api/GridInterface.getCsv\">getCsv</a>&#39;s, with a UTF-8 byte order mark (BOM) first by default - Excel needs it to read\n<code>æøå</code> (<code>bom: false</code> leaves it out).</p>\n<p>For Excel in a locale with a decimal comma (Norwegian, German ...), use <code>separator: &#39;;&#39;</code>:\nExcel splits a .csv file on the list separator of the computer&#39;s locale, and with <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> every\nrow ends up in one column.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>filename</code> the name the file is saved as, default <code>&#39;export.csv&#39;</code>. Give it the <code>.csv</code>\nending yourself, it is not added</li>\n<li><code>options</code> what to export and how, see <a href=\"#api/CsvOptions\">CsvOptions</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when the filename is not a text (<code>downloadCsv({ rows: &#39;selected&#39; })</code>: the\nfilename comes first), for an option it does not know or a value an option does not take</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('export')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.downloadCsv();\n\n// the selected rows, for Excel in Norway\ngridInterface.downloadCsv('selected.csv', { rows: 'selected', separator: ';' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["export"]},{"name":"getCsv","signatures":["getCsv(options?: CsvOptions): string"],"doc":"<p>The rows as CSV text (RFC 4180): a header line with the column labels, then a line per row,\nevery line ended with CRLF. By default every row the filter lets through, in the sort order, and\nthe columns of the layout in the order the user sees them, each value as the grid shows it. See\n<a href=\"#api/CsvOptions\">CsvOptions</a> for what can be changed: the selected rows, the selected range of cells, the\nfields, the separator (<code>&#39;;&#39;</code> for Excel in Norway), raw values ...</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The rows</strong>: when grouped, every data row in the grouped order - the rows of collapsed groups\ntoo, no group rows. Rows marked for deletion are rows of the grid until they are saved, they\nare exported too.</li>\n<li><strong>Formulas</strong>: text starting with <code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>@</code> ... gets a <code>&#39;</code> in front, so a spreadsheet\ndoes not run a formula a user typed in (<code>escapeFormulas</code>).</li>\n<li><strong>No BOM</strong> by default, unlike <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.downloadCsv\">downloadCsv</a>: the text is for code of your own.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Works without the grid on the page too: it reads the config and the datasource.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>options</code> what to export and how, see <a href=\"#api/CsvOptions\">CsvOptions</a>. Every option is optional</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the CSV text, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> when there are no columns</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for an option it does not know or a value an option does not take\n(<code>rows: &#39;some&#39;</code>)</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const text = gridInterface.getCsv(); // 'Name,Born\\r\\nAnn,2001-05-17\\r\\n...'\n\n// the selected rows, semicolons for Excel in Norway, the values as they are stored\nconst selected = gridInterface.getCsv({ rows: 'selected', separator: ';', formatted: false });\n\n// two fields, no header line\nconst names = gridInterface.getCsv({ fields: ['name', 'email'], header: false });\n\n// the cells of the range the user selected, see getRanges()\nconst range = gridInterface.getCsv({ rows: 'range' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["export"]},{"name":"getDatasource","signatures":["getDatasource(): Datasource<T>"],"doc":"<p>The datasource the grid shows: its rows, selection, sorting, filter and the events for them.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const datasource = gridInterface.getDatasource();\ndatasource.on('selection-change', () =&gt; console.log(datasource.getSelectedRows().length, 'selected'));</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getHiddenFields","signatures":["getHiddenFields(): string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields the grid knows that are not in the layout now: the ones the column chooser can add\nback. The grid knows the keys of <code>GridConfig.columns</code>, and every field that has been in the\nlayout.</p>\n<p>Was <code>getOptionalAttributes()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, {\n    config: { columns: { phone: {} }, layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 100 }] } },\n    datasource\n});\ngridInterface.getHiddenFields(); // ['phone']</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getLayoutFields","signatures":["getLayoutFields(options?: { selectedOnly?: boolean }): string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields in the layout now, in the order the user sees them: pinned left, center, pinned right,\nleft to right, and top to bottom within a column of stacked fields.</p>\n<p>With <code>selectedOnly</code>, only the fields of the columns the user selected - by clicking the column\nnumbers under the header filters, ctrl+click for more. None selected gives <code>[]</code>.</p>\n<p>Was <code>getAttributeColumns(filterSelectedColumns)</code> in v5, which gave the selected columns by default\nand every column when none was selected.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.getLayoutFields(); // ['name', 'age', 'born', 'company']\ngridInterface.getLayoutFields({ selectedOnly: true }); // ['age', 'born'] - one column, two fields\n\n// the selected columns, or every column when none is selected\nconst selected = gridInterface.getLayoutFields({ selectedOnly: true });\nconst toExport = selected.length ? selected : gridInterface.getLayoutFields();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"getRanges","signatures":["getRanges(): CellRange[]"],"doc":"<p>The ranges of cells the user selected - by dragging over the cells, Shift+click, Ctrl/Cmd+click\nfor another one, Alt+Shift+arrows - or that <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.setRanges\">setRanges</a> set. See <a href=\"#api/CellRange\">CellRange</a>: rows\nare indexes in the displayed rows, fields are field names. The last range is the one made last,\nits <code>fromRow</code> / <code>fromField</code> is the active cell. <code>[]</code> when no cells are selected.</p>\n<p>Copies: changing them changes nothing in the grid.</p>\n<p>The ranges are cleared when the displayed rows change - a filter, a sort, grouping, a group\nexpanded or collapsed, rows added or removed (<code>setData()</code>, <code>upsert()</code> that adds or removes\nrows, rows marked for deletion) - and when the fields of the layout change: a column moved,\npinned, hidden or added. A column resized keeps them, and so does an edit: the rows stay where\nthey are. <code>range-change</code> is sent every time they change.</p>\n<p>The row selection of the datasource (<code>datasource.getSelectedRows()</code>) is something else: a\nrange does not select rows, selecting rows changes no range.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const ranges = gridInterface.getRanges();\nif (ranges.length) {\n    const { fromRow, fromField, toRow, toField } = ranges[ranges.length - 1];\n    console.log(`from row ${fromRow} ${fromField} to row ${toRow} ${toField}`);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"getState","signatures":["getState(): GridState"],"doc":"<p>The state of the grid now: what the user changed - column order, pinning and widths, sorting,\ngrouping, expanded groups, the filter and what the header filters show. See <a href=\"#api/GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p>It is a copy: changing it changes nothing in the grid, and what the user does later does not\nchange it. Give it to <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.setState\">setState</a> to go back to it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const state = gridInterface.getState();\nstate.layout.center.map((column) =&gt; column.fields); // [['name'], ['age', 'born']]\nstate.sorting; // [{ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }]\n\n// later, e.g. after the user moved columns and changed the filter\ngridInterface.setState(state);</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"]},{"name":"on","signatures":["on<Type extends keyof GridEvents>(type: Type, handler: EventHandler<GridEvents[Type]>): () => void"],"doc":"<p>Subscribes to an event of the grid: cell clicks and focus, copy/paste from the row menu ...\nThe handler gets the event&#39;s payload, typed from <a href=\"#api/GridEvents\">GridEvents</a> - see there for every\nevent and what it sends. Sorting, filtering, selection and data changes are events of the\ndatasource: <code>gridInterface.getDatasource().on(...)</code>, see <a href=\"#api/DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a>.</p>\n<p>The handler stays subscribed until you call the function this returns. What the handler\nreturns is ignored (in v5 it had to return <code>true</code> to stay subscribed).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>type</code> the event name</li>\n<li><code>handler</code> called with the payload every time the event is sent</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> a function that unsubscribes the handler</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const off = gridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    if (data.attribute === 'company') {\n        console.log('company clicked:', data.rowData.company);\n    }\n});\n\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":["events"]},{"name":"openFilterEditor","signatures":["openFilterEditor(): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens the filter editor, the dialog where the user builds a filter of conditions and AND/OR\ngroups. It starts with the filter the datasource has now. The user opens it from the header\nfilter&#39;s menu (&quot;Advanced Filter&quot;) or by clicking the filter shown in the footer; call this from a\nbutton of your own.</p>\n<p>It is a modal <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> (<code>showModal()</code>): over everything on the page, the page behind it can\nnot be used while it is open. The focus moves to the dialog when it opens and goes back to where\nit was when it closes; Esc closes it (a menu open in it first). The user drags it by its title\nbar and resizes it from every edge and corner, with the mouse, a finger or a pen.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>document.getElementById('advanced-filter')!.onclick = () =&gt; gridInterface.openFilterEditor();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"openMenu","signatures":["openMenu(at: HTMLElement | MouseEvent | MenuPosition, entries: MenuEntry[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Opens a menu of your own, in the grid&#39;s menu style: a value picker for a cell, the actions of a\nbutton, a second grid as a dropdown (<a href=\"#api/MenuBlock\">MenuBlock</a>). See <a href=\"#api/MenuEntry\">MenuEntry</a> for what it can\nshow. To change the grid&#39;s own right click menus, use the <code>menus</code> hook (<a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>).</p>\n<p>The menu is a popover: shown in the top layer, over everything on the page - a container with\n<code>overflow: hidden</code> does not cut it off, no z-index covers it. Opened from an element in a\n<code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> or a popover of your own, it is put inside that element, so it can be used there\n(everything outside a modal dialog is inert).</p>\n<p>The menu open before is closed: there is one menu at a time. The grid closes this one, as its\nown, on a click outside it, on Esc, when another menu opens, on scroll (with\n<code>autoRemoveContextMenuOnScrollEvent</code>) and when the grid leaves the page. Clicking an item closes\nit too, then calls the item&#39;s action; clicking in a block does not. <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.closeMenu\">closeMenu</a> closes it\nfrom code. When the focus is in the menu as it closes (a field in a block), it goes back to the\nelement that had it when the menu opened.</p>\n<p>Called from a click handler the menu stays open: the click that opened it does not count as a\nclick outside it.</p>\n<p>The callbacks of the entries get a <a href=\"#api/MenuContext\">MenuContext</a> with <code>menu: &#39;custom&#39;</code>, the grid and the\ndatasource; it has no field, row or cell - your entries know what they were made for.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>contextMenuCustom()</code> and <code>setContextMenuElement()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><code>at</code> where it opens:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a mouse event: its top left corner at the mouse</li>\n<li>a <a href=\"#api/MenuPosition\">MenuPosition</a> <code>{ x, y }</code>: its top left corner there, in px from the window&#39;s left and\ntop edges</li>\n<li>an element: under the element, lined up with its left edge</li>\n</ul>\n<p>It is kept in the window: opened above the point (or the element) when there is no room below,\nmoved left when it sticks out on the right.</p>\n</li>\n<li><p><code>entries</code> what the menu shows, in order. Entries whose <code>visible</code> returns <code>false</code> are left out</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// a value picker on a cell\ngridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    if (data.attribute === 'fruit') {\n        const pick = (fruit: string) =&gt; {\n            data.rowData.fruit = fruit;\n            gridInterface.refresh();\n        };\n        gridInterface.openMenu(data.originalEvent, [\n            { type: 'section', id: 'fruit', label: 'Pick a fruit:' },\n            { id: 'fruit.apple', label: 'Apple', action: () =&gt; pick('Apple') },\n            { id: 'fruit.banana', label: 'Banana', action: () =&gt; pick('Banana') }\n        ]);\n    }\n});\n\n// an element of your own under a cell, closed with the grid's menus\ndeclare const cell: HTMLElement;\ndeclare const myPicker: HTMLElement;\ngridInterface.openMenu(cell, [{ type: 'block', id: 'picker', element: myPicker }]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu","dropdown-grid"]},{"name":"rebuild","signatures":["rebuild(): void"],"doc":"<p>Builds the grid again: sizes, rows, columns, header, grouping panel and footer, then renders the\ncells. For when more than the visible cells changed: what a formatter returns (the header\nfilters show it too), the texts of the page (<a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a>), the size of the element without a\nresize event, a column&#39;s options changed in place. To change an option, use <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.updateConfig\">updateConfig</a> - it rebuilds too. For the cells only,\n<a href=\"#api/GridInterface.refresh\">refresh</a> is cheaper.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page, it is built when it is put there.</p>\n<p>Was <code>triggerRebuild()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type Formatter, registerFormatter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// a formatter that reads a setting of your own\nlet decimals = 2;\nconst price: Formatter = {\n    format: (value) =&gt; (typeof value === 'number' ? value.toFixed(decimals) : ''),\n    parse: (text) =&gt; (text.trim() === '' ? null : Number(text))\n};\nregisterFormatter('price', price);\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'price' } } });\n// ...\ndecimals = 0;\ngridInterface.rebuild(); // the cells and the header filter show the prices without decimals</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"refresh","signatures":["refresh(): void"],"doc":"<p>Renders the visible cells again, with the values the rows have now. For when something the\ncells show changed without a row changing: what the <code>isReadonly</code> / <code>cellClass</code> hooks read, a\nvalue written to an object of your own instead of the row. A value set on a row shows on its\nown (the datasource&#39;s <code>rows-changed</code>, rendered in the next animation frame), and a scroll only\nrenders the rows that scroll in. Cheap, the columns and the header are not built again - that\nis <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.rebuild\">rebuild</a>.</p>\n<p>The cell input the user has typed in since it got the focus is not rendered, so its text is\nkept: it is rendered once the focus leaves it.</p>\n<p>Does nothing while the grid is not on the page.</p>\n<p>Was <code>triggerScrollEvent()</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>let highlighted = 'ACME CORP';\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ cellClass: (row) =&gt; (row.company === highlighted ? { input: 'highlight' } : null) });\n\nhighlighted = 'GLOBEX'; // the hook reads it, the grid does not know\ngridInterface.refresh();</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"resetState","signatures":["resetState(): void"],"doc":"<p>Goes back to the state the grid started in: <code>GridConfig.initialState</code>, with the config&#39;s\n<code>layout</code> (unless <code>initialState</code> has one). What <code>initialState</code> leaves out is cleared - no sorting,\nno grouping, no filter, no header filters. A <code>layout</code> or <code>initialState</code> given to\n<a href=\"#api/GridInterface.updateConfig\">updateConfig</a> since is the one it goes back to.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst gridInterface = new GridInterface(\n    {\n        layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 100 }, { fields: ['age'], width: 100 }] },\n        initialState: { sorting: [{ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }] }\n    },\n    datasource\n);\n\n// the user sorts, filters and moves columns around ...\ngridInterface.resetState(); // sorted on name again, no filter, the config's columns</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"]},{"name":"setRanges","signatures":["setRanges(ranges: CellRange[]): void"],"doc":"<p>Selects ranges of cells, replacing the ones there are - as if the user had selected them. See\n<a href=\"#api/CellRange\">CellRange</a>. The cells show them, <code>range-change</code> is sent. The focus does not move and the\ngrid does not scroll to them.</p>\n<p>The grid keeps copies, with only the four keys of a range. They are cleared when the displayed\nrows or the layout change, see <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.getRanges\">getRanges</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>ranges</code> the ranges, the last one is the active one. <code>[]</code> clears them, as <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.clearRanges\">clearRanges</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> for a range with a row that is not displayed (0 to <code>datasource.length() - 1</code>)\nor a field that is not in the layout</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// rows 0 to 4, the fields from name to age\ngridInterface.setRanges([{ fromRow: 0, fromField: 'name', toRow: 4, toField: 'age' }]);\n\n// two ranges, as Ctrl+click makes them\ngridInterface.setRanges([\n    { fromRow: 0, fromField: 'name', toRow: 0, toField: 'name' },\n    { fromRow: 5, fromField: 'age', toRow: 9, toField: 'age' }\n]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]},{"name":"setState","signatures":["setState(state: Partial<GridState>): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the state: column order, pinning and widths, sorting, grouping, expanded groups, the filter\nand what the header filters show. See <a href=\"#api/GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Applies what is given and keeps the rest</strong>: <code>setState({ sorting })</code> changes the sort and\nnothing else. To set everything, pass a whole state, e.g. one from <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.getState\">getState</a>. Within a\npart nothing is merged: <code>layout</code> replaces the whole layout, <code>headerFilters</code> every header filter.</p>\n<p>The grid keeps a copy, the object passed in is not changed later. It must be plain data (no\nfunctions, no rows from the datasource): it is copied with <code>structuredClone</code>. A state stored as\nJSON can be given as it is; its <code>Date</code>s came back as ISO text, which is kept as text - see\n<a href=\"#api/GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p><code>filter</code> is what the rows are filtered by, <code>headerFilters</code> only what the header filter cells show.\nSet both to have a header filter&#39;s condition and its cell agree, as <code>getState()</code> gives them.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>state</code> the parts to set</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridState } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const savedState: GridState;\n\n// a whole state, saved before\ngridInterface.setState(savedState);\n\n// only some parts, the rest stays as it is\ngridInterface.setState({ sorting: [{ attribute: 'age', ascending: false }] });\ngridInterface.setState({ grouping: [{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }], expandedGroups: [] });\ngridInterface.setState({ filter: null, headerFilters: {} }); // no filter</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"]},{"name":"updateConfig","signatures":["updateConfig(config: Partial<GridConfig>): void"],"doc":"<p>Changes options of the config while the grid is shown: <code>readonly</code>, <code>hideLabels</code>, the sizes,\n<code>tooltips</code>, <code>columns</code> ... and rebuilds the grid once. The functions - <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code>,\n<code>menus</code> - are not part of the config, change them with <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.updateHooks\">updateHooks</a>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Only the keys given change</strong>, the rest stay as they are. A key given as <code>undefined</code> goes\nback to its default - <code>layout</code> excepted, a grid always has one.</li>\n<li><strong><code>columns</code> replaces the options of every column</strong>, nothing is merged: a field left out gets\nthe defaults.</li>\n<li><strong><code>layout</code> is shown right away</strong>, as <code>setState({ layout })</code> does: the column order, pinning and\nwidths the user made are replaced. It is also the layout <code>resetState()</code> goes back to from now\non (unless <code>initialState</code> has a layout).</li>\n<li><strong><code>initialState</code> changes nothing now</strong>: it is the state a later <code>resetState()</code> goes back to.\nCall <code>resetState()</code> after to apply it.</li>\n<li><strong><code>texts</code> replaces the grid&#39;s texts as a whole</strong>, the ids are not merged: an id left out shows\nthe page&#39;s text again (<code>setTexts()</code>). A menu or the filter editor shows them the next time it\nopens.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The rest of the state - sorting, grouping, filter, header filters - is kept, and so are the\nhandlers subscribed with <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.on\">on</a>. The object passed in is not changed, the grid copies\n<code>columns</code>, <code>layout</code> and <code>initialState</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>config</code> the parts of the config to change</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>config</code> has <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> or <code>menus</code> (those are hooks),\na column has v5&#39;s <code>mandatory</code> (it is the field&#39;s <code>required</code> rule), <code>texts</code> is not an object of\nstrings, or a column&#39;s <code>aggregate</code> is no aggregate function or needs a number field</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.updateConfig({ readonly: false }); // editing on\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ hideFilter: true, cellHeight: 30 });\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ tooltips: undefined }); // back to the default, true\n\n// the columns the config starts with, shown now and what resetState() goes back to\ngridInterface.updateConfig({ layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 200 }] } });</code></pre>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"updateHooks","signatures":["updateHooks(hooks: GridHooks<T>): void"],"doc":"<p>Changes the hooks while the grid is shown: <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> and <code>menus</code>, see\n<a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>. <strong>Only the keys given change</strong>, a key given as <code>undefined</code> removes that hook -\nthe cells follow the config again, the menus show their defaults. The visible cells are rendered\nagain once (as <a href=\"#api/GridInterface.refresh\">refresh</a> does); a menu uses its new function the next time it opens.</p>\n<p>The object passed in is not kept: the grid copies its keys.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>hooks</code> the hooks to set, or to remove with <code>undefined</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>// company can not be edited on an inactive row\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ isReadonly: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'company' &amp;&amp; !row.isActive ? true : null) });\n\n// color the balance cells, the readonly rule stays\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'balance' &amp;&amp; row.balance &lt; 0 ? { input: 'red' } : null) });\n\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ isReadonly: undefined }); // removed: the column config decides again\ngridInterface.updateHooks({ menus: undefined }); // the menus show their defaults</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"]}]}]},{"name":"CellClass","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CellClass"],"doc":"<p>The css classes the <code>cellClass</code> hook (<a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>) adds to a cell. Each is one or more class\nnames, separated by spaces, the same as a <code>class</code> attribute.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { CellClass } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst negative: CellClass = { input: 'negative-text', background: 'negative-background' };</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"background","signatures":["background?: string"],"doc":"<p>added to the element behind the input, which fills the cell. The input is transparent, so this\nis the cell&#39;s background - the grid draws the readonly and required stripes there. On an\neditable cell it has no size (the grid&#39;s readonly and required classes give it one): give the\nclass <code>position: absolute; inset: 0</code>. Was <code>dimmedClass</code> in v5</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"input","signatures":["input?: string"],"doc":"<p>added to the cell&#39;s <code>&lt;input&gt;</code>: the text. Was <code>inputClass</code> in v5</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CellRange","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CellRange"],"doc":"<p>A range of cells: the rectangle between two cells, both included. The user makes ranges with the\nmouse and the keyboard (see guides/17-selection-and-clipboard.md); <code>gridInterface.getRanges()</code> gives\nthem, <code>setRanges()</code> sets them.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Rows</strong> are indexes in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>), 0 based - the <code>row</code> of the\ngrid events. A group row in between is part of the rectangle, but it has no cells: copy, paste\nand clear skip it.</li>\n<li><strong>Fields</strong> are field names. The fields between them are the ones between them in the layout, in\nthe order of <code>gridInterface.getLayoutFields()</code>: pinned left, center, pinned right, and a column of\nstacked fields is a field each, top to bottom - the order of the CSV export and of\n<code>aria-colindex</code>.</li>\n<li><strong><code>from</code> is where the range starts</strong> (the anchor): the cell the mouse was pressed in, or the cell\nwith the focus when it was made with the keyboard. <strong><code>to</code> is the opposite corner</strong>, it can be\nabove or left of <code>from</code>. The last range&#39;s <code>from</code> is the active cell: where the focus is.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Plain JSON: it can be stored or sent. The indexes of the rows are only good for the rows as they\nare displayed now - the grid clears the ranges when the displayed rows change (filter, sort, group,\nexpand, collapse, rows added or removed) and when the layout changes.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { CellRange } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the first three rows, from the name to the age (and every field between them in the layout)\nconst range: CellRange = { fromRow: 0, fromField: 'name', toRow: 2, toField: 'age' };\ngridInterface.setRanges([range]);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"fromField","signatures":["fromField: string"],"doc":"<p>the field the range starts at</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fromRow","signatures":["fromRow: number"],"doc":"<p>the row the range starts at: an index in the displayed rows, 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"toField","signatures":["toField: string"],"doc":"<p>the field of the opposite corner, left of <code>fromField</code> too</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"toRow","signatures":["toRow: number"],"doc":"<p>the row of the opposite corner, above <code>fromRow</code> too</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Changes","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface Changes<T = Record<string, unknown>>"],"doc":"<p>What <code>datasource.getChanges()</code> returns: the rows added, edited and marked for deletion since the\ndata was set - what to send to a server.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>newEntities</code> - rows added with <code>addNewEmpty()</code>, edits to them included. A new row has a\ntemporary key, a generated negative number: in its key field (<code>id: -1</code>), or as <code>__KEY</code> when the\ndatasource has no key field. After the save, <code>acceptChanges({ newKeys })</code> gives the rows the\nserver&#39;s keys</li>\n<li><code>modifiedEntities</code> - one entry per edited row: its key and the changed fields, see\n<a href=\"#api/ModifiedEntity\">ModifiedEntity</a></li>\n<li><code>deletedEntities</code> - rows marked with <code>markForDeletion()</code> / <code>markAllForDeletion()</code>. A new row\nthat is marked for deletion is in none of the lists: it was never saved, there is nothing to send.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Every entry is a copy, a plain object: changing it does not change the row. It is a shallow copy -\na <code>Date</code> stays a <code>Date</code>, an object in a field is the row&#39;s own object.</p>\n<p>When an edit counts: a field is edited when its value differs from the original. A field set back\nto its original value is not edited any more. Setting a blank field (<code>null</code> / <code>undefined</code>) to <code>&#39;&#39;</code>\nis no edit. Two <code>Date</code>s are compared by the field&#39;s type in the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>date</code> - on the day. A date typed into a cell gets the current time of day, so typing the same\nday again is no edit.</li>\n<li><code>datetime</code>, and every other field - to the second, the milliseconds are ignored (they are not\nshown, and typing a time stamps the current ones). A time only change is an edit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    born: Date | null;\n    lastLogin: Date | null;\n}\ndeclare const rowsFromServer: Person[];\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id', fields: { born: 'date', lastLogin: 'datetime' } });\ndatasource.setData(rowsFromServer);\n// ... the user edits, adds and deletes rows in the grid\n\nconst { newEntities, modifiedEntities, deletedEntities } = datasource.getChanges();\nconst response = await fetch('/api/people', {\n    method: 'POST',\n    body: JSON.stringify({ newEntities, modifiedEntities, deletedEntities }) // a Date becomes its ISO text\n});\n\n// saved in one transaction: the server answers with the id it gave each new row\nconst saved: { temporaryId: number; id: number }[] = await response.json();\ndatasource.acceptChanges({ newKeys: new Map(saved.map((row) =&gt; [row.temporaryId, row.id])) });</code></pre>\n","samples":["editing"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"deletedEntities","signatures":["deletedEntities: T[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows marked for deletion, with the values they have now</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"modifiedEntities","signatures":["modifiedEntities: ModifiedEntity<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>one entry per edited row: its key and the fields that changed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"newEntities","signatures":["newEntities: (T & { __KEY?: string | number })[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows added with <code>addNewEmpty()</code> (or the container&#39;s <code>setData(rows, { add: true, isNew: true })</code>),\nwith the values they have now. Without a key field the temporary key is in <code>__KEY</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CreateGridOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CreateGridOptions<T>"],"doc":"<p>What <a href=\"#api/createGrid\">createGrid</a> needs: the config and the datasource, and the hooks if any.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type CreateGridOptions, createGrid, Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst options: CreateGridOptions&lt;{ name: string; locked: boolean }&gt; = {\n    config: { readonly: false, layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] } },\n    datasource: new Datasource&lt;{ name: string; locked: boolean }&gt;(),\n    hooks: { isReadonly: (row) =&gt; (row.locked ? true : null) }\n};\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, options);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"config","signatures":["config: GridConfig"],"doc":"<p>the columns, the layout and the options, see <a href=\"#api/GridConfig\">GridConfig</a>. Plain JSON</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datasource","signatures":["datasource: Datasource<T>"],"doc":"<p>the rows, see <a href=\"#api/Datasource\">Datasource</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hooks","signatures":["hooks?: GridHooks<T>"],"doc":"<p>optional: the functions - <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> and <code>menus</code>, see <a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>. Change\nthem later with <code>gridInterface.updateHooks()</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"CsvOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface CsvOptions"],"doc":"<p>What <code>gridInterface.getCsv()</code> and <code>gridInterface.downloadCsv()</code> export, and how. Every option is\noptional, and the object is plain JSON - it can be stored, or come from a menu of your own.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>option</th>\n<th>default</th>\n<th></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>rows</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;all&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;all&#39;</code>: every row the filter lets through, in the sort order. <code>&#39;selected&#39;</code>: the selected rows. <code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the rows of the selected range of cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>fields</code></td>\n<td>the layout (<code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the range&#39;s)</td>\n<td>the fields to export, in order</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code></td>\n<td>a first line with the column labels</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>formatted</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code></td>\n<td>the values as the grid shows them; <code>false</code> the values themselves</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>separator</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;,&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;;&#39;</code> for Excel in a locale with a decimal comma</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>bom</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code> for <code>downloadCsv()</code>, <code>false</code> for <code>getCsv()</code></td>\n<td>a UTF-8 byte order mark first</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>escapeFormulas</code></td>\n<td><code>true</code></td>\n<td>text that starts with <code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>@</code> ... gets a <code>&#39;</code> in front</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>An option with a value it does not know (<code>rows: &#39;some&#39;</code>, <code>separator: &#39;|&#39;</code>), or a key it does not\nknow, throws a <code>TypeError</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { CsvOptions } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// for Excel in Norway: a semicolon between the fields, and the BOM so it reads æøå\nconst forExcel: CsvOptions = { separator: ';', bom: true };\nconst text = gridInterface.getCsv(forExcel);\n\n// the selected rows, two fields, the values as they are stored\ngridInterface.downloadCsv('selected.csv', { rows: 'selected', fields: ['name', 'born'], formatted: false });\n\n// the cells the user selected (the last range), with a header line of their columns\ngridInterface.downloadCsv('range.csv', { rows: 'range' });</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"bom","signatures":["bom?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>Writes a UTF-8 byte order mark (<code>﻿</code>) first. Excel needs it to read the file as UTF-8,\nwithout it <code>æøå</code> show up garbled. Default <code>true</code> for <code>downloadCsv()</code>, <code>false</code> for <code>getCsv()</code> -\ntext for code of your own does not want it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"escapeFormulas","signatures":["escapeFormulas?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>Default <code>true</code>: text that starts with <code>=</code>, <code>+</code>, <code>-</code>, <code>@</code>, a tab, CR or LF (or the full width\n<code>＝ ＋ － ＠</code>) gets a <code>&#39;</code> in front, so a spreadsheet shows it as text and does not run it as a\nformula. A value a user typed, <code>=HYPERLINK(&quot;http://evil.example&quot;, &quot;click&quot;)</code>, would else run on\nthe computer of whoever opens the file - &quot;CSV injection&quot;,\n<a href=\"https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/CSV_Injection\">https://owasp.org/www-community/attacks/CSV_Injection</a>.</p>\n<p>Only text is escaped: a value that is text in the row (a string, or an object), and the labels.\nA number, a boolean, a <code>Date</code> and a blank never are, whatever their formatter writes - <code>-5</code>\nstays <code>-5</code>. The value decides, not the field&#39;s type: keep the numbers of a number field as\nnumbers, one holding the text <code>&#39;-5&#39;</code> is written as <code>&#39;-5</code>. Text that only looks like a formula\ngets the <code>&#39;</code> too: a phone number <code>+47 912 34 567</code> is written <code>&#39;+47 912 34 567</code>.</p>\n<p>The <code>&#39;</code> is part of the text in the file, a program that reads it gets it too. OWASP notes that\nthe escaping is not reliable in Excel once the file is saved and opened again, so treat a file\nof data users typed with care anyway.</p>\n<p><code>false</code> writes the text as it is: for a file that is read by a program, not opened in a\nspreadsheet.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields?: string[]"],"doc":"<p>The fields to export, in this order, a column each. Default the fields of the layout now, in\nthe order the user sees them: pinned left, center, pinned right, and a column of stacked fields\ngives a CSV column for each of its fields, top to bottom - <code>gridInterface.getLayoutFields()</code>.\nThe hidden columns (<code>getHiddenFields()</code>) are not in the layout, so they are left out. With\n<code>rows: &#39;range&#39;</code> the default is the fields of the range.</p>\n<p>Any field of the rows can be given, also one that is not in the grid.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"formatted","signatures":["formatted?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>Default <code>true</code>: each value as the grid shows it, the text of the field&#39;s formatter - <code>12,5</code> with\nthe <code>numberComma</code> formatter, a date as <code>2026-11-20</code> (or as its formatter writes it), a boolean\nas <code>true</code> / <code>false</code>. A column&#39;s <code>numberOverride</code> (<code>ZERO_TO_BLANK</code>, <code>BLANK_TO_ZERO</code>) and\n<code>dynamicCellTypeColumn</code> are followed, as in the cells.</p>\n<p><code>false</code>: the values as they are stored - a number with a dot (<code>String(12.5)</code>), a <code>Date</code> as\n<code>toISOString()</code> (UTC: a date at midnight in Norway is the day before at 23:00 or 22:00), a\nboolean as <code>true</code> / <code>false</code>, a blank (null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>, an invalid Date) as nothing.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"header","signatures":["header?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>A first line with the label of each column, default <code>true</code>: the label the grid&#39;s header shows -\nthe column&#39;s <code>label</code>, else the datasource field&#39;s <code>label</code>, else the field name prettified\n(<code>first_name</code> is <code>First Name</code>).</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rows","signatures":["rows?: \"all\" | \"selected\" | \"range\""],"doc":"<p>Which rows, default <code>&#39;all&#39;</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;all&#39;</code>: every row the filter lets through, in the sort order - <code>datasource.getDataRows()</code>.\nWhen grouped, every data row in the grouped order, the rows of collapsed groups included; no\ngroup rows</li>\n<li><code>&#39;selected&#39;</code>: the selected rows, in the same order - <code>datasource.getSelectedRows()</code>. That is\nthe selected rows that are displayed: a selected row in a collapsed group is left out, as the\nrow menu&#39;s actions on the selected rows leave it out. Nothing selected gives the header only</li>\n<li><code>&#39;range&#39;</code>: the selected range of cells - the last of <code>gridInterface.getRanges()</code>, the one made\nlast: its data rows top to bottom (a group row in it is left out) and, unless <code>fields</code> is\ngiven, its fields left to right. No range gives an empty text (no fields, no rows)</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"separator","signatures":["separator?: CsvSeparator"],"doc":"<p>Between the fields, default <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> (RFC 4180). Excel uses the list separator of the computer&#39;s\nlocale when it opens a .csv file: in a locale with a decimal comma (Norwegian, German ...) that\nis <code>&#39;;&#39;</code>, and a file with <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> opens with every row in one column. Use <code>&#39;;&#39;</code> for those users.\n<code>&#39;\\t&#39;</code> gives tab separated text.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DataEntity","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DataEntity extends Entity"],"doc":"<p>A row of data, not a group row: the DataContainer wraps every one of them in an EntityHandler\nproxy, so it always has its controller. An <a href=\"#api/Entity\">Entity</a> with <code>__controller</code> set.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DataEntity } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst isEdited = (row: DataEntity) =&gt; row.__controller.__edited === true;</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"__controller","signatures":["__controller: EntityHandler"],"doc":"<p>the object that tracks the row&#39;s edits: its original values, <code>__isNew</code>, <code>__isDeleted</code>,\n<code>__edited</code>. Read it, do not change it - see <a href=\"#api/EntityHandler\">EntityHandler</a></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DatasourceEvents","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DatasourceEvents"],"doc":"<p>The events of a <a href=\"#api/Datasource\">Datasource</a>: event name -&gt; the payload its handler gets.</p>\n<p>Subscribe with <code>datasource.on(name, handler)</code>, the payload is typed from this map.\n<code>on()</code> returns a function that unsubscribes. Events with nothing to tell send an empty object.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const off = datasource.on('collection-filtered', (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log(data.info, datasource.getDataRows().length, 'rows left');\n});\ndatasource.on('selection-change', () =&gt; {\n    console.log(datasource.getSelectedRows().length, 'rows selected');\n});\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":["events"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"collection-changed","signatures":["'collection-changed': { added?: boolean; data?: Entity | Entity[] | null; info?: \"removeData\" | \"clearMarkedForDeletion\" | \"upsert\"; removed?: true }"],"doc":"<p>Rows were added, replaced or removed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>setData()</code>: <code>{ added }</code> - <code>true</code> when rows were added, <code>false</code> when they replaced the data</li>\n<li><code>addNewEmpty()</code>: <code>{ added: true }</code></li>\n<li><code>removeData()</code>: <code>{ removed: true, info: &#39;removeData&#39;, data }</code> - <code>data</code> is what was passed in</li>\n<li><code>removeAllData()</code>: <code>{ removed: true, info: &#39;removeData&#39;, data: null }</code></li>\n<li><code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>: <code>{ removed: true, info: &#39;clearMarkedForDeletion&#39; }</code></li>\n<li><code>upsert()</code>: <code>{ info: &#39;upsert&#39;, added }</code>, with <code>removed: true</code> when it removed rows. Only when it\nadded or removed rows, or the displayed rows changed (the filter, the sort order or the groups).\nAn upsert that only changed values sends none: <code>rows-changed</code> has the rows</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-collapse","signatures":["'collection-collapse': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>collapseGroup()</code> collapsed one or all groups. Empty payload.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-expand","signatures":["'collection-expand': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>expandGroup()</code> expanded one or all groups. Empty payload.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-filtered","signatures":["'collection-filtered': { info: \"markForDeletion\" | \"unmarkForDeletion\" | \"acceptChanges\" | \"filter\" | \"resetData\" | \"__internalUpdate, forced\" }"],"doc":"<p>The displayed rows were rebuilt. <code>info</code> says by what:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;filter&#39;</code>: <code>filter()</code> or <code>reloadDatasource()</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;resetData&#39;</code>: <code>resetData()</code> or <code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;markForDeletion&#39;</code>: <code>markForDeletion()</code> or <code>markAllForDeletion()</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;unmarkForDeletion&#39;</code>: <code>unmarkForDeletion()</code> or <code>unmarkAllForDeletion()</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;acceptChanges&#39;</code>: <code>acceptChanges()</code> - also when it removed rows, it sends no <code>collection-changed</code></li>\n<li><code>&#39;__internalUpdate, forced&#39;</code>: <code>setData(rows, { refilter: false })</code> or <code>addNewEmpty()</code> while\nthere is no filter, sorting or grouping. Sent before their <code>collection-changed</code>. A <code>setData()</code>\nthat runs the filter (the default) sends only <code>collection-changed</code>.</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-grouped","signatures":["'collection-grouped': { groupings?: GroupArgument[]; info: \"group\" | \"removeGroup\" }"],"doc":"<p>The grouping changed.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>group()</code>: <code>{ info: &#39;group&#39;, groupings }</code> - the grouping now applied</li>\n<li><code>removeGroup()</code>: <code>{ info: &#39;removeGroup&#39; }</code>, after the <code>&#39;group&#39;</code> event of the grouping that is left</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"collection-sorted","signatures":["'collection-sorted': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>sort()</code> ran. Empty payload.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"conflicts-changed","signatures":["'conflicts-changed': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p>The conflicts changed: <code>upsert()</code> made one, or one went - resolved with <code>resolveConflict()</code>, the\nfield is not edited any more, the row was saved (<code>acceptChanges()</code>), reset, or left the data.\nSent once the code that changed them is done (in a microtask), after <code>rows-changed</code>. Empty\npayload, read <code>datasource.getConflicts()</code>.</p>\n<p>The conflicts are the data container&#39;s: every datasource on the same <code>DataContainer</code> sends it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"current-entity","signatures":["'current-entity': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p><code>datasource.currentEntity</code> was set: a row was clicked or selected, or\n<code>setRowAsCurrentEntity()</code> was called. Also when <code>setData()</code> set it to <code>null</code> because the current\nrow is no longer in the data, and when a method that removes rows removed it (<code>removeData()</code>,\n<code>removeAllData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>, <code>acceptChanges()</code>, <code>resetData()</code>,\n<code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code>) - sent after their own event. Empty payload, read\n<code>datasource.currentEntity</code>.\nWas <code>currentEntity</code> in v5.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"history-changed","signatures":["'history-changed': { info: \"edit\" | \"undo\" | \"redo\" | \"clear\" | \"remove\" }"],"doc":"<p>The undo/redo history changed: read <code>canUndo()</code> and <code>canRedo()</code>, e.g. to enable Undo and Redo\nbuttons of your own. <code>info</code> says what changed it:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;edit&#39;</code>: a step was recorded - an edit, a paste, a clear, a (un)mark for deletion, a revert.\nSent once the code that made it is done (in a microtask): one event per step, also for a paste\nover many rows. Also when what the user typed in a cell went back to the value it started from,\nand its step was dropped</li>\n<li><code>&#39;undo&#39;</code>: <code>undo()</code> took a step back. The grid renders its cells again</li>\n<li><code>&#39;redo&#39;</code>: <code>redo()</code> did a step again. The grid renders its cells again</li>\n<li><code>&#39;clear&#39;</code>: the history was emptied - <code>clearHistory()</code>, <code>setData()</code> without <code>add</code>,\n<code>removeAllData()</code>, <code>resetData()</code>, <code>acceptChanges()</code>. Only when there was something in it</li>\n<li><code>&#39;remove&#39;</code>: rows were removed for good (<code>removeData()</code>, <code>clearMarkedForDeletion()</code>, a new row\nremoved by <code>resetDataSelectionOnly()</code>, <code>upsert(rows, { removeMissing: true })</code>) and their changes\nleft the history. Or <code>upsert()</code> gave fields the server&#39;s value as their original, and a change\nthat does nothing now was dropped (see <code>upsert()</code>)</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The history is the data container&#39;s: every datasource on the same container sends it, for a\nchange made through any of them.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rows-changed","signatures":["'rows-changed': { fields: ReadonlyMap<Entity, ReadonlySet<string>>; rows: Entity[] }"],"doc":"<p>Values of rows changed, or what the grid shows of them: sent once the code that changed them is\ndone (in a microtask) - one event however many rows and fields it set. The grid renders the rows\nof it that are on screen, in the next animation frame: a value set from code shows without\n<code>gridInterface.refresh()</code>.</p>\n<p>A row is in it when:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>a field was set on it: from code (<code>row.price = 10</code>), by the user in the grid, by <code>undo()</code> /\n<code>redo()</code>, <code>resetField()</code>, <code>resetRows()</code>, <code>resetData()</code>, <code>resolveConflict()</code>, or by <code>upsert()</code></li>\n<li>its deletion mark changed (<code>markForDeletion()</code>, undo ...) or its server error (<code>setErrors()</code>)</li>\n<li>one of its conflicts came or went</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The rows <code>upsert()</code> or <code>setData()</code> added and the rows removed are not in it: <code>collection-changed</code>\ntells those. A row in it can have left the data since it changed.</p>\n<p>The rows are the data container&#39;s: every datasource on the same <code>DataContainer</code> sends it, for a\nchange made through any of them.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"select","signatures":["select: { info: \"select-first\" | \"select-prev\" | \"select-next\" | \"select-last\"; row: number }"],"doc":"<p>A row was selected from code, the grid scrolls it into view.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code>: index in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>), 0 based</li>\n<li><code>info</code>: what selected it - <code>select(row, { notify: true })</code> sends <code>&#39;select-first&#39;</code>, <code>selectFirst()</code>\n<code>&#39;select-first&#39;</code>, <code>selectPrev()</code> <code>&#39;select-prev&#39;</code>, <code>selectNext()</code> <code>&#39;select-next&#39;</code>,\n<code>selectLast()</code> <code>&#39;select-last&#39;</code></li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selection-change","signatures":["'selection-change': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p>The selected rows changed. Also when a method that removes rows removed a selected one (see\n<code>current-entity</code>), sent after its own event. Empty payload, read <code>datasource.getSelectedRows()</code>.\nWas <code>selectionChange</code> in v5.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate: { errors: ValidationError<unknown>[] }"],"doc":"<p><code>datasource.validate()</code> ran: <code>errors</code> is what it returned. The grid renders its rows again, to\nshow the errors. An edit sends no event, though it is validated: read <code>getErrors()</code> when you\nneed them.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DatasourceOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DatasourceOptions"],"doc":"<p>Options for <code>new Datasource(options)</code>. All of them are optional, <code>new Datasource()</code> works.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>key</code> - the field that identifies a row. Selection follows the key, so it survives replacing\nthe data with fresh rows from the server, and <code>upsert()</code> merges rows from a server by it.</li>\n<li><code>fields</code> - the schema: the type, label and formatter of each field. A field that is not listed\nis <code>&#39;text&#39;</code>, labelled with its name. Sorting, grouping, filtering and the grid all read the\ntype from here. See <a href=\"#api/FieldConfig\">FieldConfig</a> and <a href=\"#api/FieldType\">FieldType</a>.</li>\n<li><code>formatters</code> - the default formatter per type, for the fields without a formatter of their own.\nThe types left out keep the built-in default (see <a href=\"#api/FieldType\">FieldType</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>A formatter is named by its id, a built-in one or one registered with <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>:\n<code>fields</code> and <code>formatters</code> are plain JSON, they can be stored (in a backend, say) and given back\nas they are. An id that is not registered throws when the datasource is made.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>selectionMode</code> - <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code> (default), <code>&#39;single&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;none&#39;</code>. A grid showing the datasource\nuses it, change it later with <code>setSelectionMode()</code>.</li>\n<li><code>container</code> - share the data with another datasource, each with its own filter, sort, grouping\nand selection. Rows added or removed through one show in the other after its\n<code>reloadDatasource()</code> (or a <code>filter()</code>) - they are not kept in sync on their own. Give the key to the container\n(<code>new DataContainer(&#39;id&#39;)</code>); a <code>key</code> that is not the container&#39;s throws. The edits are tracked\nby the container, with the field types of every datasource on it (a <code>date</code> field compares on\nthe day): a field listed by two of them must have the same type in both, the second datasource\nthrows if not. A field listed by one only has that one&#39;s type.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DataContainer, Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    key: 'id',\n    fields: {\n        id: 'number',\n        name: { label: 'Name' },\n        born: { type: 'date', label: 'Born' },\n        salary: { type: 'number', formatter: 'numberComma' },\n        active: 'boolean'\n    },\n    formatters: {\n        date: 'dateDDMMYYYY' // every date field without a formatter of its own\n    },\n    selectionMode: 'single'\n});\n\n// a second datasource on the same rows\nconst container = new DataContainer('id');\nconst left = new Datasource({ container, fields: { born: 'date' } });\nconst right = new Datasource({ container, fields: { born: 'date' } });</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"container","signatures":["container?: DataContainer"],"doc":"<p>the data container to use, to share the rows with another datasource. Default a new one.\nA field in <code>fields</code> must have the same type as in the other datasources on the container.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields?: Record<string, FieldType | FieldConfig>"],"doc":"<p>the fields: <code>{ born: &#39;date&#39;, age: { type: &#39;number&#39;, label: &#39;Age&#39; } }</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"formatters","signatures":["formatters?: Partial<Record<FieldType, string>>"],"doc":"<p>the id of the default formatter for each type, used by the fields that have no formatter of\ntheir own: <code>{ number: &#39;numberComma&#39;, date: &#39;dateDDMMYYYY&#39; }</code>. See <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a> for\nthe ids</p>\n","samples":["formatters"]},{"name":"key","signatures":["key?: string"],"doc":"<p>the field that identifies a row, e.g. <code>&#39;id&#39;</code>. Rows without it get a generated key. <code>upsert()</code>\nneeds it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selectionMode","signatures":["selectionMode?: SelectionMode"],"doc":"<p>how rows can be selected, default <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code>. A grid showing the datasource uses it</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"DateEvents","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface DateEvents"],"doc":"<p>The events of a <a href=\"#api/DateInterface\">DateInterface</a>: event name -&gt; the payload its handler gets.</p>\n<p>Subscribe with <code>dateInterface.on(name, handler)</code>, the payload is typed from this map.\n<code>on()</code> returns a function that unsubscribes. Removing the date element from the dom\nunsubscribes every handler.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { DateInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const dateInterface: DateInterface;\n\nconst off = dateInterface.on('date-select', (date) =&gt; {\n    console.log(date ? date.toISOString() : 'cleared');\n});\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"date-select","signatures":["'date-select': Date | null"],"doc":"<p>A date was picked in the date picker (<code>datepicker: true</code>): the &quot;Use&quot; button sends the\npicked date and time, the &quot;Clear&quot; button sends <code>null</code>. Clicking a day only picks it, &quot;Now&quot; goes\nto the current date and time; neither sends the event. A calendar (<code>datepicker: false</code>) never\nsends it - read <code>dateInterface.getSelected()</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Entity","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface Entity"],"doc":"<p>A data row: one of your objects, as the datasource hands it out. Group header rows are not\nentities, see <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a>.</p>\n<p>The row is your object wrapped in a <code>Proxy</code>. Your own fields are read and set as usual, setting one\nis an edit (<code>datasource.getChanges()</code>). The <code>__</code> fields below are not stored on your object: the\nproxy answers them, so <code>Object.keys(row)</code> and <code>JSON.stringify(row)</code> show your fields only.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const row = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nrow.name = 'Anna'; // an edit\nrow.__rowState; // 'M'\nrow.__KEY; // the key, e.g. the row's id</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"__controller","signatures":["__controller?: EntityHandler"],"doc":"<p>the object that tracks the row&#39;s edits: its original values, <code>__isNew</code>, <code>__isDeleted</code>,\n<code>__edited</code>. Read it, do not change it - see <a href=\"#api/EntityHandler\">EntityHandler</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__group","signatures":["__group?: undefined"],"doc":"<p>A data row never has <code>__group</code>, only a <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> has it (<code>true</code>). Declared so the two\ntypes stay apart: a group row can not be passed where an entity is expected, and\n<code>row.__group</code> tells them apart. <a href=\"#api/isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a> is the readable way to check.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupLvl","signatures":["__groupLvl?: number"],"doc":"<p>Written by grouping: how many group levels the row sits under. Do not rely on it - it is not\nset on every row (with one grouping level only the first row of each group gets it) and not\ncleared when the grouping is removed. The grid shows nothing from it on a data row.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__KEY","signatures":["__KEY?: string | number"],"doc":"<p>the row&#39;s key: the value of the key field (<code>new Datasource({ key: &#39;id&#39; })</code>), which reading and\nsetting <code>__KEY</code> go to. Without a key field a generated negative number. The selection and\n<code>setErrors()</code> use it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__rowError","signatures":["__rowError?: string | null"],"doc":"<p>an error message for the row from a server, set with <code>datasource.getDataContainer().setErrors()</code>.\n<code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> for no error. Apart from the validation errors (<code>datasource.getErrors()</code>).\nThe grid shows it on the row selector, with the validation errors: the error class, and the\nmessage as the tooltip</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__rowState","signatures":["__rowState?: string"],"doc":"<p>the row&#39;s state: <code>&#39;N&#39;</code> new (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>), <code>&#39;D&#39;</code> marked for deletion (a new row too), <code>&#39;M&#39;</code>\nedited - a field differs from its original value. <code>undefined</code> for a row as it was set, or as\n<code>acceptChanges()</code> left it. Read only, setting it does nothing</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"EntityHandler","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface EntityHandler"],"doc":"<p>The <code>Proxy</code> handler every row is wrapped in: it keeps the row&#39;s original values and tracks which\nfields were edited, whether the row is new or marked for deletion, and answers the row&#39;s <code>__</code> fields\n(<code>__KEY</code>, <code>__rowState</code> ...). The data container makes one per row.</p>\n<p>Exported as a type only: it is the type of <code>Entity.__controller</code>. Read its fields, do not change them -\nuse the datasource&#39;s methods (<code>markForDeletion()</code>, <code>resetData()</code> ...).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const row = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nrow.name = 'Anna';\nrow.__controller?.__edited; // true\nrow.__controller?.__originalValues.name; // the name before the edit</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"__controller","signatures":["__controller?: EntityHandler"],"doc":"<p>not used: reading <code>row.__controller</code> gives the handler itself</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__currentValues","signatures":["__currentValues: Record<string, any>"],"doc":"<p>the value last set, per field that was set</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__edited","signatures":["__edited?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> while a field differs from its original value</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__editedProps","signatures":["__editedProps: Record<string, boolean>"],"doc":"<p>per property set on the row: <code>true</code> while its value differs from the original, <code>false</code> once\nit was set back to it. <code>getChanges()</code> reports the <code>true</code> ones</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__group","signatures":["__group?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row, it is never a group row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupChildren","signatures":["__groupChildren?: Entity[]"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupExpanded","signatures":["__groupExpanded?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupID","signatures":["__groupID?: string"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupLvl","signatures":["__groupLvl?: number"],"doc":"<p>the grouping level the row sits under, read as <code>row.__groupLvl</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupName","signatures":["__groupName?: string"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupTotal","signatures":["__groupTotal?: number"],"doc":"<p>not used on a data row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__isDeleted","signatures":["__isDeleted?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> while the row is marked for deletion, see <code>markForDeletion()</code> / <code>unmarkForDeletion()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__isNew","signatures":["__isNew?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> for a new row: <code>addNewEmpty()</code>, or the container&#39;s <code>setData(rows, { isNew: true })</code>. Until\n<code>acceptChanges()</code> makes it an ordinary row. Stays <code>true</code> while a new row is marked for deletion</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__KEY","signatures":["__KEY?: string | number"],"doc":"<p>the row&#39;s generated key, when the container has no key field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__KEYSTRING","signatures":["__KEYSTRING?: string | number"],"doc":"<p>the container&#39;s key field, <code>undefined</code> when there is none</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__newprops","signatures":["__newprops: Record<string, any>"],"doc":"<p>the fields set on the row since it was made (or its changes were accepted), <code>true</code> each</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__originalValues","signatures":["__originalValues: Record<string, any>"],"doc":"<p>the value each field had before its first edit, per field that was set</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__rowError","signatures":["__rowError?: string | null"],"doc":"<p>the row&#39;s error, read as <code>row.__rowError</code>, see <code>DataContainer.setErrors()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__rowState","signatures":["__rowState?: string"],"doc":"<p>not used: <code>row.__rowState</code> is computed from <code>__isNew</code>, <code>__isDeleted</code> and <code>__edited</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"get","signatures":["get(target: any, prop: string): any"],"doc":"<p>The proxy&#39;s get trap, called by the <code>Proxy</code> when a field of the row is read. Not for calling\nyourself.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"set","signatures":["set(obj: any, prop: string, value: any, receiver: Entity): boolean"],"doc":"<p>The proxy&#39;s set trap, called by the <code>Proxy</code> when a field of the row is set: it records the edit,\nand the container records it for undo and validates the field. Not for calling yourself.</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Field","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface Field"],"doc":"<p>A field as the datasource resolved it: every default filled in. Returned by <code>datasource.getField()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const { type, label, formatter, validate } = datasource.getField('born');\nformatter.format(new Date(2026, 10, 20)); // '2026-11-20' for a date field with the default formatter\nconst required = validate.some((rule) =&gt; rule.id === 'required');</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"formatter","signatures":["formatter: Formatter"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s own formatter, else the datasource&#39;s default for its type</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the label from <code>fields</code>, else the field name</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"multiline","signatures":["multiline: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when <code>fields</code> gave the field <code>multiline: true</code>. The grid also shows a value with a line\nbreak as multiline text, in any text field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"name","signatures":["name: string"],"doc":"<p>the field name, the property on the row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: FieldType"],"doc":"<p>the type from <code>fields</code>, <code>&#39;text&#39;</code> when the field is not listed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate: readonly ValidationRuleObject[]"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s validation rules, each written out as an object: <code>&#39;required&#39;</code> is <code>{ id: &#39;required&#39; }</code>.\n<code>[]</code> when the field has none. The datasource&#39;s own list, do not change it</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FieldConfig","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FieldConfig"],"doc":"<p>How one field of the datasource is described in <code>DatasourceOptions.fields</code>. All of it is\noptional, and writing just the type (<code>born: &#39;date&#39;</code>) is the same as <code>born: { type: &#39;date&#39; }</code>.</p>\n<p>It is plain JSON: the formatter and the validators are named by their ids (see\n<a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a> and <a href=\"#api/registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>), so the fields can be stored, e.g. in a\nbackend.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: {\n        born: 'date',\n        age: { type: 'number', label: 'Age (years)', validate: ['required', { id: 'min', value: 0 }] },\n        price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'numberComma' }, // a built-in formatter, by its id\n        company: { label: 'Company name', validate: ['required'] }, // a text field with a label\n        notes: { label: 'Notes', multiline: true } // a text of several lines\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-formatter","validation"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"formatter","signatures":["formatter?: string"],"doc":"<p>the id of the field&#39;s formatter: a built-in one (<code>&#39;numberComma&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;dateDDMMYYYY&#39;</code> ...) or one\nregistered with <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>. Default the datasource&#39;s formatter for the field&#39;s\ntype (see <code>DatasourceOptions.formatters</code>). An id that is not registered throws when the\ndatasource is made</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label?: string"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s name for people, default the field name. The grid&#39;s column label falls back to it\nwhen the column has no <code>label</code> of its own, and <code>getFilterString()</code> / <code>getFilterTree()</code> use it.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"multiline","signatures":["multiline?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>a text of several lines: notes, an address. The grid shows the first line of the cell, with a\nmarker when there is more, and the whole text in its tooltip. Enter, F2, a double click or\ntyping opens an editor over the cell, a bigger textarea: Ctrl+Enter saves, Esc cancels. See the\nediting guide.</p>\n<p>A text cell whose value has a line break is shown and edited like this without the option too:\nthe input of a cell can not hold a line break (the browser strips them). The option is for a\nfield of several lines whose values have none yet. Text fields only: <code>true</code> on another type\nthrows when the datasource is made. Default <code>false</code></p>\n","samples":["multiline"]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type?: FieldType"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s type, default <code>&#39;text&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"validate","signatures":["validate?: ValidationRule[]"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s validation rules, checked when the field is edited and by <code>datasource.validate()</code>:\nthe id of a validator (<code>&#39;required&#39;</code>), or the id with options and a message\n(<code>{ id: &#39;min&#39;, value: 0, message: &#39;at least {value}&#39; }</code>), see <a href=\"#api/ValidationRule\">ValidationRule</a>. The\nbuilt-ins are <code>required</code>, <code>min</code>, <code>max</code>, <code>minLength</code>, <code>maxLength</code> and <code>pattern</code>, register your\nown with <a href=\"#api/registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>. An id that is not registered throws when the datasource is\nmade. A field with <code>&#39;required&#39;</code> gets the grid&#39;s required stripes while it is empty.</p>\n","samples":["validation"]}]}]},{"name":"FilterCondition","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FilterCondition"],"doc":"<p>One test on one field: <code>field</code> <code>operator</code> <code>value</code>. The field&#39;s type comes from the datasource&#39;s\n<code>fields</code> (<code>&#39;text&#39;</code> when it is not listed), the condition has none of its own.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code> - the property on the row</li>\n<li><code>operator</code> - how to compare, see <a href=\"#api/FilterOperator\">FilterOperator</a></li>\n<li><code>value</code> - what to compare with. Left out for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>, an array for <code>IN</code> /\n<code>NOT_IN</code>, a <code>Date</code> for date fields. A number value compares as a number and a <code>Date</code> as a date,\nalso on a field that is not listed</li>\n<li><code>valueField</code> - compare with another field of the same row instead of <code>value</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>A condition without <code>field</code> or <code>operator</code>, and a date condition without the value it needs, is\nignored: it does not filter out anything.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#api/where\">where</a> builds one. A <code>valueField</code> condition is written out:</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nwhere('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18); // { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: 18 }\n\n// rows changed after they were approved\ndatasource.filter({ field: 'changed', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', valueField: 'approved' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field to test, the property on the row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator: FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>how to compare, see <a href=\"#api/FilterOperator\">FilterOperator</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value?: unknown"],"doc":"<p>what to compare with, not used by <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code> or when <code>valueField</code> is set</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"valueField","signatures":["valueField?: string"],"doc":"<p>the name of another field: the row&#39;s value of that field is what is compared with</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FilterConditionNode","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FilterConditionNode"],"doc":"<p>One condition of <a href=\"#api/FilterGroupNode\">FilterGroupNode</a>, ready to show: the field&#39;s label and the value as text.\nPart of what <code>getFilterTree()</code> returns.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { FilterConditionNode } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst describe = (node: FilterConditionNode) =&gt; (node.hasValue ? `${node.label} ${node.operator} ${node.value}` : `${node.label} ${node.operator}`);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"hasValue","signatures":["hasValue: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>, they take no value</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"kind","signatures":["kind: \"condition\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;condition&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the field&#39;s label, or what the <code>label</code> function given to <code>getFilterTree()</code> returns</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator: string"],"doc":"<p>the operator&#39;s name, e.g. <code>&#39;EQUAL&#39;</code>, see <a href=\"#api/FilterOperator\">FilterOperator</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value: string"],"doc":"<p>the value as text: formatted with the field&#39;s formatter, the values of <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> joined by\n<code>&#39;, &#39;</code>, a <code>valueField</code> as <code>[label]</code>. <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FilterGroup","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FilterGroup"],"doc":"<p>Conditions and groups joined by AND (every child must match) or OR (one is enough). Groups nest,\nso any mix of AND and OR can be written. A group without children is ignored.</p>\n<p><a href=\"#api/and\">and</a> and <a href=\"#api/or\">or</a> build one.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, type FilterGroup, or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// age &gt;= 18 AND (country = 'Norway' OR country = 'Sweden')\nconst filter: FilterGroup = {\n    group: 'AND',\n    children: [\n        { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO', value: 18 },\n        {\n            group: 'OR',\n            children: [\n                { field: 'country', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'Norway' },\n                { field: 'country', operator: 'EQUAL', value: 'Sweden' }\n            ]\n        }\n    ]\n};\n// the same, with the builders\nand(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO', 18), or(where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'), where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Sweden')));</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"children","signatures":["children: FilterExpression[]"],"doc":"<p>the conditions and groups in the group</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"group","signatures":["group: \"AND\" | \"OR\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;AND&#39;</code>: every child must match, <code>&#39;OR&#39;</code>: one is enough</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"FilterGroupNode","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface FilterGroupNode"],"doc":"<p>A group of filter nodes joined by one logical operator, as <code>getFilterTree()</code> returns it. It keeps the\nnesting of the filter, so the grouping can be shown, not flattened away - the grid&#39;s footer draws\nthese as bracketed chips.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { FilterNode } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// the filter as text: (age GREATER_THAN 18 AND (country EQUAL Norway OR country EQUAL Sweden))\nconst toText = (node: FilterNode): string =&gt;\n    node.kind === 'group'\n        ? `(${node.children.map(toText).join(` ${node.logicalOperator} `)})`\n        : `${node.label} ${node.operator} ${node.value}`;\n\nconst tree = datasource.getFilterTree();\nconst text = tree ? toText(tree) : 'no filter';</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"children","signatures":["children: FilterNode[]"],"doc":"<p>the conditions and groups in it. The conditions the filter ignores are left out</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"kind","signatures":["kind: \"group\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;group&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"logicalOperator","signatures":["logicalOperator: \"AND\" | \"OR\""],"doc":"<p>how the children are joined: <code>&#39;AND&#39;</code>, or <code>&#39;OR&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Formatter","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface Formatter"],"doc":"<p>Turns the values of a field into text and back. Every field has one: its own (<code>FieldConfig.formatter</code>),\nor the datasource&#39;s default for the field&#39;s type (<code>DatasourceOptions.formatters</code>). The options name\na formatter by its id: register yours with <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>, the built-in ones are\nregistered from the start.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> is used for everything shown as text: the cells, the edit and filter inputs, the group\nheaders, the footer&#39;s filter and <code>getFilterString()</code>. Booleans are the exception, the grid&#39;s\ncheckbox shows the raw value. The header filter&#39;s value list (text fields only) shows the raw\nvalues, in upper case.</li>\n<li><code>parse</code> turns what the user typed or pasted into the value stored in the row.</li>\n<li><code>parseFilter</code> turns what the user typed into a filter input into the value filtered on. Left out,\n<code>parse</code> is used.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The grid always calls <code>parse</code> and <code>parseFilter</code> with text. The built-in formatters are plain\nobjects, so a variant is a spread away: <code>{ ...NumberFormatterDot, format: (value) =&gt; ... }</code>.\nDo not use <code>this</code> in a formatter&#39;s methods, the datasource may call them detached.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type Formatter, registerFormatter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// money with two decimals and a space between the thousands: 12345.6 -&gt; '12 345.60'\nconst money: Formatter = {\n    format: (value) =&gt; (typeof value === 'number' ? value.toFixed(2).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ' ') : ''),\n    parse: (text) =&gt; (text.trim() === '' ? null : Number(text.replaceAll(' ', ''))),\n    placeholder: '0.00'\n};\nregisterFormatter('money', money);\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: {\n        price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'money' }\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-formatter","formatters"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"placeholder","signatures":["placeholder?: string"],"doc":"<p>Optional: shown in an empty header filter input when the column has no <code>placeholderFilter</code>,\ne.g. <code>&#39;YYYY-MM-DD&#39;</code>.</p>\n","samples":[]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"format","signatures":["format(value: unknown): string"],"doc":"<p>A value of the field as text. Give <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for a blank value (null, undefined).</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>value</code> the value in the row, can be anything the row holds</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"parse","signatures":["parse(text: string): unknown"],"doc":"<p>Text the user typed or pasted into a cell, as the value to store in the row.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>text</code> what the user typed</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"parseFilter","signatures":["parseFilter?(text: string): unknown"],"doc":"<p>Optional: text typed into a filter input, as the value to filter on. Left out, <code>parse</code> is used.\nThe built-in date formatters use it to make a filter boundary start at 00:00:00, where <code>parse</code>\nkeeps the current time of day.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>text</code> what the user typed</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridCellEventData","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>The cell a grid event happened on. Most <a href=\"#api/GridEvents\">GridEvents</a> send this, some with more fields.\n<code>cell-header-focus</code> sends it with a different <code>rowData</code>, see there.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { EventHandler, GridCellEventData } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst logCell: EventHandler&lt;GridCellEventData&gt; = (data) =&gt; console.log(data.attribute, data.row, data.rowData);\ngridInterface.on('copy-cell', logCell);\ngridInterface.on('clear', logCell);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"attribute","signatures":["attribute: string"],"doc":"<p>the attribute (field) of the cell</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell","signatures":["cell: HTMLCellElement"],"doc":"<p>the cell element</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cellType","signatures":["cellType: string"],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;row-cell&#39;</code> for a data cell, <code>&#39;filter&#39;</code> for a header filter cell</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"celno","signatures":["celno: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the cell in the column, a column can have more than one row of cells. 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"colType","signatures":["colType: ColType"],"doc":"<p>the section of the grid the cell is in</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"column","signatures":["column: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the column in its section (<code>colType</code>), 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the row in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>), 0 based. 0 for header cells</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowData","signatures":["rowData: Entity"],"doc":"<p>the data row of the cell. Never a group row, a group row has no cells</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridEvents","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridEvents"],"doc":"<p>The events of a <a href=\"#api/GridInterface\">GridInterface</a>: event name -&gt; the payload its handler gets.\nThe datasource has its own events, see <a href=\"#api/DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a>.</p>\n<p>Subscribe with <code>gridInterface.on(name, handler)</code>, the payload is typed from this map.\n<code>on()</code> returns a function that unsubscribes.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>const off = gridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log('clicked', data.attribute, 'in row', data.row, data.rowData);\n});\ngridInterface.on('grid-connected', () =&gt; {\n    gridInterface.autoResizeColumns();\n});\noff(); // unsubscribe</code></pre>\n","samples":["events"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"cell-click","signatures":["'cell-click': GridCellEventData & { originalEvent: MouseEvent }"],"doc":"<p>A data cell was clicked. Sent in a <code>setTimeout</code> after the click, so the row is already the\ncurrent entity. <code>originalEvent</code> is the click. Not sent for a boolean (checkbox) cell.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell-focus-button-click","signatures":["'cell-focus-button-click': GridCellEventData & { originalEvent: FocusEvent | KeyboardEvent; target: HTMLElement }"],"doc":"<p>The focus button of a cell was clicked, or Space pressed in the cell. The button is shown\nby <code>focusButton</code> on the column (<code>ColumnConfig.focusButton</code>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>target</code>: the cell&#39;s input, focus it to give the focus back to the cell</li>\n<li><code>originalEvent</code>: the focus event of the cell (button clicked) or the keydown (Space)</li>\n</ul>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell-header-focus","signatures":["'cell-header-focus': Omit<GridCellEventData, \"rowData\"> & { rowData: Entity | GroupRow | undefined }"],"doc":"<p>A header filter cell got focus. <code>cellType</code> is <code>&#39;filter&#39;</code>, <code>row</code> is 0.</p>\n<p><code>rowData</code> is not the header&#39;s own: it is the first displayed row (<code>datasource.getRow(0)</code>)\nfrom when the header cell was last rendered. That is a <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> when the datasource\nis grouped, and <code>undefined</code> when no rows were displayed - check with <code>isGroupRow()</code> before\nreading it as a data row.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cell-row-focus","signatures":["'cell-row-focus': GridCellEventData & { originalEvent: FocusEvent }"],"doc":"<p>A data cell got focus, by click or keyboard. <code>originalEvent</code> is the focus event. Not sent for a\nboolean (checkbox) cell.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"clear","signatures":["clear: GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Cleared from the row menu (Clear: Cell): the column, in the selected rows.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"copy-cell","signatures":["'copy-cell': GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Copied from the row menu (Copy: Cell Value): the value of the cell.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"copy-column","signatures":["'copy-column': GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Copied from the row menu (Copy: Column): the column, in the selected rows.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"copy-row","signatures":["'copy-row': GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Copied from the row menu (Copy: Row): all columns, in the selected rows.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"copy-row-col","signatures":["'copy-row-col': GridCellEventData"],"doc":"<p>Copied from the row menu (Copy: Row, selected rows/col): the selected columns (all when none\nare selected), in the selected rows.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filter-operator-change","signatures":["'filter-operator-change': { column: ColumnConfig; field: string; operator: FilterOperator; rebuildHeader: () => void }"],"doc":"<p>An operator was picked in the &quot;Set Operator&quot; part of the filter cell menu, and the filter\nran with it. The operator is state, <code>getState().headerFilters[field].operator</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code>: the column&#39;s field</li>\n<li><code>operator</code>: the operator picked</li>\n<li><code>column</code>: the options of the column as the grid uses them (from <code>GridConfig.columns</code>). Change\nthem to change what the header shows, e.g. <code>placeholderFilter</code></li>\n<li><code>rebuildHeader()</code>: renders the header again, call it after changing <code>column</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Was <code>{ cellConfig, rebuildHeader }</code> in v5, with the operator in <code>cellConfig.operator</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('filter-operator-change', (data) =&gt; {\n    data.column.placeholderFilter = data.operator; // show the operator in the empty filter cell\n    data.rebuildHeader();\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["filter-operator-header"]},{"name":"grid-connected","signatures":["'grid-connected': Record<string, never>"],"doc":"<p>A grid element connected to this interface: <code>element.connectInterface(gridInterface)</code>,\nor the element was put back in the dom. Empty payload. Was <code>gridConnected</code> in v5.</p>\n<p><code>createGrid()</code> connects before it returns: a handler subscribed after it hears this only when\nthe element is put back in the dom.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"paste","signatures":["paste: Omit<GridCellEventData, \"rowData\"> & { entity: Entity }"],"doc":"<p>Pasted from the row menu (Paste: Cell). Sent once per selected row pasted into, <code>entity</code>\nis that row. The other fields are the cell the menu was opened on.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"range-change","signatures":["'range-change': { ranges: CellRange[] }"],"doc":"<p>The ranges of cells changed: the user dragged over the cells, Shift+clicked, Ctrl/Cmd+clicked,\npressed Alt+Shift+arrows or Esc, moved to another cell, or <code>setRanges()</code> / <code>clearRanges()</code> were\ncalled. Also when the grid cleared them: the displayed rows or the layout changed, see\n<code>gridInterface.getRanges()</code>. While the mouse drags it is sent each time the range reaches another\ncell. Not sent when nothing changed.</p>\n<p><code>ranges</code> is what <code>getRanges()</code> gives now, <code>[]</code> when they were cleared.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('range-change', ({ ranges }) =&gt; {\n    console.log(ranges.length ? `${ranges.length} ranges, the last ends at row ${ranges[ranges.length - 1].toRow}` : 'no cells selected');\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["ranges"]}]}]},{"name":"GridHooks","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridHooks<T = unknown>"],"doc":"<p>The functions of a grid: what can not be written as data. They are kept apart from the\n<a href=\"#api/GridConfig\">GridConfig</a>, so the config is plain JSON and can be stored - in a backend, say - while the\nhooks stay in your code.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>isReadonly</code> - makes a cell readonly, or editable, from the values of its row</li>\n<li><code>cellClass</code> - adds css classes to a cell, from the values of its row</li>\n<li><code>menus</code> - changes the grid&#39;s right click menus, see <a href=\"#api/GridMenus\">GridMenus</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Give them to <code>createGrid(host, { config, datasource, hooks })</code> (or <code>new GridInterface(config, datasource, hooks)</code>), and change them while the grid is shown with <code>gridInterface.updateHooks()</code>.\nAll of them are optional.</p>\n<p>Do not use <code>this</code> in them: the grid calls them on its own copy of the hooks object.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, from the datasource: the row the hooks get is an\n<a href=\"#api/EntityUnion\">EntityUnion</a><code>&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig, type GridHooks } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Account {\n    company: string;\n    balance: number;\n    isActive: boolean;\n}\n\n// the config is plain JSON: it can come from a backend\nconst config: GridConfig = JSON.parse(\n    '{&quot;readonly&quot;: false, &quot;layout&quot;: {&quot;center&quot;: [{&quot;fields&quot;: [&quot;company&quot;], &quot;width&quot;: 150}, {&quot;fields&quot;: [&quot;balance&quot;], &quot;width&quot;: 100}]}}'\n);\n\n// the hooks are code\nconst hooks: GridHooks&lt;Account&gt; = {\n    // company can not be edited on an inactive row, every other cell follows the config\n    isReadonly: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'company' &amp;&amp; !row.isActive ? true : null),\n    // .negative { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.25); }\n    cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'balance' &amp;&amp; row.balance &lt; 0 ? { background: 'negative' } : null),\n    // no summary in the row menu\n    menus: { row: (defaults) =&gt; defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; !entry.id.startsWith('row.summary')) }\n};\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, { config, datasource, hooks });</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling","context-menu"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"menus","signatures":["menus?: GridMenus"],"doc":"<p>Changes the grid&#39;s right click menus: hide entries, reorder them, change their labels, add your\nown. One function per menu - <code>row</code> (a cell), <code>header</code> (a header label), <code>filter</code> (a header\nfilter) - that gets the grid&#39;s own entries and what the menu was opened on, and returns the\nentries to show. Called every time the menu opens. A menu without a function shows its defaults.</p>\n<p>The ids of the grid&#39;s own entries are listed in <code>MENU_IDS</code>, see <a href=\"#api/GridMenus\">GridMenus</a> and\n<a href=\"#api/MenuEntry\">MenuEntry</a>. Set or remove the functions later with <code>gridInterface.updateHooks({ menus })</code>.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>contextMenuCustom()</code> for the grid&#39;s own menus; a menu of your own is opened with\n<code>gridInterface.openMenu()</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridHooks, isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst hooks: GridHooks = {\n    menus: {\n        // no &quot;Clear:&quot; in the row menu, and an entry of your own at the end\n        row: (defaults, context) =&gt; [\n            ...defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; entry.id !== 'row.clear' &amp;&amp; entry.id !== 'row.clear.cell'),\n            { type: 'section', id: 'my.section', label: 'Row:' },\n            {\n                id: 'my.logRow',\n                label: 'Log row',\n                visible: () =&gt; !isGroupRow(context.row),\n                action: () =&gt; console.log(context.field, context.row)\n            }\n        ],\n        // the header menu without the grouping part\n        header: (defaults) =&gt; defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; !entry.id.startsWith('header.grouping'))\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"]}]},{"title":"Methods","members":[{"name":"cellClass","signatures":["cellClass?(row: EntityUnion<T>, field: string): CellClass | null | undefined"],"doc":"<p>Adds css classes to a cell, from the values of its row: to color a cell by its value, say. Called\nevery time a cell is rendered, keep it fast. See <a href=\"#api/CellClass\">CellClass</a> for where each class goes.</p>\n<p>Return <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> for no classes of your own.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>gridInterface.cellAppendClassSetter(callback)</code>: <code>inputClass</code> is <code>input</code>,\n<code>dimmedClass</code> is <code>background</code>, the row comes first and the third argument (readonly) is gone.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the cell&#39;s row. Always a data row: a group row has no cells</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the cell&#39;s field</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridHooks } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// .low { position: absolute; inset: 0; background: rgba(239, 68, 68, 0.25); }\nconst hooks: GridHooks = {\n    cellClass: (row, field) =&gt; {\n        if (field === 'balance' &amp;&amp; row.balance &lt; 0) {\n            return { background: 'low', input: 'bold-text' };\n        }\n        return null;\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"]},{"name":"isReadonly","signatures":["isReadonly?(row: EntityUnion<T>, field: string, readonlyByConfig: boolean): boolean | null | undefined"],"doc":"<p>Makes a cell readonly, or editable, from the values of its row. Called every time a cell is\nrendered, and by the row menu&#39;s paste, clear and delete for each selected row.</p>\n<p>Return <code>true</code> (readonly) or <code>false</code> (editable). <code>null</code> or <code>undefined</code> leaves it to the config:\nthe column&#39;s <code>readonly</code> option, which is passed in as <code>readonlyByConfig</code>. The grid&#39;s own\n<code>readonly: true</code> makes every cell readonly, whatever this returns.</p>\n<p>A row it returns <code>true</code> for in every column of the layout is locked: the row menu&#39;s delete\n(<code>row.delete.rows</code>) skips it. The column&#39;s <code>readonly</code> option does not lock a row.</p>\n<p>Called often: keep it fast. When what it reads changes, call <code>gridInterface.refresh()</code> to render\nthe cells again.</p>\n<p>Replaces v5&#39;s <code>gridInterface.readonlySetter(callback)</code>; the row comes first now.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code> the cell&#39;s row. Always a data row: a group row has no cells</li>\n<li><code>field</code> the cell&#39;s field</li>\n<li><code>readonlyByConfig</code> the column&#39;s <code>readonly</code> option, <code>false</code> when it is not set</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridHooks } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// company can not be edited on an inactive row, every other cell follows the config\nconst hooks: GridHooks = {\n    isReadonly: (row, field) =&gt; (field === 'company' &amp;&amp; row.isActive === false ? true : null)\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["cell-styling"]}]}]},{"name":"GridLayout","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridLayout"],"doc":"<p>Where the columns go. Each list is a list of columns from left to right; a column shows one field,\nor several stacked on top of each other.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>left</code> - pinned to the left, does not scroll sideways</li>\n<li><code>center</code> - scrolls sideways</li>\n<li><code>right</code> - pinned to the right</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridLayout } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst layout: GridLayout = {\n    left: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }],\n    center: [\n        { fields: ['age', 'born'], width: 100 }, // two fields stacked in one column\n        { fields: ['company'], width: 200 }\n    ],\n    right: [] // the same as leaving it out\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["column-layout"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"center","signatures":["center: LayoutColumn[]"],"doc":"<p>the columns that scroll sideways</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"left","signatures":["left?: LayoutColumn[]"],"doc":"<p>the columns pinned to the left, default none</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"right","signatures":["right?: LayoutColumn[]"],"doc":"<p>the columns pinned to the right, default none</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridMenus","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridMenus"],"doc":"<p>Changes the grid&#39;s right click menus: the <code>menus</code> hook (<a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>). Each function gets the\ngrid&#39;s own entries for that menu (<code>defaults</code>, in the order shown in <a href=\"#api/MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a>) and what the\nmenu was opened on, and returns the entries to show - hide some, reorder them, change them, add\nyour own. Called every time the menu opens.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>row</code>: right click on a cell - copy, filter on the value, paste, clear, summary ...</li>\n<li><code>header</code>: right click on a header label - pin, hide, column chooser, sizes, grouping</li>\n<li><code>filter</code>: right click on a header filter - clear, is blank, operator, the value list</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The grid&#39;s own entries are new objects every time, change them as you like. Left out, a menu shows\nits defaults. Change the functions while the grid is shown with <code>gridInterface.updateHooks({ menus })</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridMenus } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// createGrid(host, { config, datasource, hooks: { menus } })\nconst menus: GridMenus = {\n    row: (defaults, context) =&gt; [\n        // no summary\n        ...defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; !entry.id.startsWith('row.summary')),\n        { type: 'section', id: 'my.section', label: 'Mine:' },\n        { id: 'my.logRow', label: 'Log row', action: () =&gt; console.log(context.field, context.row) }\n    ],\n    // the value list first, then the rest\n    filter: (defaults) =&gt; [\n        ...defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; entry.id === 'filter.values'),\n        ...defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; entry.id !== 'filter.values')\n    ],\n    // a label of your own\n    header: (defaults) =&gt;\n        defaults.map((entry) =&gt; (entry.id === 'header.column.hide' ? { ...entry, label: 'Hide column' } : entry))\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"filter","signatures":["filter?: (defaults: MenuEntry[], context: MenuContext) => MenuEntry[]"],"doc":"<p>the menu of a header filter</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"header","signatures":["header?: (defaults: MenuEntry[], context: MenuContext) => MenuEntry[]"],"doc":"<p>the menu of a header label</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row?: (defaults: MenuEntry[], context: MenuContext) => MenuEntry[]"],"doc":"<p>the menu of a cell</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GridState","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GridState"],"doc":"<p>What the user changes while working with the grid: <code>gridInterface.getState()</code> reads it,\n<code>setState()</code> sets it, <code>resetState()</code> goes back to the one the grid started with\n(<code>GridConfig.initialState</code>, and the config&#39;s <code>layout</code>).</p>\n<p>It is plain data, so it can be stored, e.g. as JSON. The one value JSON changes is a <code>Date</code> in the\nfilter or a header filter: it comes back as its ISO text, and <code>setState()</code> keeps it as text. A\n<code>date</code> or <code>datetime</code> field reads the text as the same moment - the same rows, the same date in the\nheader filter. A field not listed as <code>date</code> / <code>datetime</code> in the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code> filters on a\n<code>Date</code> as a date only while it is a <code>Date</code>, after JSON it compares the text: list its type.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridState } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// keep what the user did, and give it back next time\nlocalStorage.setItem('my-grid', JSON.stringify(gridInterface.getState()));\n\nconst saved: GridState | null = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem('my-grid') ?? 'null');\nif (saved) {\n    gridInterface.setState(saved);\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"expandedGroups","signatures":["expandedGroups: string[]"],"doc":"<p>the ids of the expanded groups, <code>datasource.getExpanded()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"filter","signatures":["filter: FilterExpression | null"],"doc":"<p>the filter, <code>datasource.getFilter()</code>: the header filters&#39; conditions are part of it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"grouping","signatures":["grouping: GroupArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>the grouping, <code>datasource.getGrouping()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"headerFilters","signatures":["headerFilters: Record<string, HeaderFilter>"],"doc":"<p>what the header filter cells show, keyed by field: the value typed or picked, and the operator\npicked in the header filter&#39;s menu. Only the columns that have one are listed.</p>\n<p>The rows are filtered by <code>filter</code>: these are what the header shows, the conditions they made are\nin <code>filter</code> already. A state from <code>getState()</code> has both.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"layout","signatures":["layout: GridLayout"],"doc":"<p>column order, pinning and widths</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"sorting","signatures":["sorting: SortArgument[]"],"doc":"<p>the sort, <code>datasource.getLastSorting()</code>. When grouped, the grouped fields come first</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GroupArgument","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GroupArgument"],"doc":"<p>One level of grouping: the field to group on and its title. <code>datasource.group()</code> takes a list of\nthem, the first is the outer group. It is what <code>GridState.grouping</code> holds.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GroupArgument } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst grouping: GroupArgument[] = [\n    { attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' },\n    { attribute: 'company', title: 'Company' } // inside each country\n];\ndatasource.group(grouping);</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"attribute","signatures":["attribute: string"],"doc":"<p>the field to group on</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"title","signatures":["title: string"],"doc":"<p>shown in the group rows (<code>&#39;Country: Norway&#39;</code>, its first letter made upper case) and in the\ngrouping panel above the grid. The grid uses the column&#39;s label when the user groups by dragging\na column to the panel</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"GroupRow","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface GroupRow"],"doc":"<p>A group header row. When the datasource is grouped, the displayed rows\n(<code>datasource.getRows()</code>) mix your data rows with these headers - one per group, in front of\nits rows. A group row is made by the datasource, it is not one of your objects: it can not be\nselected, edited or marked for deletion, and <code>getDataRows()</code>, <code>getSelectedRows()</code> and\n<code>getAllData()</code> never contain one. Tell the two kinds apart with <a href=\"#api/isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a>.</p>\n<p>Read the fields, do not change them - expand and collapse with <code>datasource.expandGroup(id)</code> /\n<code>collapseGroup(id)</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.group([{ attribute: 'country', title: 'Country' }]);\ndatasource.expandGroup();\n\nfor (const row of datasource.getRows()) {\n    if (isGroupRow(row)) {\n        console.log(row.__groupName, row.__groupTotal, row.__groupExpanded ? 'open' : 'closed');\n    } else {\n        console.log('  ', row.name);\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"__group","signatures":["__group: true"],"doc":"<p>always <code>true</code>, the mark of a group row - see <a href=\"#api/isGroupRow\">isGroupRow</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupChildren","signatures":["__groupChildren: (Entity | GroupRow)[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows in the group: data rows, or the group rows of the next level when grouped on more than one attribute</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupExpanded","signatures":["__groupExpanded: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when the group is expanded and its rows are displayed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupID","signatures":["__groupID: string"],"doc":"<p>id of the group, for <code>expandGroup(id)</code> / <code>collapseGroup(id)</code>: the grouped value as the field&#39;s\nformatter shows it, <code>&#39;Norway&#39;</code>. On a sub group the ids of the groups above it come first, joined\nby <code>-</code>: <code>&#39;Norway-Apple&#39;</code>. The group of the blank values is <code>&#39; blank&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupLvl","signatures":["__groupLvl: number"],"doc":"<p>the grouping level, 0 for the first <code>group()</code> attribute. The grid indents the row by it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupName","signatures":["__groupName: string"],"doc":"<p>the text the grid shows: the group&#39;s title (its first letter in upper case) and the value,\n<code>&#39;Country: Norway&#39;</code>. The group of the blank values shows the text <code>grouping.blank</code>,\n<code>&#39;Country: blank&#39;</code> - see <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"__groupTotal","signatures":["__groupTotal: number"],"doc":"<p>number of data rows in the group, the ones in its sub groups included</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"HeaderFilter","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface HeaderFilter"],"doc":"<p>The header filter of one column, see <code>GridState.headerFilters</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { HeaderFilter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst headerFilters: Record&lt;string, HeaderFilter&gt; = {\n    name: { value: 'ann*' }, // typed in the name column, with the column's operator\n    age: { value: 30, operator: 'LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO' }, // the operator picked in the menu\n    active: { value: true } // a boolean column's checkbox\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator?: FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>the operator picked in the header filter&#39;s menu. Left out, the column&#39;s <code>operator</code> is used</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"value","signatures":["value: unknown"],"doc":"<p>what the header filter cell shows: the text typed, the date picked, <code>true</code>/<code>false</code> for a checkbox. null is empty</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"HTMLCellElement","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface HTMLCellElement extends HTMLElement"],"doc":"<p>A cell element of the grid: the <code>cell</code> the grid events and the menu context give you. The grid\nreuses these elements while scrolling, so the <code>$</code> fields say what the cell shows now - read them\nin the handler, do not keep the element for later.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log(data.cell.$attribute, data.cell.$row); // the same as data.attribute, data.row\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"$attribute","signatures":["$attribute: string | null"],"doc":"<p>the field of the cell. null on group and selector cells, they have no field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$celno","signatures":["$celno: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the cell in the column (a column can stack several fields), 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$coltype","signatures":["$coltype: ColType"],"doc":"<p>the section of the grid the cell is in</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$column","signatures":["$column: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the column in its section (<code>$coltype</code>), 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$focused","signatures":["$focused: boolean"],"doc":"<p>helper to know if cell is focused</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"$row","signatures":["$row: number"],"doc":"<p>index of the row in the displayed rows, 0 based</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"IDateConfig","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface IDateConfig"],"doc":"<p>The config of a <a href=\"#api/DateInterface\">DateInterface</a>: a date picker (<code>datepicker: true</code> - one month, one date with a\ntime, and Clear / Now / Use buttons) or a calendar (<code>datepicker: false</code> - one or more months, click\ndays to select them).</p>\n<p>The type requires every field but <code>texts</code>, <code>datepickerDate</code>, <code>datepickerHour</code>, <code>datepickerMinute</code> and\n<code>datepickerHeight</code>.</p>\n<p>The names of the months and days and the buttons are texts, the ids <code>datePicker.*</code> of <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>:\nset with <a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a>, or with <code>texts</code> for this picker.</p>\n<p>The grid&#39;s date picker (<code>GridConfig.datePickerConfig</code>) takes a <code>Partial&lt;IDateConfig&gt;</code>: the fields to\nchange. It reads only <code>showWeek</code>, <code>isoWeek</code>, <code>weekStart</code>, <code>rowHeight</code>, <code>monthWidth</code>, <code>monthMargin</code>,\n<code>hideDimmedDates</code>, <code>showYearInMonth</code> and <code>datepickerHeight</code>, each with a default; the others it sets\nitself - <code>texts</code> to the grid&#39;s texts.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type DateElement, DateInterface, type IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\nimport '@simple-html/grid/date.css';\n\nconst config: IDateConfig = {\n    datepicker: true,\n    datepickerDate: new Date(), // the date it opens on\n    monthsToShow: 1,\n    monthColumns: 1,\n    startMonth: 0, // set from datepickerDate in a date picker\n    startYear: 2026,\n    weekStart: 1, // the week starts on monday\n    showWeek: true,\n    isoWeek: true,\n    rowHeight: 22,\n    monthWidth: 230,\n    monthMargin: 10,\n    hideDimmedDates: false,\n    showYearInMonth: false,\n    headerTitle: ''\n};\n\nconst dateInterface = new DateInterface(config);\nconst element = document.createElement('simple-html-date') as DateElement;\nelement.classList.add('simple-html-date');\nelement.connectInterface(dateInterface);\nhost.appendChild(element);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"datepicker","signatures":["datepicker: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code>: a date picker - one month, one date and its time, and Clear / Now / Use buttons that\nsend the <code>date-select</code> event. <code>false</code>: a calendar - click days to select them, shift+click a\nrange, read them with <code>getSelected()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerDate","signatures":["datepickerDate?: Date | null"],"doc":"<p>the date the date picker opens on and shows picked. null or undefined: the datepicker opens on today.\nThe picker changes this date in place (seconds and milliseconds set to 0)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerHeight","signatures":["datepickerHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>grid only: the height of the date picker in px, default 317. The grid opens the picker above the\ncell when there is no room for this below it</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerHour","signatures":["datepickerHour?: number"],"doc":"<p>the hour of the picked time, set from <code>datepickerDate</code> by the date picker</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datepickerMinute","signatures":["datepickerMinute?: number"],"doc":"<p>the minutes of the picked time, set from <code>datepickerDate</code> by the date picker</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"headerTitle","signatures":["headerTitle: string"],"doc":"<p>the title above the months of a calendar. Not shown by a date picker</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hideDimmedDates","signatures":["hideDimmedDates: boolean"],"doc":"<p>hides the days of the month before and after, which are shown dimmed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"isoWeek","signatures":["isoWeek: boolean"],"doc":"<p>ISO week numbers (weeks start on monday), else weeks that start on sunday</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"monthColumns","signatures":["monthColumns: number"],"doc":"<p>how many months a calendar shows side by side, before it starts a new row. A date picker sets 1</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"monthMargin","signatures":["monthMargin: number"],"doc":"<p>the space on each side of a month, in px</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"monthsToShow","signatures":["monthsToShow: number"],"doc":"<p>how many months a calendar shows. A date picker shows 1, whatever this is</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"monthWidth","signatures":["monthWidth: number"],"doc":"<p>the width of a month, in px</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowHeight","signatures":["rowHeight: number"],"doc":"<p>the height of a row of days, in px</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"showWeek","signatures":["showWeek: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the week numbers in front of each week</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"showYearInMonth","signatures":["showYearInMonth: boolean"],"doc":"<p>a calendar shows the year after the month&#39;s name: <code>November-2026</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"startMonth","signatures":["startMonth: number"],"doc":"<p>the first month shown, 0 (January) to 11. A date picker sets it from <code>datepickerDate</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"startYear","signatures":["startYear: number"],"doc":"<p>the year of the first month shown. A date picker sets it from <code>datepickerDate</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"texts","signatures":["texts?: Texts"],"doc":"<p>The texts of this picker, by id: the ones to change, they win over the page&#39;s (<a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a>).\nThe ids are <code>datePicker.*</code> of <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>: <code>datePicker.month.january</code> ..., <code>datePicker.day.sunday</code>\n... (<code>&#39;Su&#39;</code>), and the buttons and labels. The grid sets it to its own <code>texts</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { IDateConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst texts: IDateConfig['texts'] = { 'datePicker.month.january': 'Januar', 'datePicker.day.monday': 'Ma' };</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"weekStart","signatures":["weekStart: number"],"doc":"<p>the first day of the week: 0 Sunday, 1 Monday ... The days are shown from it on</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"IStyle","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface IStyle"],"doc":"<p>The style of one date in a calendar, for <a href=\"#api/DateInterface.styleRange\">DateInterface.styleRange</a> - which is not implemented\nyet: it only logs a warning.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"addClass","signatures":["addClass?: string | string[]"],"doc":"<p>css classes to add</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"backgroundColor","signatures":["backgroundColor?: string"],"doc":"<p>the background color, a css color</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"bold","signatures":["bold?: string"],"doc":"<p>a css font weight</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"borderColor","signatures":["borderColor?: string"],"doc":"<p>the border color, a css color</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"date","signatures":["date: Date"],"doc":"<p>the date to style</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"fontColor","signatures":["fontColor?: string"],"doc":"<p>the text color, a css color</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"LayoutColumn","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface LayoutColumn"],"doc":"<p>One column of the <a href=\"#api/GridLayout\">GridLayout</a>: the fields it shows, stacked from top to bottom, and its\nwidth. The options of a field (label, placeholders, readonly ...) are in <code>GridConfig.columns</code>, its\ntype and default label in the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>.</p>\n<p>Every column gets as many cells as the column with the most fields; a column with fewer fields\nleaves the rest empty. A column without fields is left out.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { LayoutColumn } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst single: LayoutColumn = { fields: ['name'], width: 150 };\nconst stacked: LayoutColumn = { fields: ['firstName', 'lastName'], width: 120 };</code></pre>\n","samples":["column-layout"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"fields","signatures":["fields: string[]"],"doc":"<p>the fields shown in this column, top to bottom</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"width","signatures":["width: number"],"doc":"<p>width in px</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuBlock","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuBlock"],"doc":"<p>An element shown in the menu as it is. The grid adds it to the menu and does nothing else with it:\nthe element handles its own clicks and input, and clicking in it does not close the menu - call\n<code>gridInterface.closeMenu()</code> for that.</p>\n<p>The header filter menu&#39;s value list (search box, checkboxes, &quot;Run Search&quot;) is a block of the grid&#39;s\nown, <code>&#39;filter.values&#39;</code>: hide or move it as one entry, it is not built from items.</p>\n<p>Also for something bigger than a list of items in a menu of your own: a second grid as a dropdown,\nwhich then closes with the grid&#39;s menus (outside click, scroll, another menu opening).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type GridConfig, type GridElement, GridInterface } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const cell: HTMLElement;\ndeclare const dropdownConfig: GridConfig;\nconst dropdownDatasource = new Datasource();\n\n// a grid to pick from, opened under a cell\nconst dropdown = document.createElement('simple-html-grid') as GridElement;\ndropdown.style.width = '300px';\ndropdown.style.height = '250px';\ndropdown.connectInterface(new GridInterface(dropdownConfig, dropdownDatasource));\ngridInterface.openMenu(cell, [{ type: 'block', id: 'company-picker', element: dropdown }]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["dropdown-grid"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"element","signatures":["element: HTMLElement"],"doc":"<p>the element shown</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: \"block\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;block&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the block out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuContext","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuContext"],"doc":"<p>What a menu was opened on, handed to every callback of its entries (<code>action</code>, <code>visible</code>, <code>disabled</code>,\n<code>selected</code>) and to the <a href=\"#api/GridMenus\">GridMenus</a> functions.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow, type MenuItem } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst copyKey: MenuItem = {\n    id: 'my.copyKey',\n    label: 'Copy key',\n    visible: (context) =&gt; context.row !== undefined &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(context.row),\n    action: (context) =&gt; {\n        if (context.row &amp;&amp; !isGroupRow(context.row)) {\n            navigator.clipboard.writeText(String(context.row.id));\n        }\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"cell","signatures":["cell: HTMLElement | undefined"],"doc":"<p>the cell the menu was opened on, <code>undefined</code> in a menu opened with <code>openMenu()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datasource","signatures":["datasource: Datasource<unknown>"],"doc":"<p>the grid&#39;s datasource, <code>gridInterface.getDatasource()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field of the cell the menu was opened on. <code>&#39;&#39;</code> in a menu opened with <code>openMenu()</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"gridInterface","signatures":["gridInterface: GridInterface<unknown>"],"doc":"<p>the grid</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"menu","signatures":["menu: \"filter\" | \"header\" | \"row\" | \"custom\""],"doc":"<p>which menu: <code>&#39;row&#39;</code> (right click on a cell), <code>&#39;header&#39;</code> (on a header label), <code>&#39;filter&#39;</code> (on a\nheader filter) or <code>&#39;custom&#39;</code> (opened with <code>gridInterface.openMenu()</code>)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: Entity | GroupRow | undefined"],"doc":"<ul>\n<li>row menu: the row of the cell, always a data row (a group row has no cells)</li>\n<li>header and filter menus: the first displayed row, a <a href=\"#api/GroupRow\">GroupRow</a> when the datasource is\ngrouped and <code>undefined</code> when no rows are shown - as <code>cell-header-focus</code> sends it</li>\n<li><code>openMenu()</code>: <code>undefined</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Check with <code>isGroupRow()</code> before reading it as a data row.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowIndex","signatures":["rowIndex: number"],"doc":"<p>the index of <code>row</code> in the displayed rows (<code>datasource.getRows()</code>): 0 in the header and filter\nmenus, -1 in a menu opened with <code>openMenu()</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuItem","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuItem"],"doc":"<p>An entry to click. Clicking it closes the menu, then calls <code>action</code>.</p>\n<p><code>type</code> can be left out, an entry without one is an item.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow, type MenuItem } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst logRow: MenuItem = {\n    id: 'my.logRow',\n    label: 'Log row',\n    hint: 'console',\n    action: (context) =&gt; console.log(context.field, context.row),\n    // only on data rows, and greyed out while nothing is selected\n    visible: (context) =&gt; !isGroupRow(context.row),\n    disabled: (context) =&gt; context.datasource.getSelectedRows().length === 0\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"action","signatures":["action: (context: MenuContext) => void"],"doc":"<p>called when the item is clicked, after the menu is closed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"disabled","signatures":["disabled?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> shows the item greyed out, and clicking it does nothing. Called when the menu opens</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hint","signatures":["hint?: string"],"doc":"<p>shown after the label, in italics and in parentheses: <code>Paste cell (selected rows)</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the text shown</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"selected","signatures":["selected?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> shows the item as the one picked now, as the header filter menu does with its operator.\nCalled when the menu opens</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type?: \"item\""],"doc":"<p><code>&#39;item&#39;</code>, or left out</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the item out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuPosition","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuPosition"],"doc":"<p>Where <code>gridInterface.openMenu()</code> opens a menu: a point in the window, in px from its left and top\nedges - the same as a mouse event&#39;s <code>clientX</code> / <code>clientY</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuEntry, MenuPosition } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const button: HTMLButtonElement;\ndeclare const entries: MenuEntry[];\n\nconst rect = button.getBoundingClientRect();\nconst position: MenuPosition = { x: rect.left, y: rect.bottom };\ngridInterface.openMenu(position, entries);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"x","signatures":["x: number"],"doc":"<p>px from the left edge of the window</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"y","signatures":["y: number"],"doc":"<p>px from the top edge of the window</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuSection","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuSection"],"doc":"<p>A section header, &quot;Copy:&quot; or &quot;Filter:&quot; in the grid&#39;s menus, with a line under it. Not clickable.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuSection } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst section: MenuSection = { type: 'section', id: 'my.export', label: 'Export:' };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label: string"],"doc":"<p>the text shown, the grid&#39;s own end with a colon</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: \"section\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;section&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the header out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"MenuSeparator","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface MenuSeparator"],"doc":"<p>A dashed line between two entries.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuSeparator } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst separator: MenuSeparator = { type: 'separator', id: 'my.separator' };</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>a name for the entry, unique in its menu. See <a href=\"#api/MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a> for the grid&#39;s own</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"type","signatures":["type: \"separator\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;separator&#39;</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"visible","signatures":["visible?: (context: MenuContext) => boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> leaves the line out of the menu. Called when the menu opens, left out it is shown</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"RemovedConflict","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface RemovedConflict<T = any>"],"doc":"<p>A row in conflict as a whole: <code>datasource.upsert(rows, { removeMissing: true })</code> did not get it from\nthe server, but the row has local changes - edits, a deletion mark, or the user is typing in it. It\nis kept, with this conflict, instead of being removed.</p>\n<p>Part of <a href=\"#api/Conflict\">Conflict</a>, see there.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { RemovedConflict } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst describe = (conflict: RemovedConflict) =&gt; `row ${conflict.row.__KEY} is no longer on the server`;</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: null"],"doc":"<p>always <code>null</code>: the row as a whole, not a field. Tells it from a <a href=\"#api/ValueConflict\">ValueConflict</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"remote","signatures":["remote: \"removed\""],"doc":"<p>always <code>&#39;removed&#39;</code>: the server no longer has the row</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: EntityUnion<T>"],"doc":"<p>the row, the one the datasource handed out</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"SortArgument","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface SortArgument"],"doc":"<p>One field to sort on, and the direction. <code>datasource.sort()</code> takes one or a list of them, the first\nin the list decides first. It is what <code>GridState.sorting</code> holds.</p>\n<p>Blank values (null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) come first when ascending, last when descending.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { SortArgument } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst byAge: SortArgument = { attribute: 'age', ascending: false };\ndatasource.sort([{ attribute: 'country', ascending: true }, byAge]);</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"ascending","signatures":["ascending: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> for A-Z / 0-9 / oldest first, <code>false</code> for the other way round</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"attribute","signatures":["attribute: string"],"doc":"<p>the field to sort on</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"UpsertOptions","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface UpsertOptions"],"doc":"<p>The options of <code>datasource.upsert(rows, options)</code>. Both are optional.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { UpsertOptions } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const rowsFromServer: object[];\n\n// the server sent every row: the rows it did not send are gone there\nconst options: UpsertOptions = { removeMissing: true };\ndatasource.upsert(rowsFromServer, options);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"refilter","signatures":["refilter?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>false</code> to leave the filter out, default <code>true</code>: the filter runs on the rows, so a row whose new\nvalues the filter leaves out is no longer shown. With <code>false</code> the rows shown stay shown (the\nrows added are shown too) until the filter runs again - the sorting and grouping still run, as\nfor <code>setData(rows, { refilter: false })</code></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removeMissing","signatures":["removeMissing?: boolean"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when the rows are every row there is (a full poll): a row whose key is not among them\nis removed. Default <code>false</code>, the rows are changes only (a push of what changed). A row with\nlocal changes is not removed, it gets a <a href=\"#api/RemovedConflict\">RemovedConflict</a>; a new row (<code>addNewEmpty()</code>)\nis never removed, the server does not have it yet</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"UpsertResult","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface UpsertResult<T = any>"],"doc":"<p>What <code>datasource.upsert()</code> did, the rows themselves (not copies).</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>declare const rowsFromServer: object[];\n\nconst { added, updated, removed, conflicts } = datasource.upsert(rowsFromServer, { removeMissing: true });\nconsole.log(`${added.length} new, ${updated.length} changed, ${removed.length} removed, ${conflicts.length} conflicts`);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"added","signatures":["added: EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows of keys that were not in the data: added, as loaded rows (not new, not edited)</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"conflicts","signatures":["conflicts: Conflict<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the conflicts this upsert made, or gave a newer server value. <code>getConflicts()</code> has every one</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"removed","signatures":["removed: EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows <code>removeMissing</code> removed</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"updated","signatures":["updated: EntityUnion<T>[]"],"doc":"<p>the rows a value of the server changed, or that got a conflict - each once</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ValidationError","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ValidationError<T = unknown>"],"doc":"<p>The validation errors of one field of one row, what <code>datasource.validate()</code> and <code>getErrors()</code>\nreturn a list of.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of your rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ValidationError } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst errors: ValidationError[] = datasource.validate();\nfor (const { row, field, messages } of errors) {\n    console.log(row.__KEY, datasource.getField(field).label, messages.join(', '));\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"messages","signatures":["messages: string[]"],"doc":"<p>a message per rule the value fails, in the order of the field&#39;s rules</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: Entity & T"],"doc":"<p>the row itself, not a copy</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ValidationRuleObject","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ValidationRuleObject"],"doc":"<p>A validation rule written out: the id of its validator, its options, and a message of its own.\nThe validator gets it as its <code>rule</code> argument - a rule given as text (<code>&#39;required&#39;</code>) is\n<code>{ id: &#39;required&#39; }</code> there.</p>\n<p>The built-in validators take their option as <code>value</code> (see <a href=\"#api/registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>). A validator\nof your own can take any options: they are what the rule has besides <code>id</code> and <code>message</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ValidationRuleObject } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst atLeastZero: ValidationRuleObject = { id: 'min', value: 0 };\nconst notTooOld: ValidationRuleObject = { id: 'max', value: 150, message: 'too old, at most {value}' };</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"id","signatures":["id: string"],"doc":"<p>the id of the validator: a built-in one (<code>&#39;required&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;min&#39;</code> ...) or one registered with <a href=\"#api/registerValidator\">registerValidator</a></p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"message","signatures":["message?: string"],"doc":"<p>the message when the value fails the rule, instead of the validator&#39;s: the message itself, or a\ntext id - a text set with <code>setTexts()</code>, so it can be translated. <code>{name}</code> in it is replaced by\nthe rule&#39;s option <code>name</code>: <code>&#39;at most {value}&#39;</code> is <code>&#39;at most 150&#39;</code> for <code>{ id: &#39;max&#39;, value: 150 }</code></p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"ValueConflict","group":"Interfaces","kind":"Interface","signatures":["interface ValueConflict<T = any>"],"doc":"<p>A field in conflict: <code>datasource.upsert()</code> brought a new value from the server for a field the user\nhas edited and not saved (or is typing in). The user&#39;s value is kept in the row, the server&#39;s is\nthe field&#39;s original now - so <code>getChanges()</code> sends the user&#39;s value, as an edit of what the server\nhas now.</p>\n<p>Part of <a href=\"#api/Conflict\">Conflict</a>, see there. <code>getConflicts()</code> makes the objects: <code>local</code> is the value the row\nhas when it is called.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ValueConflict } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst describe = (conflict: ValueConflict) =&gt;\n    `${conflict.field}: yours ${conflict.local}, the server's ${conflict.remote} (it was ${conflict.original})`;</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"field","signatures":["field: string"],"doc":"<p>the field in conflict</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"local","signatures":["local: unknown"],"doc":"<p>the user&#39;s value: the value the row has, kept by the merge</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"original","signatures":["original: unknown"],"doc":"<p>the value the user&#39;s edit started from: the original before the server changed it. A second\nmerge that changes the field again keeps it, it gives <code>remote</code> the newer value</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"remote","signatures":["remote: unknown"],"doc":"<p>the server&#39;s value: the field&#39;s original now, what <code>resolveConflict(row, field, &#39;remote&#39;)</code> takes</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"row","signatures":["row: EntityUnion<T>"],"doc":"<p>the row, the one the datasource handed out</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"AggregateFunction","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type AggregateFunction = \"sum\" | \"avg\" | \"min\" | \"max\" | \"count\""],"doc":"<p>How <a href=\"#api/Datasource.aggregate\">Datasource.aggregate</a> sums up the values of a field over rows. Blank values (<code>null</code>,\n<code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>, an invalid <code>Date</code>) are left out by all of them; <code>0</code> and <code>false</code> are values.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>function</th>\n<th>the result</th>\n<th>of no values</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;sum&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the sum of the numbers</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;avg&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the average of the numbers: their sum / how many there are</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;min&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the smallest number</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;max&#39;</code></td>\n<td>the largest number</td>\n<td><code>null</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;count&#39;</code></td>\n<td>how many values are not blank, of any type</td>\n<td><code>0</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>min</code> and <code>max</code> take numbers only: a value that is no number (text, even <code>&#39;12&#39;</code>, a\n<code>Date</code>, <code>NaN</code>, <code>Infinity</code>) is left out, as a blank is. Nothing is rounded: format the result with the field&#39;s\nformatter. The sum is added up with a compensated sum (Neumaier), so it does not drift away over\nmany rows: 100 000 times <code>0.1</code> is <code>10000</code>.</p>\n<p>It is what a column&#39;s <code>aggregate</code> in the grid config shows, in the group rows and the totals row.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { AggregateFunction } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst fn: AggregateFunction = 'sum';\ndatasource.aggregate('balance', fn); // over the rows the filter lets through</code></pre>\n","samples":["aggregates"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ColType","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ColType = \"group\" | \"selector\" | \"left-pinned\" | \"middle-pinned\" | \"right-pinned\""],"doc":"<p>Which section of the grid a cell is in, the <code>colType</code> of the grid events:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;left-pinned&#39;</code> - the columns pinned left (<code>GridLayout.left</code>)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;middle-pinned&#39;</code> - the columns that scroll sideways (<code>GridLayout.center</code>)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;right-pinned&#39;</code> - the columns pinned right (<code>GridLayout.right</code>)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;selector&#39;</code> - the row selector at the far left, with the row numbers</li>\n<li><code>&#39;group&#39;</code> - the cells of a group row</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>gridInterface.on('cell-click', (data) =&gt; {\n    if (data.colType === 'left-pinned') {\n        console.log('a pinned column', data.attribute);\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ColumnConfig","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ColumnConfig"],"doc":"<p>The options of one column, in <code>GridConfig.columns</code> under the field&#39;s name. Every option is\noptional, a field without an entry gets the defaults.</p>\n<p>The type of the column comes from the datasource (<code>datasource.getField(field).type</code>), set it in the\ndatasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>, not here. So do the validation rules: a value the user has to fill in is the\nfield&#39;s <code>required</code> rule (<code>fields: { company: { validate: [&#39;required&#39;] } }</code>), which also gives its\nempty editable cells the grid&#39;s blue stripes (<code>simple-html-mandatory</code>). It replaces v5&#39;s\n<code>mandatory</code> column option.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ColumnConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst columns: Record&lt;string, ColumnConfig&gt; = {\n    company: { label: 'Company', placeholderRow: 'required' },\n    age: { operator: 'EQUAL', numberOverride: 'ZERO_TO_BLANK' },\n    born: { placeholderFilter: 'from date', readonly: true },\n    country: { focusButton: 'ALWAYS', allowPasteClearOnly: true }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"aggregate","signatures":["aggregate?: AggregateFunction"],"doc":"<p>sums the column up: <code>&#39;sum&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;avg&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;min&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;max&#39;</code> or <code>&#39;count&#39;</code>, see\n<a href=\"#api/AggregateFunction\">AggregateFunction</a>. The grid shows it in the column&#39;s place in each group row\n(<code>GridConfig.groupAggregates</code>, on by default) and in the totals row (<code>GridConfig.totalsRow</code>), with\na short label in front: <code>Sum 1234.5</code> (the texts <code>aggregate.*</code>). The datasource computes it:\n<code>datasource.aggregate(field, fn)</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>sum</code>, <code>avg</code>, <code>min</code> and <code>max</code> are for a <code>number</code> field (the datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>), anything\nelse throws a <code>TypeError</code> when the grid is made or <code>updateConfig()</code> is given the column. They\ntake the numbers, blanks and what is no number are left out. The value is shown with the\nfield&#39;s formatter, not rounded: give the field a formatter with the decimals you want.</li>\n<li><code>count</code> counts the values that are not blank, in a field of any type. Shown as a whole number.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        balance: { aggregate: 'sum' },\n        age: { aggregate: 'avg' },\n        email: { aggregate: 'count' }\n    },\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['email'], width: 200 }, { fields: ['age'], width: 80 }, { fields: ['balance'], width: 120 }] },\n    totalsRow: true\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["aggregates"]},{"name":"allowPasteClearOnly","signatures":["allowPasteClearOnly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the cells can not be typed in, only changed by the row menu&#39;s paste and clear (and by your own\ncode, e.g. a dropdown from <code>focusButton</code>). Typed text is undone right away</p>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"dynamicCellTypeColumn","signatures":["dynamicCellTypeColumn?: string"],"doc":"<p>the name of another column whose value in the row is the type of this cell -\n<code>&#39;text&#39; | &#39;number&#39; | &#39;boolean&#39; | &#39;date&#39; | &#39;datetime&#39;</code>. A number/text/date etc in the same\ncolumn, for property/value style data. Only for a <code>text</code> field (the default), and a value that\nis no type leaves the cell <code>text</code>.\nPS! sorting, grouping and filtering still use the field&#39;s own type</p>\n","samples":["dynamic-cell-types"]},{"name":"focusButton","signatures":["focusButton?: \"SHOW_IF_GRID_NOT_READONLY\" | \"SHOW_IF_GRID_AND_CELL_NOT_READONLY\" | \"ALWAYS\""],"doc":"<p>shows a <code>...</code> button at the right of the cell while it has focus; clicking it, or Space in the cell,\nsends the <code>cell-focus-button-click</code> event - open a dialog or a dropdown from there. When it is\nshown: <code>&#39;SHOW_IF_GRID_NOT_READONLY&#39;</code> the grid is editable, <code>&#39;SHOW_IF_GRID_AND_CELL_NOT_READONLY&#39;</code>\nthe grid and the cell are editable, <code>&#39;ALWAYS&#39;</code> always. Not on a boolean (checkbox) cell</p>\n","samples":["dropdown-grid"]},{"name":"label","signatures":["label?: string"],"doc":"<p>the column&#39;s header text. Left out, the label of the datasource field (<code>FieldConfig.label</code>) is\nused, and without that the field name prettified (<code>first_name</code> is <code>First Name</code>). The grid shows\nthe same label everywhere: header, column chooser, group chip, filter editor, footer filter</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"numberOverride","signatures":["numberOverride?: \"ZERO_TO_BLANK\" | \"BLANK_TO_ZERO\""],"doc":"<p>for a number field, what a cell shows - the value is not changed: <code>&#39;ZERO_TO_BLANK&#39;</code> shows 0 as an\nempty cell, <code>&#39;BLANK_TO_ZERO&#39;</code> shows an empty value as <code>0</code>. Default: the value as the formatter\nshows it</p>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"operator","signatures":["operator?: FilterOperator"],"doc":"<p>the operator the column&#39;s header filter starts with. Default <code>&#39;GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO&#39;</code> for\nnumber and date fields, <code>&#39;EQUAL&#39;</code> for the rest. For text <code>&#39;EQUAL&#39;</code> is the whole text, ignoring\ncase: <code>ann</code> finds <code>Ann</code>, not <code>Anna</code>. Set <code>&#39;CONTAINS&#39;</code> for a search anywhere in the text,\n<code>&#39;BEGIN_WITH&#39;</code> for the start. The operator the user picks in the header filter&#39;s menu is state:\n<code>GridState.headerFilters[field].operator</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: { name: { operator: 'CONTAINS' } }, // `ann` finds Ann, Anna and Joanna\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["filter-operator-header"]},{"name":"placeholderFilter","signatures":["placeholderFilter?: string"],"doc":"<p>shown in the empty header filter. Default: the formatter&#39;s placeholder (date fields), else the field&#39;s type: <code>Text</code> or <code>Number</code> (texts <code>filter.placeholder.*</code>)</p>\n","samples":["required-placeholders"]},{"name":"placeholderRow","signatures":["placeholderRow?: string"],"doc":"<p>shown in an empty cell, see <code>GridConfig.placeholderRowCurrentEntityOnly</code></p>\n","samples":["required-placeholders"]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>makes the column&#39;s cells readonly while the grid is editable (<code>GridConfig.readonly: false</code>). The\ngrid draws red stripes behind them. The <code>isReadonly</code> hook (<a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>) can decide per row\ninstead</p>\n","samples":[]}]}]},{"name":"Conflict","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type Conflict<T = any> = ValueConflict<T> | RemovedConflict<T>"],"doc":"<p>What <code>datasource.getConflicts()</code> lists: a server value that <code>upsert()</code> did not write because the user\nchanged the same thing. Tell the two kinds apart by <code>field</code>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><a href=\"#api/ValueConflict\">ValueConflict</a> (<code>field</code> is the field&#39;s name): the server changed a field the user has\nedited. The user&#39;s value stays, the server&#39;s is the original now</li>\n<li><a href=\"#api/RemovedConflict\">RemovedConflict</a> (<code>field</code> is <code>null</code>): the server no longer has a row that has local\nchanges, <code>upsert(rows, { removeMissing: true })</code> kept it</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Resolve one with <code>datasource.resolveConflict(row, field, &#39;local&#39; | &#39;remote&#39;)</code>. A conflict also goes\nwhen what it is about goes: the field is not edited any more (reverted, undone, typed back to the\nserver&#39;s value, saved with <code>acceptChanges()</code>), the row has no local changes any more, or it leaves\nthe data.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of the rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>for (const conflict of datasource.getConflicts()) {\n    if (conflict.field === null) {\n        console.log(`row ${conflict.row.__KEY} was removed on the server, it has changes here`);\n    } else {\n        console.log(`${conflict.field}: yours ${conflict.local}, the server's ${conflict.remote}`);\n    }\n}</code></pre>\n","samples":["live-data"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"CsvSeparator","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type CsvSeparator = \",\" | \";\" | \"\\t\""],"doc":"<p>The separators <a href=\"#api/CsvOptions\">CsvOptions</a> can use: <code>&#39;,&#39;</code> (RFC 4180), <code>&#39;;&#39;</code> (what Excel expects in a locale\nwith a decimal comma, Norwegian for one) and <code>&#39;\\t&#39;</code> (tab separated text).</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"EntityUnion","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type EntityUnion<T> = Entity & T"],"doc":"<p>A data row as the datasource hands it out: your object <code>T</code> and the fields of an <a href=\"#api/Entity\">Entity</a> - the\nkey, the row state, the error and the edit tracking controller. <code>getDataRows()</code>, <code>getSelectedRows()</code>,\n<code>getAllData()</code> ... return these.</p>\n<p>The row is your own object, wrapped in a <code>Proxy</code> that tracks the edits: setting a field on it is an\nedit (<code>getChanges()</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>T</code> the type of your rows, the <code>T</code> of <code>Datasource&lt;T&gt;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type EntityUnion } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n}\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id' });\ndatasource.setData([{ id: 1, name: 'Ann' }]);\nconst ann: EntityUnion&lt;Person&gt; = datasource.getDataRows()[0];\nann.name; // 'Ann'\nann.__rowState; // undefined: not edited</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"EventHandler","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type EventHandler<Payload> = (data: Payload) => void"],"doc":"<p>A handler for one event: it gets the event&#39;s payload. What it returns is ignored, a handler\nstays subscribed until you call the function <code>on()</code> returned.</p>\n<p>Only needed when you write a handler on its own, before passing it to <code>on()</code>.\nThe payload type comes from the event map: <a href=\"#api/DatasourceEvents\">DatasourceEvents</a>, <a href=\"#api/GridEvents\">GridEvents</a>,\n<a href=\"#api/DateEvents\">DateEvents</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Type parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>Payload</code> the payload of the event, e.g. <code>DatasourceEvents[&#39;select&#39;]</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { DatasourceEvents, EventHandler } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst onSelect: EventHandler&lt;DatasourceEvents['select']&gt; = (data) =&gt; {\n    console.log('row', data.row, 'selected by', data.info);\n};\nconst off = datasource.on('select', onSelect);</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"FieldType","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type FieldType = \"text\" | \"number\" | \"boolean\" | \"date\" | \"datetime\""],"doc":"<p>The type of a field. It decides how the datasource sorts, groups and filters the field, which\nformatter it gets by default, and how the grid shows and edits it.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>type</th>\n<th>value</th>\n<th>sorts / filters</th>\n<th>default formatter</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;text&#39;</code></td>\n<td>string</td>\n<td>as text</td>\n<td><code>&#39;text&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/TextFormatter\">TextFormatter</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;number&#39;</code></td>\n<td>number</td>\n<td>as numbers</td>\n<td><code>&#39;numberDot&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/NumberFormatterDot\">NumberFormatterDot</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;boolean&#39;</code></td>\n<td>boolean</td>\n<td>true / false</td>\n<td><code>&#39;boolean&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/BooleanFormatter\">BooleanFormatter</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;date&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>Date</code></td>\n<td>on the day, the time of day is ignored</td>\n<td><code>&#39;dateYYYYMMDD&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/DateFormatterYYYYMMDD\">DateFormatterYYYYMMDD</a></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;datetime&#39;</code></td>\n<td><code>Date</code></td>\n<td>on the full timestamp</td>\n<td><code>&#39;datetimeYYYYMMDD&#39;</code>, <a href=\"#api/DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS\">DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS</a></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>A field that is not listed in <code>fields</code> is <code>&#39;text&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: {\n        age: 'number',\n        born: 'date', // 1990-05-17, filters match the whole day\n        lastLogin: 'datetime', // 2026-11-20T08:15:00\n        active: 'boolean'\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"FilterExpression","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type FilterExpression = FilterGroup | FilterCondition"],"doc":"<p>A filter: one <a href=\"#api/FilterCondition\">FilterCondition</a>, or a <a href=\"#api/FilterGroup\">FilterGroup</a> of them. This is what\n<code>datasource.filter()</code> takes, <code>datasource.getFilter()</code> returns and the grid keeps in its state\n(<code>GridState.filter</code>). It is plain data, so it can be stored as JSON (a <code>Date</code> value comes back as\ntext, which a <code>date</code> / <code>datetime</code> field still reads).</p>\n<p>Build one with <a href=\"#api/and\">and</a>, <a href=\"#api/or\">or</a> and <a href=\"#api/where\">where</a>, or write the objects out.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// a single condition\ndatasource.filter(where('balance', 'GREATER_THAN', 2500));\n\n// age &gt; 18 AND (a = 'x' OR a = 'y')\ndatasource.filter(and(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18), or(where('a', 'EQUAL', 'x'), where('a', 'EQUAL', 'y'))));\n\n// no filter\ndatasource.filter(null);</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"FilterNode","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type FilterNode = FilterConditionNode | FilterGroupNode"],"doc":"<p>A node of the tree <code>datasource.getFilterTree()</code> returns: a <a href=\"#api/FilterGroupNode\">FilterGroupNode</a> or a\n<a href=\"#api/FilterConditionNode\">FilterConditionNode</a>. Tell them apart by <code>kind</code>.</p>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"FilterOperator","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type FilterOperator = \"EQUAL\" | \"LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"LESS_THAN\" | \"GREATER_THAN\" | \"CONTAINS\" | \"NOT_EQUAL_TO\" | \"DOES_NOT_CONTAIN\" | \"BEGIN_WITH\" | \"END_WITH\" | \"IN\" | \"NOT_IN\" | \"IS_BLANK\" | \"IS_NOT_BLANK\""],"doc":"<p>How a <a href=\"#api/FilterCondition\">FilterCondition</a> compares the row&#39;s value with its <code>value</code>. The field&#39;s type (from\nthe datasource&#39;s <code>fields</code>, <code>&#39;text&#39;</code> when it is not listed) decides how the two are compared.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>EQUAL</code> - text: the same, ignoring case - the whole text, <code>&#39;an&#39;</code> does not match <code>&#39;Ann&#39;</code> (use a\nwildcard, <code>&#39;an*&#39;</code>, or <code>CONTAINS</code>). Number: the same. <code>date</code>: the same day, <code>datetime</code>: the same second</li>\n<li><code>NOT_EQUAL_TO</code> - the opposite of <code>EQUAL</code></li>\n<li><code>LESS_THAN</code> - number and date: smaller / earlier. Text: compared as lower case text</li>\n<li><code>LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code> - <code>LESS_THAN</code> or <code>EQUAL</code></li>\n<li><code>GREATER_THAN</code> - number and date: larger / later. Text: compared as lower case text</li>\n<li><code>GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code> - <code>GREATER_THAN</code> or <code>EQUAL</code></li>\n<li><code>CONTAINS</code> - text: has the value somewhere in it, ignoring case. Number and date: <code>GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code></li>\n<li><code>DOES_NOT_CONTAIN</code> - text: does not have the value in it, ignoring case. Number and date: <code>LESS_THAN</code></li>\n<li><code>BEGIN_WITH</code> - text: starts with the value, ignoring case. Number and date: <code>GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code></li>\n<li><code>END_WITH</code> - text: ends with the value, ignoring case. Number and date: <code>LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO</code></li>\n<li><code>IN</code> - one of a list: <code>value</code> is an array (or text with one value per line), compared as upper case text. Number and date fields compare their formatted text. <code>&#39;NULL&#39;</code> in the list matches a blank</li>\n<li><code>NOT_IN</code> - the opposite of <code>IN</code></li>\n<li><code>IS_BLANK</code> - the row value is null, undefined, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> or 0 (or an invalid Date, in a date field). Takes no <code>value</code></li>\n<li><code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code> - the opposite of <code>IS_BLANK</code>. Takes no <code>value</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>In a text value <code>*</code> and <code>%</code> are wildcards: <code>where(&#39;name&#39;, &#39;EQUAL&#39;, &#39;per*2&#39;)</code> matches <code>person2</code>.\nA blank row date (null, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>, an invalid Date) is never before, after or on a date: of the\ncomparisons it only matches <code>NOT_EQUAL_TO</code>. A <code>boolean</code> field compares every operator as <code>EQUAL</code>,\napart from <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> and the blank ones.</p>\n<p><strong>0 is blank.</strong> A row value of 0 counts as blank, on purpose: in ERP style data 0 and empty mean\nthe same. <code>IS_BLANK</code> matches a 0 (the number, in any field - the text <code>&#39;0&#39;</code> is not blank) and\n<code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code> leaves it out, and the header&#39;s value list (shown for text fields) puts a 0 under its\n&quot;Blank&quot; entry. <code>IN</code> / <code>NOT_IN</code> take a 0 in a text field as <code>&#39;NULL&#39;</code>; a number field compares its\nformatted text there, <code>&#39;0&#39;</code>. The other way round, a blank row value of\na number field compares as 0: <code>where(&#39;age&#39;, &#39;LESS_THAN&#39;, 5)</code> matches the rows without an age.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndatasource.filter(where('age', 'GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO', 18));\ndatasource.filter(where('name', 'CONTAINS', 'son'));\ndatasource.filter(where('country', 'IN', ['Norway', 'Sweden']));\ndatasource.filter(where('email', 'IS_BLANK'));</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"GridConfig","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type GridConfig"],"doc":"<p>The grid&#39;s config: the options of each column (<code>columns</code>), where the columns go (<code>layout</code>), sizes\nand behaviour. It is what you write. What the user changes while working with the grid - column\norder and widths, sorting, grouping, filters - is the <a href=\"#api/GridState\">GridState</a>: read it with\n<code>gridInterface.getState()</code>, set it with <code>setState()</code>, and give the state the grid starts in as\n<code>initialState</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>It is plain JSON</strong>: no functions, so it can be stored - in a backend, say - and given back as it\nis. The functions of a grid (<code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code>, <code>menus</code>) are <a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>, given next\nto the config: <code>createGrid(host, { config, datasource, hooks })</code>. A <code>Date</code> in <code>initialState</code>&#39;s\nfilter is the one value that does not survive JSON as it was: it comes back as its ISO text, see\n<a href=\"#api/GridState\">GridState</a>.</p>\n<p>To change an option while the grid is shown, use <code>gridInterface.updateConfig()</code>.</p>\n<p>The grid does not change the object you pass in: it keeps its own copy of <code>columns</code>, <code>layout</code> and\n<code>initialState</code>, the parts it changes while the user works.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, Datasource, type GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { name: { validate: ['required'] }, age: 'number', born: 'date' } });\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    columns: {\n        name: { label: 'Name', placeholderFilter: 'search' },\n        age: { readonly: true }\n        // born is in the layout without an entry here: it gets the defaults\n    },\n    layout: {\n        left: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }], // pinned left\n        center: [{ fields: ['age', 'born'], width: 100 }] // two fields stacked in one column\n    },\n    cellHeight: 22,\n    readonly: false,\n    initialState: { sorting: [{ attribute: 'name', ascending: true }] }\n};\n\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(document.getElementById('grid')!, { config, datasource });</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid","column-layout"],"memberGroups":[{"title":"Properties","members":[{"name":"autoRemoveContextMenuOnScrollEvent","signatures":["autoRemoveContextMenuOnScrollEvent?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>closes the open menu (the right click menus, <code>openMenu()</code>, the date picker ...) when the grid is\nscrolled, default false. Leave it off where scrolling happens by accident, on a small touch screen</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cellHeaderLabelHeight","signatures":["cellHeaderLabelHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of a header label cell in px, default <code>cellHeight</code>. Make it 2-3 times <code>cellHeight</code> for long\nlabels that wrap. <code>autoResizeColumns()</code> measures the label on one line</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"cellHeight","signatures":["cellHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of a cell in px, default 22</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"columns","signatures":["columns?: Record<string, ColumnConfig>"],"doc":"<p>The options of each column, keyed by the field name. A field in the <code>layout</code> without an entry\nhere gets the defaults. A field with an entry that is not in the layout is not shown, but the\nuser can add it from the column chooser.</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"datePickerConfig","signatures":["datePickerConfig?: Partial<IDateConfig>"],"doc":"<p>the date picker of date cells and date header filters: only the fields to change. Of the\n<a href=\"#api/IDateConfig\">IDateConfig</a> the grid reads <code>showWeek</code> (default true), <code>isoWeek</code> (true), <code>weekStart</code> (1,\nmonday), <code>rowHeight</code> (22), <code>monthWidth</code> (230), <code>monthMargin</code> (10), <code>hideDimmedDates</code> (false),\n<code>showYearInMonth</code> (false) and <code>datepickerHeight</code> (317), and sets the rest itself. Its texts - the\nnames of the months and days, the buttons - are the grid&#39;s <code>texts</code> (<code>datePicker.*</code>)</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['born'], width: 120 }] },\n    datePickerConfig: { weekStart: 0, isoWeek: false } // weeks from sunday, the rest the defaults\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"dimRepeatedValues","signatures":["dimRepeatedValues?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>dims a cell when it repeats the value of the row above, so only the first row of a\nrun of equal values reads at full strength. Default = false.</p>\n<p>A cell always shows at full strength again at the start of a group, and blanks are\nnever dimmed. Can be toggled from the row context menu.</p>\n","samples":["misc-options"]},{"name":"editedMarker","signatures":["editedMarker?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows a marker in the top left corner of an edited cell, default <code>true</code>: a small triangle on a\ncell whose value differs from its original value (the datasource tracks it per field, see\n<code>getChanges()</code>). Not on a new row, every cell of it is new. Its tooltip shows the original\nvalue, and a click on it puts the original value back (<code>datasource.resetField()</code>, a step of the\nundo history) - in an editable grid.</p>\n<p><code>false</code> shows no marker. The cell element has the class <code>simple-html-cell-edited</code> either way,\nfor a look of your own. The colour is <code>--simple-html-grid-edited-color</code></p>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"footerHeight","signatures":["footerHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of the footer in px, default 45</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"groupAggregates","signatures":["groupAggregates?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the aggregate of each column that has one (<code>ColumnConfig.aggregate</code>) in the group rows,\ndefault <code>true</code>: in the column&#39;s place, over the group&#39;s rows - the rows of its sub groups and\nof collapsed groups included. The group&#39;s name stays at the left, over the first columns.</p>\n<p>A group row is one line high; when an aggregated field is not the first of a column with\nstacked fields, the group rows get as many lines as it takes to show it on its own line.\n<code>false</code> shows the name only, as without aggregates</p>\n","samples":["aggregates"]},{"name":"hideFilter","signatures":["hideFilter?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>hides the row of header filters, default false</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"hideLabels","signatures":["hideLabels?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>hides the row of header labels (the column names, click to sort), default false</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"initialState","signatures":["initialState?: Partial<GridState>"],"doc":"<p>The state the grid starts in, and <code>resetState()</code> goes back to: sorted, grouped, filtered ...\nWhat is left out starts empty (no sorting, no filter ...), the layout is <code>layout</code>.</p>\n<p>The grid applies it to the datasource when it is made: a filter, sort or grouping set on the\ndatasource before is replaced, and cleared when <code>initialState</code> leaves it out.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridConfig, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 100 }, { fields: ['age'], width: 100 }] },\n    initialState: {\n        sorting: [{ attribute: 'age', ascending: false }],\n        filter: where('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18),\n        headerFilters: { age: { value: 18, operator: 'GREATER_THAN' } } // what the header shows\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["grid-state"]},{"name":"layout","signatures":["layout: GridLayout"],"doc":"<p>Where the columns go: pinned left, the scrolling center and pinned right. It is the layout the\ngrid starts with (unless <code>initialState.layout</code> is given) and <code>resetState()</code> goes back to. The\nuser changes it - drag/drop, pinning, the column chooser, resizing - those changes are in\n<code>getState().layout</code>.</p>\n","samples":["column-layout"]},{"name":"panelHeight","signatures":["panelHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of the top panel (grouping) in px, default 25</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"placeholderRowCurrentEntityOnly","signatures":["placeholderRowCurrentEntityOnly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows a column&#39;s <code>placeholderRow</code> on the current row (the current entity) only.\ndefault = true, so you need to set this to false to display on all rows</p>\n","samples":["required-placeholders"]},{"name":"readonly","signatures":["readonly?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>the whole grid is readonly, default <code>true</code>: no cell can be edited, and the row menu has no paste\nor clear. Set <code>false</code> to edit; the column&#39;s <code>readonly</code> and the <code>isReadonly</code> hook\n(<a href=\"#api/GridHooks\">GridHooks</a>) can still make cells readonly</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"rowStatus","signatures":["rowStatus?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the state of each row on its row number, default <code>true</code>: an icon for a new row (+), an\nedited row (a pencil), a row marked for deletion (a trash can, the row number and the text of\nits cells struck through) and a row with an error (!, with the red bar). The tooltip and a\nscreen reader get the state as text. One icon: deleted wins, then an error, then new or edited.\nThe row numbers are a little wider, to make room for the icon.</p>\n<p><code>false</code> shows the plain row number. The classes <code>row-is-new</code>, <code>row-is-modified</code> and\n<code>row-is-deleted</code> around the number, and the error bar (<code>simple-html-row-error</code>), are there\neither way - for a look of your own. The colours are the theme&#39;s variables\n(<code>--simple-html-grid-new-color</code> ...), see the theming guide</p>\n","samples":["editing"]},{"name":"selectSizeHeight","signatures":["selectSizeHeight?: number"],"doc":"<p>height of the column selector row under the header filters in px, default 18</p>\n","samples":[]},{"name":"texts","signatures":["texts?: Texts"],"doc":"<p>The texts of this grid, by id: the ones to change. They win over the texts of the page\n(<a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a>), which win over the defaults (<a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>, English). Plain JSON.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Every text the grid shows: the menus, the filter editor, the column chooser, the footer, the\ntooltips (ids ending with <code>.tooltip</code>) and the date picker. Not the texts the datasource makes -\nthe validation messages, <code>getFilterString()</code> and the name of the group of blank values: they are\nset with <code>setTexts()</code> only.</li>\n<li><code>updateConfig({ texts })</code> replaces them as a whole, and rebuilds the grid. A menu or the filter\neditor shows them the next time it opens.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For one language on the whole page, <code>setTexts()</code> is enough: this is for a grid that differs.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }] },\n    texts: {\n        'row.copy': 'Kopier:',\n        'filterEditor.addCondition.tooltip': 'Legg til betingelse'\n    }\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["translation"]},{"name":"tooltips","signatures":["tooltips?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>renders the built in tooltip, default = true: on the buttons and icons of the filter editor,\nand the validation messages on a cell with an error and on its row selector</p>\n<p>the <code>data-tooltip</code> attribute is always written to the elements, also when this is\nfalse, so you can hook up your own tooltip library instead. The texts of the tooltips are\ntexts like the others, their ids end with <code>.tooltip</code>: see <code>texts</code></p>\n","samples":["tooltips","validation"]},{"name":"totalsRow","signatures":["totalsRow?: boolean"],"doc":"<p>shows the totals row under the rows, default <code>false</code>: the aggregate of each column that has one\n(<code>ColumnConfig.aggregate</code>), over the rows the filter lets through - when grouped, the rows of\ncollapsed groups too. &quot;Total&quot; at the left (the text <code>aggregate.total</code>). It follows the columns\nwhen they scroll sideways, and the values follow the filter and every change of a row: an edit,\nundo, <code>upsert()</code>. The horizontal scrollbar is between the rows and the totals row</p>\n","samples":["aggregates"]}]}]},{"name":"MenuEntry","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type MenuEntry = MenuItem | MenuSection | MenuSeparator | MenuBlock"],"doc":"<p>One entry of a menu: an item to click, a section header, a separator line, or a block (an element\nshown as it is). The grid&#39;s own menus are lists of these, see <a href=\"#api/GridMenus\">GridMenus</a> to change them, and\n<code>gridInterface.openMenu()</code> opens a menu of your own.</p>\n<p>Every entry has an <code>id</code>. The ids of the grid&#39;s own entries are listed in <a href=\"#api/MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a>; give\nyours ids that do not clash with them.</p>\n<p>An entry with a <code>visible</code> callback that returns <code>false</code> is left out. A section header or separator\nis shown as long as it is in the list: hide it together with the entries under it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { MenuEntry } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const pick: (fruit: string | null) =&gt; void;\ndeclare const event: MouseEvent;\n\nconst entries: MenuEntry[] = [\n    { type: 'section', id: 'fruit', label: 'Pick a fruit:' },\n    { id: 'fruit.apple', label: 'Apple', action: () =&gt; pick('Apple') },\n    { id: 'fruit.banana', label: 'Banana', action: () =&gt; pick('Banana') },\n    { type: 'separator', id: 'fruit.separator' },\n    { id: 'fruit.none', label: 'None', hint: 'clears the cell', action: () =&gt; pick(null) }\n];\ngridInterface.openMenu(event, entries);</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ModifiedEntity","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ModifiedEntity<T> = Partial<T> & { __KEY?: string | number }"],"doc":"<p>One edited row in <a href=\"#api/Changes\">Changes</a>: the row&#39;s key and the fields whose value differs from the\noriginal, with their new value.</p>\n<p>The key is under the name of the key field (<code>id</code> with <code>new Datasource({ key: &#39;id&#39; })</code>), or under\n<code>__KEY</code> when the datasource has no key - then it is a generated negative number, a server can not\nuse it.</p>\n<p>A field edited back to its original value is not in it, and a row with no field left that\ndiffers is not edited. When a value differs depends on the field&#39;s type, see <a href=\"#api/Changes\">Changes</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ninterface Person {\n    id: number;\n    name: string;\n    city: string;\n}\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource&lt;Person&gt;({ key: 'id' });\ndatasource.setData([{ id: 7, name: 'Ann', city: 'Oslo' }]);\ndatasource.getDataRows()[0].city = 'Bergen';\n\ndatasource.getChanges().modifiedEntities; // [{ id: 7, city: 'Bergen' }]</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"SelectionMode","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type SelectionMode = \"none\" | \"single\" | \"multiple\""],"doc":"<p>How rows can be selected:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code> - many rows: ctrl+click adds a row, shift+click a range (the default)</li>\n<li><code>&#39;single&#39;</code> - one row at a time</li>\n<li><code>&#39;none&#39;</code> - no selection. Clicking a row still makes it the current entity</li>\n</ul>\n<p><code>selectAll()</code> (and a click on the grid&#39;s top left corner) selects only in <code>&#39;multiple&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p>The datasource owns it: set it with <code>DatasourceOptions.selectionMode</code> or\n<code>datasource.setSelectionMode()</code>. A grid reads it from its datasource, it has no option of its own\n(v5&#39;s <code>GridConfig.selectionMode</code> is removed).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ key: 'id', selectionMode: 'single' });\ndatasource.setSelectionMode('none'); // later, also while it is shown in a grid</code></pre>\n","samples":["selection"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"TextId","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type TextId = \"row.copy\" | \"row.copy.cell\" | \"row.copy.column\" | \"row.copy.column.hint\" | \"row.copy.row\" | \"row.copy.row.hint\" | \"row.copy.selectedColumns\" | \"row.copy.selectedColumns.hint\" | \"row.copy.range\" | \"row.filter\" | \"row.filter.replace\" | \"row.filter.replace.hint\" | \"row.filter.add\" | \"row.filter.add.hint\" | \"row.view\" | \"row.view.dimRepeatedValues\" | \"row.view.changedOnly\" | \"row.paste\" | \"row.paste.cell\" | \"row.paste.cell.hint\" | \"row.paste.range\" | \"row.clear\" | \"row.clear.cell\" | \"row.clear.cell.hint\" | \"row.clear.range\" | \"row.delete\" | \"row.delete.rows\" | \"row.delete.rows.hint\" | \"row.delete.undo\" | \"row.delete.undo.hint\" | \"row.edit\" | \"row.edit.undo\" | \"row.edit.undo.hint\" | \"row.edit.redo\" | \"row.edit.redo.hint\" | \"row.edit.revertCell\" | \"row.edit.revertRow\" | \"row.edit.revertRows\" | \"row.edit.revertRows.hint\" | \"row.summary\" | \"row.summary.count\" | \"row.summary.sum\" | \"row.summary.max\" | \"row.summary.min\" | \"row.summary.avg\" | \"row.export\" | \"row.export.csv\" | \"row.export.csvSelected\" | \"header.column\" | \"header.column.pinLeft\" | \"header.column.pinLeftCopy\" | \"header.column.pinRight\" | \"header.column.pinRightCopy\" | \"header.column.unpin\" | \"header.column.hide\" | \"header.column.removeSorting\" | \"header.column.chooser\" | \"header.size\" | \"header.size.column\" | \"header.size.all\" | \"header.grouping\" | \"header.grouping.expandAll\" | \"header.grouping.collapseAll\" | \"header.grouping.clear\" | \"filter.filter\" | \"filter.filter.clear\" | \"filter.filter.clearAll\" | \"filter.filter.isBlank\" | \"filter.filter.isNotBlank\" | \"filter.filter.advanced\" | \"filter.operator\" | \"filter.operator.greaterThanOrEqualTo\" | \"filter.operator.lessThanOrEqualTo\" | \"filter.operator.equal\" | \"filter.operator.notEqualTo\" | \"filter.operator.contains\" | \"filter.values.search\" | \"filter.values.searchPlaceholder\" | \"filter.values.availableOnly\" | \"filter.values.rowsFound\" | \"filter.values.truncated\" | \"filter.values.selectAll\" | \"filter.values.blank\" | \"filter.values.run\" | \"columnChooser.title\" | \"columnChooser.search\" | \"columnChooser.close\" | \"filterEditor.title\" | \"filterEditor.title.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.close.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.operatorAnd\" | \"filterEditor.operatorAnd.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.operatorOr\" | \"filterEditor.operatorOr.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.wrapGroup.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.addSubGroup.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.addCondition.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.deleteGroup.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.clearAll.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.label.field\" | \"filterEditor.label.operator\" | \"filterEditor.label.value\" | \"filterEditor.pickAttribute\" | \"filterEditor.pickAttribute.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.pickOperator\" | \"filterEditor.pickOperator.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.pickValueAttribute\" | \"filterEditor.pickValueAttribute.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.deleteCondition.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.useValue.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.useAttribute.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.filterAndClose\" | \"filterEditor.filterAndClose.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.filterOnly\" | \"filterEditor.filterOnly.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.closeButton\" | \"filterEditor.closeButton.tooltip\" | \"filterEditor.fieldMenu\" | \"filterEditor.fieldMenu.search\" | \"filterEditor.operatorMenu\" | \"filterEditor.operator.EQUAL\" | \"filterEditor.operator.LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"filterEditor.operator.GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"filterEditor.operator.LESS_THAN\" | \"filterEditor.operator.GREATER_THAN\" | \"filterEditor.operator.CONTAINS\" | \"filterEditor.operator.NOT_EQUAL_TO\" | \"filterEditor.operator.DOES_NOT_CONTAIN\" | \"filterEditor.operator.BEGIN_WITH\" | \"filterEditor.operator.END_WITH\" | \"filterEditor.operator.IN\" | \"filterEditor.operator.NOT_IN\" | \"filterEditor.operator.IS_BLANK\" | \"filterEditor.operator.IS_NOT_BLANK\" | \"footer.rowCount\" | \"footer.clear\" | \"footer.clear.tooltip\" | \"footer.filter.tooltip\" | \"footer.collapsed.one\" | \"footer.collapsed.other\" | \"footer.and\" | \"footer.or\" | \"footer.changedOnly\" | \"footer.operator.EQUAL\" | \"footer.operator.LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"footer.operator.GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"footer.operator.LESS_THAN\" | \"footer.operator.GREATER_THAN\" | \"footer.operator.CONTAINS\" | \"footer.operator.NOT_EQUAL_TO\" | \"footer.operator.DOES_NOT_CONTAIN\" | \"footer.operator.BEGIN_WITH\" | \"footer.operator.END_WITH\" | \"footer.operator.IN\" | \"footer.operator.NOT_IN\" | \"footer.operator.IS_BLANK\" | \"footer.operator.IS_NOT_BLANK\" | \"aggregate.sum\" | \"aggregate.avg\" | \"aggregate.min\" | \"aggregate.max\" | \"aggregate.count\" | \"aggregate.total\" | \"filter.placeholder.text\" | \"filter.placeholder.number\" | \"grid.label\" | \"grid.rowSelector\" | \"grid.filter\" | \"grid.groupToggle\" | \"grid.removeGroup\" | \"rowStatus.new\" | \"rowStatus.edited\" | \"rowStatus.deleted\" | \"rowStatus.error\" | \"cell.editedMarker.tooltip\" | \"cell.editedMarker.blank\" | \"cell.editedMarker.revert\" | \"cell.multiline.more\" | \"cell.multiline.hint\" | \"cell.multiline.hintReadonly\" | \"datePicker.hours\" | \"datePicker.minutes\" | \"datePicker.week\" | \"datePicker.clear\" | \"datePicker.now\" | \"datePicker.use\" | \"datePicker.month.january\" | \"datePicker.month.february\" | \"datePicker.month.march\" | \"datePicker.month.april\" | \"datePicker.month.may\" | \"datePicker.month.june\" | \"datePicker.month.july\" | \"datePicker.month.august\" | \"datePicker.month.september\" | \"datePicker.month.october\" | \"datePicker.month.november\" | \"datePicker.month.december\" | \"datePicker.day.sunday\" | \"datePicker.day.monday\" | \"datePicker.day.tuesday\" | \"datePicker.day.wednesday\" | \"datePicker.day.thursday\" | \"datePicker.day.friday\" | \"datePicker.day.saturday\" | \"validation.required\" | \"validation.min\" | \"validation.max\" | \"validation.minLength\" | \"validation.maxLength\" | \"validation.pattern\" | \"filterString.and\" | \"filterString.or\" | \"filterString.operator.EQUAL\" | \"filterString.operator.LESS_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"filterString.operator.GREATER_THAN_OR_EQUAL_TO\" | \"filterString.operator.LESS_THAN\" | \"filterString.operator.GREATER_THAN\" | \"filterString.operator.CONTAINS\" | \"filterString.operator.NOT_EQUAL_TO\" | \"filterString.operator.DOES_NOT_CONTAIN\" | \"filterString.operator.BEGIN_WITH\" | \"filterString.operator.END_WITH\" | \"filterString.operator.IN\" | \"filterString.operator.NOT_IN\" | \"filterString.operator.IS_BLANK\" | \"filterString.operator.IS_NOT_BLANK\" | \"grouping.blank\""],"doc":"<p>The id of a text of the grid or the datasource: a key of <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>, e.g. <code>&#39;row.copy&#39;</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { TextId } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst id: TextId = 'filterEditor.title';</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"Texts","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type Texts = { [id in TextId]?: string } & { [id: string]: string }"],"doc":"<p>Texts by id, for <a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a> and <code>GridConfig.texts</code>: plain JSON, a text for each id to\nchange. An id left out shows the text it had: the one set with <code>setTexts()</code>, else the default in\n<a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>.</p>\n<p>The ids of <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a> are suggested by the editor. An id of your own is allowed too: a validator\n(or a rule&#39;s <code>message</code>) can give an id, and its text is looked up the same way - see\n<a href=\"#api/registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>.</p>\n<p><code>{name}</code> in a text is filled in when it is shown: <code>&#39;Count: {count}&#39;</code>. Keep the names of the\ndefault text, a name the text does not use is not shown.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { Texts } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst norwegian: Texts = {\n    'row.copy': 'Kopier:',\n    'row.summary.count': 'Antall: {count}',\n    'validation.required': 'Må fylles ut',\n    'validation.phoneNO': 'Må være 8 siffer' // an id of your own, returned by a validator\n};</code></pre>\n","samples":["translation"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ValidationOption","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ValidationOption = string | number | boolean | null | ValidationOption[] | { [key: string]: ValidationOption }"],"doc":"<p>The value of an option of a <a href=\"#api/ValidationRuleObject\">ValidationRuleObject</a>: plain JSON - text, a number, <code>true</code> /\n<code>false</code>, <code>null</code>, or a list or an object of them. So the rules can be stored, e.g. in a backend.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import type { ValidationOption } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst values: ValidationOption = ['Norway', 'Sweden'];</code></pre>\n","samples":[],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"ValidationRule","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type ValidationRule = string | ValidationRuleObject"],"doc":"<p>A validation rule of a field, in <code>FieldConfig.validate</code>: the id of a validator as text, for a rule\nwithout options (<code>&#39;required&#39;</code>), or a <a href=\"#api/ValidationRuleObject\">ValidationRuleObject</a> with the options\n(<code>{ id: &#39;min&#39;, value: 0 }</code>).</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type ValidationRule } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst ageRules: ValidationRule[] = ['required', { id: 'min', value: 0 }, { id: 'max', value: 150, message: 'too old' }];\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { age: { type: 'number', validate: ageRules } } });</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"Validator","group":"Type Aliases","kind":"Type Alias","signatures":["type Validator = (value: unknown, row: Entity, rule: ValidationRuleObject) => string | null"],"doc":"<p>Checks one value of a field: returns <code>null</code> when the value is valid (<code>&#39;&#39;</code> counts as valid too),\nelse the error. Register it under an id with <a href=\"#api/registerValidator\">registerValidator</a>, and name it in a field&#39;s\nrules.</p>\n<p>The error is a text id - a <code>validation.*</code> id of <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>, like the built-ins return, or an id\nof your own given a text with <code>setTexts()</code> - or the message itself. The rule&#39;s own <code>message</code> is used\ninstead when it has one, and <code>{name}</code> in the message is replaced by the rule&#39;s option <code>name</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>value</code> - the field&#39;s value in the row</li>\n<li><code>row</code> - the row, to compare with its other fields. Such a validator runs when its own field is\nedited, and on <code>validate()</code></li>\n<li><code>rule</code> - the rule written out, with its options: <code>{ id, ...options, message? }</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p>A blank value (<code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>) should pass, the way the built-ins other than\n<code>required</code> do: an optional field can be empty, the <code>required</code> rule makes it fail. Do not use\n<code>this</code>, keep it fast (it runs on every key the user types), and do not change the row.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { registerValidator, type Validator } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// { id: 'oneOf', values: ['Norway', 'Sweden'] }\nconst oneOf: Validator = (value, _row, rule) =&gt; {\n    if (value === null || value === undefined || value === '') {\n        return null; // an empty value is the required rule's job\n    }\n    return Array.isArray(rule.values) &amp;&amp; rule.values.includes(String(value)) ? null : 'Must be one of {values}';\n};\nregisterValidator('oneOf', oneOf);</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"BooleanFormatter","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const BooleanFormatter: { format: any; parse: any }"],"doc":"<p>Formatter for booleans, the default for <code>boolean</code> fields. Registered as <code>&#39;boolean&#39;</code>, the options\nname it by that id (see <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>). The grid shows a boolean field as a\ncheckbox from the raw value, this formatter is for the places that show it as text: the filter\nstring, group headers, and a value pasted into the column.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> - <code>true</code> -&gt; <code>&#39;true&#39;</code>, <code>false</code> -&gt; <code>&#39;false&#39;</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for null and undefined</li>\n<li><code>parse</code> / <code>parseFilter</code> - <code>&#39;true&#39;</code> (any case, spaces around it ignored) is true, blank text,\nnull and undefined are null, any other text is false. A boolean passes through</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { BooleanFormatter, Datasource, registerFormatter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nBooleanFormatter.format(true); // 'true'\nBooleanFormatter.parse('TRUE'); // true\nBooleanFormatter.parse(''); // null\n\n// show yes/no in the filter string and group headers\nconst yesNo = { ...BooleanFormatter, format: (value: unknown) =&gt; (value === true ? 'yes' : value === false ? 'no' : '') };\nregisterFormatter('yesNo', yesNo);\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { active: { type: 'boolean', formatter: 'yesNo' } }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"DateFormatterDDMMYYYY","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const DateFormatterDDMMYYYY: { placeholder: string; format: any; parse: any; parseFilter: any }"],"doc":"<p>Formatter for dates as <code>DD.MM.YYYY</code>, e.g. <code>20.11.2026</code>. Registered as <code>&#39;dateDDMMYYYY&#39;</code>, the options\nname it by that id (see <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> - a <code>Date</code> (or a date string/timestamp) as <code>20.11.2026</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for a blank or invalid date</li>\n<li><code>parse</code> - <code>&#39;20.11.2026&#39;</code> as a <code>Date</code>. A month or year left out is the current one (<code>&#39;20&#39;</code> is the\n20th of this month), and the time of day is the current time, so an edited date keeps a time.\nA <code>Date</code> passes through, null and undefined are returned as they are, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> gives null and text\nthat is no date gives <code>&#39;&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>parseFilter</code> - like <code>parse</code>, but at the start of the day (00:00:00.000). A <code>Date</code> is moved to the\nstart of its day</li>\n<li><code>placeholder</code> - <code>&#39;DD.MM.YYYY&#39;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, DateFormatterDDMMYYYY } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nDateFormatterDDMMYYYY.format(new Date(2026, 10, 20)); // '20.11.2026'\nDateFormatterDDMMYYYY.parseFilter('20.11.2026'); // Date 2026-11-20 00:00:00\n\n// one field, by its id\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { born: { type: 'date', formatter: 'dateDDMMYYYY' } }\n});\n\n// or every date field\nconst datasource2 = new Datasource({\n    fields: { born: 'date', hired: 'date' },\n    formatters: { date: 'dateDDMMYYYY' }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"DateFormatterDDMMYYYYTHHMMSS","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const DateFormatterDDMMYYYYTHHMMSS: { placeholder: string; format: any; parse: any; parseFilter: any }"],"doc":"<p>Formatter for a date with time as <code>DD.MM.YYYYTHH:MM:SS</code>, e.g. <code>20.11.2026T13:45:12</code>. Registered as\n<code>&#39;datetimeDDMMYYYY&#39;</code>, the options name it by that id (see <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> - a <code>Date</code> (or a date string/timestamp) as <code>20.11.2026T13:45:12</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for a blank or\ninvalid date</li>\n<li><code>parse</code> - <code>&#39;20.11.2026T13:45:12&#39;</code> as a <code>Date</code>. A month or year left out is the current one, and so\nare the hours, minutes and seconds left out. A <code>Date</code> passes through, null and undefined are\nreturned as they are, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> gives null and text that is no date gives <code>&#39;&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>parseFilter</code> - like <code>parse</code>, but the time parts left out are 0, and so are the milliseconds:\n<code>&#39;20.11.2026&#39;</code> is 2026-11-20 00:00:00.000. A <code>Date</code> passes through</li>\n<li><code>placeholder</code> - <code>&#39;DD.MM.YYYYTHH:MM:SS&#39;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, DateFormatterDDMMYYYYTHHMMSS } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nDateFormatterDDMMYYYYTHHMMSS.format(new Date(2026, 10, 20, 13, 45, 12)); // '20.11.2026T13:45:12'\n\n// a field names it by its id\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { lastLogin: { type: 'datetime', formatter: 'datetimeDDMMYYYY' } }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"DateFormatterYYYYMMDD","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const DateFormatterYYYYMMDD: { placeholder: string; format: any; parse: any; parseFilter: any }"],"doc":"<p>Formatter for dates as <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>, e.g. <code>2026-11-20</code>. The default for <code>date</code> fields. Registered as\n<code>&#39;dateYYYYMMDD&#39;</code>, the options name it by that id (see <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> - a <code>Date</code> (or a date string/timestamp) as <code>2026-11-20</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for a blank or invalid date</li>\n<li><code>parse</code> - <code>&#39;2026-11-20&#39;</code> as a <code>Date</code>. A month or day left out is the current one\n(<code>&#39;2026&#39;</code> is today&#39;s month and day in 2026), and the time of day is the current time, so an\nedited date keeps a time. A <code>Date</code> passes through, null and undefined are returned as they are,\n<code>&#39;&#39;</code> gives null and text that is no date gives <code>&#39;&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>parseFilter</code> - like <code>parse</code>, but at the start of the day (00:00:00.000). A <code>Date</code> is moved to the\nstart of its day</li>\n<li><code>placeholder</code> - <code>&#39;YYYY-MM-DD&#39;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, DateFormatterYYYYMMDD } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nDateFormatterYYYYMMDD.format(new Date(2026, 10, 20, 13, 45)); // '2026-11-20'\nDateFormatterYYYYMMDD.parse('2026-11-20'); // Date 2026-11-20, current time of day\nDateFormatterYYYYMMDD.parseFilter('2026-11-20'); // Date 2026-11-20 00:00:00\n\n// the default for date fields, set it by its id on one field or as the default to be explicit\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { born: { type: 'date', formatter: 'dateYYYYMMDD' } },\n    formatters: { date: 'dateYYYYMMDD' }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS: { placeholder: string; format: any; parse: any; parseFilter: any }"],"doc":"<p>Formatter for a date with time as <code>YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS</code>, e.g. <code>2026-11-20T13:45:12</code>. The default\nfor <code>datetime</code> fields. Registered as <code>&#39;datetimeYYYYMMDD&#39;</code>, the options name it by that id (see\n<a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> - a <code>Date</code> (or a date string/timestamp) as <code>2026-11-20T13:45:12</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for a blank or\ninvalid date</li>\n<li><code>parse</code> - <code>&#39;2026-11-20T13:45:12&#39;</code> as a <code>Date</code>. A month or day left out is the current one, and so\nare the hours, minutes and seconds left out (<code>&#39;2026-11-20T13&#39;</code> is 13 o&#39;clock and the current\nminutes and seconds). A <code>Date</code> passes through, null and undefined are returned as they are,\n<code>&#39;&#39;</code> gives null and text that is no date gives <code>&#39;&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>parseFilter</code> - like <code>parse</code>, but the time parts left out are 0, and so are the milliseconds:\n<code>&#39;2026-11-20&#39;</code> is 2026-11-20 00:00:00.000. A <code>Date</code> passes through</li>\n<li><code>placeholder</code> - <code>&#39;YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SS&#39;</code></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nDateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS.format(new Date(2026, 10, 20, 13, 45, 12)); // '2026-11-20T13:45:12'\nDateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS.parseFilter('2026-11-20T13'); // Date 2026-11-20 13:00:00\n\n// the default for datetime fields\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { lastLogin: 'datetime' }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"MENU_IDS","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const MENU_IDS: { filter: readonly [\"filter.filter\", \"filter.filter.clear\", \"filter.filter.clearAll\", \"filter.filter.blankSeparator\", \"filter.filter.isBlank\", \"filter.filter.isNotBlank\", \"filter.filter.advancedSeparator\", \"filter.filter.advanced\", \"filter.operator\", \"filter.operator.greaterThanOrEqualTo\", \"filter.operator.lessThanOrEqualTo\", \"filter.operator.equal\", \"filter.operator.notEqualTo\", \"filter.operator.contains\", \"filter.values\"]; header: readonly [\"header.column\", \"header.column.pinLeft\", \"header.column.pinLeftCopy\", \"header.column.pinRight\", \"header.column.pinRightCopy\", \"header.column.unpin\", \"header.column.hide\", \"header.column.removeSorting\", \"header.column.chooserSeparator\", \"header.column.chooser\", \"header.size\", \"header.size.column\", \"header.size.all\", \"header.grouping\", \"header.grouping.expandAll\", \"header.grouping.collapseAll\", \"header.grouping.clear\"]; row: readonly [\"row.edit\", \"row.edit.undo\", \"row.edit.redo\", \"row.edit.revertCell\", \"row.edit.revertRow\", \"row.edit.revertRows\", \"row.copy\", \"row.copy.cell\", \"row.copy.column\", \"row.copy.row\", \"row.copy.selectedColumns\", \"row.copy.range\", \"row.filter\", \"row.filter.replace\", \"row.filter.add\", \"row.view\", \"row.view.dimRepeatedValues\", \"row.view.changedOnly\", \"row.paste\", \"row.paste.cell\", \"row.paste.range\", \"row.clear\", \"row.clear.cell\", \"row.clear.range\", \"row.delete\", \"row.delete.rows\", \"row.delete.undo\", \"row.summary\", \"row.summary.count\", \"row.summary.sum\", \"row.summary.max\", \"row.summary.min\", \"row.summary.avg\", \"row.export\", \"row.export.csv\", \"row.export.csvSelected\"] }"],"doc":"<p>The ids of the grid&#39;s own menu entries, per menu, in the order the menus show them - the <code>defaults</code>\na <a href=\"#api/GridMenus\">GridMenus</a> function gets. Every entry is always in <code>defaults</code>: the ones that do not apply\n(paste on a readonly cell, the summary of a text column ...) have a <code>visible</code> callback that hides\nthem. Ids are <code>menu.section</code> for a section header and <code>menu.section.entry</code> for what is under it.</p>\n<p>The ids stay the same between versions, so a menu changed by id keeps working. They are text ids\ntoo: the label of an entry is the text of its id, its hint the text <code>&lt;id&gt;.hint</code> - see <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>\nand <a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a>. The &quot;shown as&quot; below is the English text; the separators and <code>filter.values</code>\nhave no text of their own.</p>\n<p>Row menu (<code>GridMenus.row</code>), right click on a cell:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>id</th>\n<th>shown as</th>\n<th>shown when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>row.edit</code></td>\n<td>Edit: - first in the menu</td>\n<td>the grid is editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.edit.undo</code></td>\n<td>Undo last change (Ctrl+Z) - <code>datasource.undo()</code>, the last edit, paste, clear, delete or revert. Greyed out when there is nothing to undo</td>\n<td>the grid is editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.edit.redo</code></td>\n<td>Redo (Ctrl+Y) - <code>datasource.redo()</code>. Greyed out when there is nothing to redo</td>\n<td>the grid is editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.edit.revertCell</code></td>\n<td>Undo cell edit - the cell&#39;s original value (<code>datasource.resetField()</code>). Greyed out when the cell is not edited</td>\n<td>the grid is editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.edit.revertRow</code></td>\n<td>Undo row edits - the row right clicked back to its original values, unmarked for deletion (<code>datasource.resetRows(row)</code>), no selection needed. Greyed out when the row is not edited or marked</td>\n<td>the grid is editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.edit.revertRows</code></td>\n<td>Undo row edits (selected rows) - the selected rows back, unmarked for deletion (<code>datasource.resetRows()</code>). Greyed out when no selected row is edited or marked</td>\n<td>the grid is editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.copy</code></td>\n<td>Copy:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.copy.cell</code></td>\n<td>Cell Value</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.copy.column</code></td>\n<td>Column (selected rows)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.copy.row</code></td>\n<td>Row (selected rows)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.copy.selectedColumns</code></td>\n<td>Row (selected rows/col) - the selected columns, all when none is selected</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.copy.range</code></td>\n<td>Range - the last range of cells, as Ctrl+C copies it: tab separated text and an html table</td>\n<td>there are ranges of cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.filter</code></td>\n<td>Filter:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.filter.replace</code></td>\n<td>Replace filter (all)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.filter.add</code></td>\n<td>Add to filter (and)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.view</code></td>\n<td>View:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.view.dimRepeatedValues</code></td>\n<td>Use dimmed values, with a ✓ when on</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.view.changedOnly</code></td>\n<td>Changed rows only, with a ✓ when on - the new, edited and deleted rows of the filter (<code>datasource.filterChangedOnly()</code>)</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.paste</code></td>\n<td>Paste:</td>\n<td>the grid and the cell are editable, or the grid is and there are ranges of cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.paste.cell</code></td>\n<td>Paste cell (selected rows)</td>\n<td>the grid and the cell are editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.paste.range</code></td>\n<td>Paste range - the clipboard as Ctrl+V pastes it with ranges: one value into every cell of them, a block from the top left of the last one</td>\n<td>the grid is editable, there are ranges of cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.clear</code></td>\n<td>Clear:</td>\n<td>the grid and the cell are editable, or the grid is and there are ranges of cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.clear.cell</code></td>\n<td>Clear cell (selected rows) - sets the field to <code>null</code>, also a number field (emptying the cell stores 0)</td>\n<td>the grid and the cell are editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.clear.range</code></td>\n<td>Clear range - every cell of the ranges, as Delete: <code>null</code>, the readonly cells skipped</td>\n<td>the grid is editable, there are ranges of cells</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.delete</code></td>\n<td>Delete:</td>\n<td>the grid is editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.delete.rows</code></td>\n<td>Rows (selected rows) - marks them for deletion (<code>markForDeletion()</code>), they stay in the grid until the changes are accepted. Skips a row the <code>isReadonly</code> hook returns <code>true</code> for in every column of the layout. Greyed out when no selected row is left to mark</td>\n<td>the grid is editable</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.delete.undo</code></td>\n<td>Undo (selected rows) - takes the mark off the selected rows marked for deletion (<code>unmarkForDeletion()</code>)</td>\n<td>the grid is editable, and a selected row is marked for deletion</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.summary</code></td>\n<td>Summary:</td>\n<td>a number field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.summary.count</code></td>\n<td>Count: 3 - of the selected rows, click to copy</td>\n<td>a number field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.summary.sum</code></td>\n<td>Sum: 60</td>\n<td>a number field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.summary.max</code></td>\n<td>Max: 30</td>\n<td>a number field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.summary.min</code></td>\n<td>Min: 10</td>\n<td>a number field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.summary.avg</code></td>\n<td>Avg: 20</td>\n<td>a number field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.export</code></td>\n<td>Export:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.export.csv</code></td>\n<td>CSV, all rows - <code>gridInterface.downloadCsv()</code>: the rows the filter lets through, as the grid shows them</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>row.export.csvSelected</code></td>\n<td>CSV, selected rows - <code>downloadCsv(&#39;export.csv&#39;, { rows: &#39;selected&#39; })</code>. Greyed out when no row is selected</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Header menu (<code>GridMenus.header</code>), right click on a header label:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>id</th>\n<th>shown as</th>\n<th>shown when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>header.column</code></td>\n<td>Column:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.pinLeft</code></td>\n<td>Pin left</td>\n<td>not pinned left</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.pinLeftCopy</code></td>\n<td>Pin left (copy)</td>\n<td>not pinned left</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.pinRight</code></td>\n<td>Pin right</td>\n<td>not pinned right</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.pinRightCopy</code></td>\n<td>Pin right (copy)</td>\n<td>not pinned right</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.unpin</code></td>\n<td>Unpin</td>\n<td>pinned</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.hide</code></td>\n<td>Hide</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.removeSorting</code></td>\n<td>Remove sorting - keeps the sort of the grouped fields</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.chooserSeparator</code></td>\n<td>a line</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.column.chooser</code></td>\n<td>Column chooser</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.size</code></td>\n<td>Size:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.size.column</code></td>\n<td>Resize Column</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.size.all</code></td>\n<td>Resize all columns</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.grouping</code></td>\n<td>Grouping:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.grouping.expandAll</code></td>\n<td>Expand all</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.grouping.collapseAll</code></td>\n<td>Collapse all</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>header.grouping.clear</code></td>\n<td>Clear all</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Filter menu (<code>GridMenus.filter</code>), right click on a header filter:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>id</th>\n<th>shown as</th>\n<th>shown when</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>filter.filter</code></td>\n<td>Filter:</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.filter.clear</code></td>\n<td>Clear Filter - the column&#39;s conditions</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.filter.clearAll</code></td>\n<td>Clear All Filters</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.filter.blankSeparator</code></td>\n<td>a line</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.filter.isBlank</code></td>\n<td>Set &quot;Is Blank&quot;</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.filter.isNotBlank</code></td>\n<td>Set &quot;Is Not Blank&quot;</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.filter.advancedSeparator</code></td>\n<td>a line</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.filter.advanced</code></td>\n<td>Advanced Filter - the filter editor</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.operator</code></td>\n<td>Set Operator:</td>\n<td>not a boolean field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.operator.greaterThanOrEqualTo</code></td>\n<td>Greater than or equal</td>\n<td>a number, date or datetime field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.operator.lessThanOrEqualTo</code></td>\n<td>Less than or equal</td>\n<td>a number, date or datetime field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.operator.equal</code></td>\n<td>Equal</td>\n<td>not a boolean field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.operator.notEqualTo</code></td>\n<td>Not Equal</td>\n<td>a text field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.operator.contains</code></td>\n<td>Contains</td>\n<td>a text field</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filter.values</code></td>\n<td>the value list: &quot;Search:&quot;, search box, a checkbox per value, &quot;Run Search&quot; - a <a href=\"#api/MenuBlock\">MenuBlock</a>, its texts are <code>filter.values.*</code></td>\n<td>a text field</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { type GridHooks, MENU_IDS } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// a row menu without the copy entries\nconst hooks: GridHooks = {\n    menus: { row: (defaults) =&gt; defaults.filter((entry) =&gt; !entry.id.startsWith('row.copy')) }\n};\n\nMENU_IDS.row.includes('row.paste.cell'); // true</code></pre>\n","samples":["context-menu"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"NumberFormatterComma","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const NumberFormatterComma: { format: any; parse: any }"],"doc":"<p>Formatter for numbers with a comma as the decimal separator: <code>12,5</code>. Registered as <code>&#39;numberComma&#39;</code>,\nthe options name it by that id (see <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> - a number as text with a comma, <code>12.5</code> -&gt; <code>&#39;12,5&#39;</code>. Anything that does not read as a\nnumber (null, undefined, <code>&#39;abc&#39;</code>) gives <code>&#39;&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>parse</code> / <code>parseFilter</code> - <code>&#39;12,5&#39;</code> and <code>&#39;12.5&#39;</code> both give 12.5. A number passes through,\nnull and undefined give null, text that is no number (<code>&#39;&#39;</code> too) gives 0. So emptying a number\ncell in the grid stores 0; the row menu&#39;s Clear stores null. A formatter whose <code>parse</code> gives null\nfor <code>&#39;&#39;</code> stores null</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, NumberFormatterComma } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nNumberFormatterComma.format(1234.5); // '1234,5'\nNumberFormatterComma.parse('12,5'); // 12.5\n\n// one field, by its id\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'numberComma' } }\n});\n\n// or every number field\nconst datasource2 = new Datasource({\n    fields: { price: 'number', amount: 'number' },\n    formatters: { number: 'numberComma' }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"NumberFormatterDot","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const NumberFormatterDot: { format: any; parse: any }"],"doc":"<p>Formatter for numbers with a dot as the decimal separator: <code>12.5</code>. The default for <code>number</code> fields.\nRegistered as <code>&#39;numberDot&#39;</code>, the options name it by that id (see <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> - a number as text, <code>12.5</code> -&gt; <code>&#39;12.5&#39;</code>. Anything that does not read as a number\n(null, undefined, <code>&#39;abc&#39;</code>) gives <code>&#39;&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>parse</code> / <code>parseFilter</code> - <code>&#39;12.5&#39;</code> and <code>&#39;12,5&#39;</code> both give 12.5. A number passes through,\nnull and undefined give null, text that is no number (<code>&#39;&#39;</code> too) gives 0. So emptying a number\ncell in the grid stores 0; the row menu&#39;s Clear stores null. A formatter whose <code>parse</code> gives null\nfor <code>&#39;&#39;</code> stores null</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, NumberFormatterDot, registerFormatter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nNumberFormatterDot.format(1234.5); // '1234.5'\nNumberFormatterDot.parse('12,5'); // 12.5\n\n// the default, set it by its id to be explicit\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'numberDot' } }\n});\n\n// a variant: spread it, replace what you need and register it under an id of your own\nconst twoDecimals = { ...NumberFormatterDot, format: (value: unknown) =&gt; (typeof value === 'number' ? value.toFixed(2) : '') };\nregisterFormatter('twoDecimals', twoDecimals);</code></pre>\n","samples":["formatters"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"TextFormatter","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const TextFormatter: { format: any; parse: any }"],"doc":"<p>Formatter for text, the default for <code>text</code> fields (and so for every field not listed in <code>fields</code>).\nRegistered as <code>&#39;text&#39;</code>, the options name it by that id (see <a href=\"#api/registerFormatter\">registerFormatter</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>format</code> - the value as text, <code>&#39;&#39;</code> for null and undefined. Anything else goes through\n<code>String()</code>: 0 is <code>&#39;0&#39;</code>, false is <code>&#39;false&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>parse</code> / <code>parseFilter</code> - the text as it is</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, registerFormatter, TextFormatter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nTextFormatter.format(null); // ''\nTextFormatter.format(42); // '42'\n\n// a variant: show the text in upper case, edit and filter it as it is\nconst upperCase = { ...TextFormatter, format: (value: unknown) =&gt; TextFormatter.format(value).toUpperCase() };\nregisterFormatter('upperCase', upperCase);\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { country: { formatter: 'upperCase' } }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-formatter"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"TEXTS","group":"Variables","kind":"Variable","signatures":["const TEXTS: Readonly<Record<TextId, string>>"],"doc":"<p>Every text the grid and the datasource show, by id: the English defaults. Change them with\n<a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a> (for the page) and <code>GridConfig.texts</code> (for one grid); this object stays as it is.</p>\n<p>The ids are grouped by area, the area first:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>ids</th>\n<th>where</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>row.*</code>, <code>header.*</code>, <code>filter.*</code></td>\n<td>the right click menus: the ids of <a href=\"#api/MENU_IDS\">MENU_IDS</a>. A hint (the text in parentheses) is <code>&lt;id&gt;.hint</code>. <code>filter.values.*</code>: the value list of the filter menu</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>columnChooser.*</code></td>\n<td>the column chooser</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filterEditor.*</code></td>\n<td>the filter editor, its field and operator menus. <code>filterEditor.operator.&lt;FilterOperator&gt;</code>: the names of the operators</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>footer.*</code></td>\n<td>the footer: the row count, the filter chips. <code>footer.operator.&lt;FilterOperator&gt;</code>: the short names of the operators (<code>=</code>, <code>contains</code>)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>aggregate.*</code></td>\n<td>the aggregates of the columns: the label in front of a value in the group rows and the totals row (<code>aggregate.&lt;AggregateFunction&gt;</code>), and the label of the totals row</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>grid.*</code></td>\n<td>labels for screen readers</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>rowStatus.*</code></td>\n<td>the state of a row on its row number: the tooltip, and the text for a screen reader</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>cell.*</code></td>\n<td>the cells: the marker of an edited cell, a cell of several lines and its editor</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>datePicker.*</code></td>\n<td>the date picker: the buttons, the names of the months and the days</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>validation.*</code></td>\n<td>the messages of the built-in validators. Made by the datasource</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>filterString.*</code></td>\n<td><code>datasource.getFilterString()</code>: AND, OR and the operators. Made by the datasource</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>grouping.blank</code></td>\n<td>the value in the name of the group of blank values. Made by the datasource</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>The tooltip of an element is <code>&lt;id&gt;.tooltip</code>: <code>filterEditor.addCondition.tooltip</code>. <code>{name}</code> in a text\nis filled in when it is shown (<code>&#39;Count: {count}&#39;</code>).</p>\n<p>The texts guide has every id with its text and where it is shown.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { setTexts, TEXTS } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nTEXTS['row.summary.count']; // 'Count: {count}'\n\n// every id with its English text, e.g. to hand to a translator\nconst english: string = JSON.stringify(TEXTS, null, 2);\nconsole.log(english);\n\nsetTexts({ 'row.summary.count': 'Antall: {count}' });</code></pre>\n","samples":["translation"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"and","group":"Functions","kind":"Function","signatures":["function and(...children: FilterExpression[]): FilterGroup"],"doc":"<p>A group where every child must match.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>children</code> conditions and groups. None gives an empty group, which filters out nothing</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { and, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// country = 'Norway' AND age &lt; 30\ndatasource.filter(and(where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'), where('age', 'LESS_THAN', 30)));</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"createGrid","group":"Functions","kind":"Function","signatures":["function createGrid<T>(host: HTMLElement, options: CreateGridOptions<T>): GridInterface<T>"],"doc":"<p>Puts a grid in a container on the page, in one call: makes the <a href=\"#api/GridInterface\">GridInterface</a> for the config\nand the datasource, and a <code>&lt;simple-html-grid&gt;</code> element that fills the container (width and height\n100%), connects them and adds the element to the container.</p>\n<p>The container needs a size: the grid fills it, it does not grow with its rows.</p>\n<p><code>gridInterface.destroy()</code> takes the grid off the page again. To place and size the element yourself,\nsee <a href=\"#api/GridElement\">GridElement</a>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>host</code> the container, the element is added as its last child</li>\n<li><code>options</code> the config, the datasource and the hooks</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Returns</strong> the grid interface, to work with the grid</p>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when the config has <code>isReadonly</code>, <code>cellClass</code> or <code>menus</code> (those are hooks), or\na column has v5&#39;s <code>mandatory</code> (it is the field&#39;s <code>required</code> rule)</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, Datasource, type GridConfig } from '@simple-html/grid';\nimport '@simple-html/grid/grid.css';\n\nconst datasource = new Datasource({ fields: { age: 'number' } });\ndatasource.setData([{ name: 'Ann', age: 30 }, { name: 'Bob', age: 42 }]);\n\nconst config: GridConfig = {\n    layout: { center: [{ fields: ['name'], width: 150 }, { fields: ['age'], width: 80 }] }\n};\n\n// &lt;div id=&quot;grid&quot; style=&quot;height: 400px&quot;&gt;&lt;/div&gt;\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(document.getElementById('grid')!, { config, datasource });\n\n// later, when the grid is not needed any more\ngridInterface.destroy();</code></pre>\n","samples":["basic-grid"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"isGroupRow","group":"Functions","kind":"Function","signatures":["function isGroupRow(row: Entity | GroupRow | null | undefined): row is GroupRow"],"doc":"<p><code>true</code> when the row is a group header row, <code>false</code> for a data row - and for <code>null</code> or\n<code>undefined</code>, so it can be given <code>datasource.getRow(n)</code> or <code>datasource.currentEntity</code> as they\nare. It narrows the type, a data row&#39;s own fields can be read after it.</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { isGroupRow } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nconst row = datasource.getRow(0);\nif (isGroupRow(row)) {\n    datasource.expandGroup(row.__groupID);\n} else {\n    console.log(row.name);\n}\n\n// only the data rows - getDataRows() is the same, plus the rows of collapsed groups\nconst dataRows = datasource.getRows().filter((row) =&gt; !isGroupRow(row));</code></pre>\n","samples":["sorting-grouping"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"or","group":"Functions","kind":"Function","signatures":["function or(...children: FilterExpression[]): FilterGroup"],"doc":"<p>A group where one matching child is enough.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>children</code> conditions and groups. None gives an empty group, which filters out nothing</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { or, where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// country = 'Norway' OR country = 'Sweden'\ndatasource.filter(or(where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Norway'), where('country', 'EQUAL', 'Sweden')));</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"registerFormatter","group":"Functions","kind":"Function","signatures":["function registerFormatter(id: string, formatter: Formatter): void"],"doc":"<p>Registers a formatter under an id, for the datasource options to name it: a field&#39;s <code>formatter</code>\nand the default per type in <code>formatters</code> are ids, so the options are plain JSON and can be stored,\ne.g. in a backend. The formatter itself is code: register it when the page loads, before the\ndatasource that names it is made.</p>\n<p>The built-in formatters are registered from the start:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>id</th>\n<th>formatter</th>\n<th>shows</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;text&#39;</code></td>\n<td><a href=\"#api/TextFormatter\">TextFormatter</a></td>\n<td>the text, the default for <code>text</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;boolean&#39;</code></td>\n<td><a href=\"#api/BooleanFormatter\">BooleanFormatter</a></td>\n<td><code>true</code> / <code>false</code>, the default for <code>boolean</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;numberDot&#39;</code></td>\n<td><a href=\"#api/NumberFormatterDot\">NumberFormatterDot</a></td>\n<td><code>1234.5</code>, the default for <code>number</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;numberComma&#39;</code></td>\n<td><a href=\"#api/NumberFormatterComma\">NumberFormatterComma</a></td>\n<td><code>1234,5</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;dateYYYYMMDD&#39;</code></td>\n<td><a href=\"#api/DateFormatterYYYYMMDD\">DateFormatterYYYYMMDD</a></td>\n<td><code>2026-11-20</code>, the default for <code>date</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;dateDDMMYYYY&#39;</code></td>\n<td><a href=\"#api/DateFormatterDDMMYYYY\">DateFormatterDDMMYYYY</a></td>\n<td><code>20.11.2026</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;datetimeYYYYMMDD&#39;</code></td>\n<td><a href=\"#api/DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS\">DateFormatterYYYYMMDDTHHMMSS</a></td>\n<td><code>2026-11-20T13:45:12</code>, the default for <code>datetime</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;datetimeDDMMYYYY&#39;</code></td>\n<td><a href=\"#api/DateFormatterDDMMYYYYTHHMMSS\">DateFormatterDDMMYYYYTHHMMSS</a></td>\n<td><code>20.11.2026T13:45:12</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Registering an id again replaces the formatter</strong> - a built-in one too, and replacing a built-in\ndefault (<code>&#39;numberDot&#39;</code> ...) changes every field of that type without a formatter of its own. Pick\nan id of your own unless that is what you want.</li>\n<li><strong>A datasource looks its ids up when it is made</strong> and keeps the formatters it found: replacing a\nformatter later changes the datasources made after, not the ones made before.</li>\n<li>There is one registry for the page, shared by every datasource.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the name the options use, e.g. <code>&#39;money&#39;</code>. Any text but <code>&#39;&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>formatter</code> the formatter, see <a href=\"#api/Formatter\">Formatter</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when the id is not a text, or the formatter has no <code>format</code> or <code>parse</code></p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, type Formatter, NumberFormatterDot, registerFormatter } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// two decimals and a space between the thousands: 12345.6 -&gt; '12 345.60'\nconst money: Formatter = {\n    ...NumberFormatterDot,\n    format: (value) =&gt; (typeof value === 'number' ? value.toFixed(2).replace(/\\B(?=(\\d{3})+(?!\\d))/g, ' ') : ''),\n    parse: (text) =&gt; NumberFormatterDot.parse(text.replaceAll(' ', ''))\n};\nregisterFormatter('money', money);\n\n// the options name it: plain JSON, they can come from a backend\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: { price: { type: 'number', formatter: 'money' } },\n    formatters: { date: 'dateDDMMYYYY' } // a built-in, the default for every date field\n});\ndatasource.getFormatter('price').format(12345.6); // '12 345.60'</code></pre>\n","samples":["custom-formatter"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"registerValidator","group":"Functions","kind":"Function","signatures":["function registerValidator(id: string, validator: Validator): void"],"doc":"<p>Registers a validator under an id, for the fields&#39; rules to name it: a field&#39;s <code>validate</code> lists\nrules by id (<code>validate: [&#39;required&#39;, { id: &#39;min&#39;, value: 0 }]</code>), so the fields are plain JSON and\ncan be stored, e.g. in a backend. The validator itself is code: register it when the page loads,\nbefore the datasource that names it is made.</p>\n<p>The built-in validators are registered from the start. They take their option as <code>value</code>:</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>id</th>\n<th>the value fails when</th>\n<th>message id</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><code>&#39;required&#39;</code></td>\n<td>it is <code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>, an invalid Date or 0</td>\n<td><code>&#39;validation.required&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;min&#39;</code></td>\n<td>it is a number below <code>value</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;validation.min&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;max&#39;</code></td>\n<td>it is a number above <code>value</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;validation.max&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;minLength&#39;</code></td>\n<td>it is text shorter than <code>value</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;validation.minLength&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;maxLength&#39;</code></td>\n<td>it is text longer than <code>value</code></td>\n<td><code>&#39;validation.maxLength&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>&#39;pattern&#39;</code></td>\n<td>it is text the regular expression <code>value</code> (as text) does not find</td>\n<td><code>&#39;validation.pattern&#39;</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>0 fails <code>required</code></strong>, like the filter&#39;s <code>IS_BLANK</code> takes 0 as blank: an emptied number cell\nstores 0 (the number formatters parse <code>&#39;&#39;</code> as 0), so a required number must not take it. <code>false</code>\npasses, it is a value. For a number where 0 is a real value, register a rule of your own (below).</li>\n<li><strong>The other built-ins pass a blank value</strong> (<code>null</code>, <code>undefined</code>, <code>&#39;&#39;</code>): an optional field can be\nempty, add <code>&#39;required&#39;</code> to make it fail. They check only values of their kind - <code>min</code> / <code>max</code>\nnumbers, the others text - and pass the rest.</li>\n<li><strong><code>pattern</code> is not anchored</strong>: <code>&#39;[0-9]&#39;</code> finds a digit anywhere, write <code>&#39;^[0-9]+$&#39;</code> for the whole\ntext. It is a <code>RegExp</code> without flags.</li>\n<li><strong>The messages are texts</strong>: the built-ins return the ids <code>validation.*</code> of <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a>, changed\nwith <a href=\"#api/setTexts\">setTexts</a>. A rule&#39;s <code>message</code> replaces what the validator returns. Either is the\nmessage itself or a text id: an id of your own gets its text from <code>setTexts()</code>, so it is translated\nlike the built-ins&#39; (<code>&#39;validation.phoneNO&#39;</code> below).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Registering an id again replaces the validator - a built-in one too, for the fields that name\nit (its options are not checked then, and the grid&#39;s stripes for <code>required</code> still mark what the\nbuilt-in takes as missing). <strong>A datasource looks its ids up when it is made</strong> and keeps the validators it found, like the\nformatters. There is one registry for the page, shared by every datasource.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>id</code> the name the rules use, e.g. <code>&#39;phone&#39;</code>. Any text but <code>&#39;&#39;</code></li>\n<li><code>validator</code> the function that checks a value, see <a href=\"#api/Validator\">Validator</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when the id is not a text, or the validator is not a function</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { Datasource, registerValidator, setTexts } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\n// a Norwegian phone number: 8 digits, spaces allowed. Returns a text id, its text is set below\nregisterValidator('phoneNO', (value) =&gt;\n    typeof value === 'string' &amp;&amp; value !== '' &amp;&amp; !/^(\\d\\s*){8}$/.test(value) ? 'validation.phoneNO' : null\n);\nsetTexts({ 'validation.phoneNO': 'Must be 8 digits' });\n// a number that must be there, 0 included (the built-in required takes 0 as missing)\nregisterValidator('present', (value) =&gt; (value === null || value === undefined ? 'validation.required' : null));\n\n// the fields name them: plain JSON, they can come from a backend\nconst datasource = new Datasource({\n    fields: {\n        name: { validate: ['required', { id: 'maxLength', value: 50 }] },\n        age: { type: 'number', validate: ['required', { id: 'min', value: 0 }, { id: 'max', value: 150, message: 'too old' }] },\n        phone: { validate: ['phoneNO'] },\n        discount: { type: 'number', validate: ['present'] }\n    }\n});</code></pre>\n","samples":["validation"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"setTexts","group":"Functions","kind":"Function","signatures":["function setTexts(texts: Texts): void"],"doc":"<p>Sets the texts of the page: every grid and datasource uses them. An app with one language calls\nit once, before it makes its grids. A text for one grid only is <code>GridConfig.texts</code>, which wins over\nthese.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>It replaces the texts set before</strong>: an id left out shows its default again, <code>setTexts({})</code> goes\nback to the defaults (English). The object is copied.</li>\n<li><strong>Nothing is rendered again</strong>: a grid shows the new texts after its next rebuild\n(<code>gridInterface.rebuild()</code>), a menu, the filter editor and the date picker the next time they\nopen. <code>getFilterString()</code> uses them from its next call. A validation message is made when a value\nis validated: an error already shown keeps its text until the field is validated again. The name\nof the group of blank values changes the next time the rows are grouped.</li>\n<li>The texts of the datasource - <code>validation.*</code>, <code>filterString.*</code>, <code>grouping.blank</code> - are set here\nonly: the datasource has no grid, <code>GridConfig.texts</code> does not change them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>texts</code> a text for each id to change, see <a href=\"#api/TEXTS\">TEXTS</a> for the ids. Plain JSON, it can come\nfrom a backend</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Throws</strong> a <code>TypeError</code> when <code>texts</code> is not an object, or a text is not a string</p>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { createGrid, type GridConfig, setTexts } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\ndeclare const config: GridConfig;\n\n// once, before the grids are made\nsetTexts({\n    'row.copy': 'Kopier:',\n    'row.summary.count': 'Antall: {count}',\n    'validation.required': 'Må fylles ut'\n});\nconst gridInterface = createGrid(host, { config, datasource });\n\n// later: back to English\nsetTexts({});\ngridInterface.rebuild();</code></pre>\n","samples":["translation"],"memberGroups":[]},{"name":"where","group":"Functions","kind":"Function","signatures":["function where(field: string, operator: FilterOperator, value?: unknown): FilterCondition"],"doc":"<p>A condition: <code>field</code> <code>operator</code> <code>value</code>.</p>\n<p><strong>Parameters</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>field</code> the field to test, the property on the row</li>\n<li><code>operator</code> how to compare, see <a href=\"#api/FilterOperator\">FilterOperator</a></li>\n<li><code>value</code> what to compare with. Leave it out for <code>IS_BLANK</code> / <code>IS_NOT_BLANK</code>, the condition\nthen has no <code>value</code> property</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Example</strong></p>\n<pre class=\"code-block\" data-lang=\"ts\"><code>import { where } from '@simple-html/grid';\n\nwhere('age', 'GREATER_THAN', 18); // { field: 'age', operator: 'GREATER_THAN', value: 18 }\nwhere('born', 'LESS_THAN', new Date(2000, 0, 1));\nwhere('country', 'NOT_IN', ['Norway', 'Sweden']);\nwhere('email', 'IS_BLANK'); // { field: 'email', operator: 'IS_BLANK' }</code></pre>\n","samples":["filtering"],"memberGroups":[]}]}